(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport said that the Royal Government of Cambodia will set standards for vehicles imported back to Cambodia to facilitate and guarantee to consumers.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Pov Maly, after the 2018 Asia Technical Meeting at the Ministry of Public Works on the evening of October 16, 2018, said that mechanical problems are very important for vehicles to use. He added that currently in Cambodia, there is no standard setting yet, because Cambodia is a country that imports vehicles, and Cambodia will work on setting vehicle standards in the future.
"We are also preparing to standardize vehicles," he said. We are working with the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts and the Standards Institute to discuss future vehicle specifications. What kind of vehicle to import to our country appropriately. "Even though we are a car importer, we need to set the standard for cars imported into our country."
However, the Secretary of State said that the standardization of vehicles for import into the country will follow all ASEAN countries, which may be done by 2023. All ASEAN members will set import standards for vehicles in accordance with international regulations.
He claimed that at present, Cambodia has difficulty controlling the import of standard cars because Cambodia has imported used cars, but there are also some companies importing new cars. Cambodia imports used cars from many countries, regardless of which country has the standard.
Mr. Pov Maly also mentioned that today's meeting to study for 2023 to determine what kind of car to use on Cambodian territory. At that time, Cambodia has already set the standard, and any type of car that meets the standard will be imported into Cambodia, regardless of the country.
Ms. Naomi Miri, Deputy Director of the Technical Department (JASIC) of Japan, said that the standard setting depends on the Cambodian side to implement, while the Japanese side only provides technical advice to implement.
