Russian, Pakistani troops hold joint 2018 military exercise on a mountain in Pakistan
(Moscow): From October 21 to November 4, the Russian and Pakistani military will jointly hold the 2018 friendly exercise in the mountains of Pakistan. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday evening, October 16, 2018.
According to the head of the Russian military information department in the southern region, the joint military exercise will take place at a training ground in the mountainous city of Pabbi, northwestern Pakistan, and the two countries' armies will carry out various military exercises during At an altitude of 1,400 meters above sea level.
Russia and Pakistan have been holding friendly military exercises since 2016. In 2017, a total of more than 200 Russian and Pakistani troops held joint exercises in the North Caucasus region of southern Russia at high altitudes. 2,300 meters above sea level. Cambodia, Canada agree to renew trade facilitation agreement to strengthen bilateral cooperation
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Canada have agreed to renew the Trade Facilitation Agreement to strengthen and expand bilateral economic and trade cooperation on a win-win basis. This agreement was made between the Ministry of Commerce of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Office of Trade Facilitation (TFO) of the Republic of Canada, which expired on September 30, 2018.
The agreement was renewed during a bilateral meeting between Mr. Pan Sosak and Ms. Donica Pottie, Ambassador of Canada to the Kingdom of Cambodia on Tuesday morning, October 16, 2018 in Ta Prohm Room. Of the Ministry of Commerce.
During the meeting, the Minister briefed the Canadian side on Cambodia's strong economic growth from the participation of the construction sector, textiles, tourism and agriculture. Of that, the value of the garment industry in 2017 was about 7 billion US dollars, and the industry created 760,000 jobs, mostly women in rural areas.
Minister Pan Sosak highlighted the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to support the textile sector by continuing to explore additional potential markets and increase the maximum wage for workers from $ 140 in 2016 to $ 170 per year. 2018 and plans to increase to $ 182 at the beginning of 2019.
In response, Ambassador Donika Poti praised the reform of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in promoting the textile sector and seeking benefits for workers in the past. Come on.
The Ambassador encouraged the Cambodian government to continue its efforts and adhere to this work ethic to bring win-win to all stakeholders for this industry, and she will examine the possibility of helping Canadian investors come to invest. On the processing of key raw materials to serve the development of the textile industry and the modernization of the agricultural sector in Cambodia.
Please be informed that in 2017, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Canada reached a total of 1.04 billion US dollars with an average annual growth rate of 11%. Of that, exports from Cambodia to Canada amounted to 1 billion US dollars and imports amounted to 40 million US dollars. Cambodia's potential export products include: clothing, footwear, auto parts, furniture, plastics, toys and agricultural products.
