Minister of Commerce: Cambodia is ready to strengthen cooperation with Indonesia from culture to technology
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, informed the Indonesian diplomat that Cambodia is ready to strengthen and expand cooperation with Indonesia in various priority areas from trade, culture to technology to cut Reduce the annual trade deficit of the two countries.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak mentioned the traditional friendship between Cambodia and Indonesia and the harmony of history and culture of the two countries, such as language, literature and ancient sculpture. The Minister also pointed out to the Indonesian side the potential of Cambodia's agriculture, tourism and industry, which is being taken care of by the Royal Government of Cambodia in diversifying (expanding) exports to regional and global markets.
The Minister briefed on the progress of trade between the two countries and proposed direct flights from Indonesia to Cambodia to promote tourism and culture, as well as strengthen cooperation between the two countries' private sectors, especially the exchange of experiences. In the field of telecommunications technology and innovation (innovation), which is the key to promoting entrepreneurship to diversify employment opportunities and promote national economic growth.
In response, Mr. Sudamen Hasseng agreed with the Minister and stated that Indonesia intends to expand economic, trade and other priority areas with Cambodia, and next week the Indonesian Ministry of Commerce will facilitate his visit. Cambodian business delegation seeking business opportunities in Bandung, West Java.
The Ambassador added that the Indonesian government is considering buying rice and other agricultural products from Cambodia and has encouraged Indonesian traders to participate in the One Village, One Product Fair, which is scheduled to be held in Phnom Penh, Cambodia from 8 to 8 days. December 11 to promote cooperation and reduce the bilateral trade deficit to a maximum.
(Preah Vihear): A woman named Ros Sotheavy, 44 years old, living in Sra Em Khang Cheung village, Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, was sued for more than $ 60,000 in cash and scams related to buying stones to sell to a road construction company. .
