(Phnom Penh): The operation to crack down on overweight trucks is like a sharp war between law enforcement officials and corrupt traders who like to do business overweight.
Mr. Seng Chhuon, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, was given a special mission by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, as the Chairman of the Working Group to clear overweight traffic on this road.
Since taking office, Mr. Seng Chhuon has been given the nickname "Iron Officer" to dismiss overweight cases without understanding, even though the overweight business owner is rich, powerful and influential. Anyway.
The biggest challenge in enforcing the law to eliminate overcrowding is when it comes to seizing the vehicles of big and influential merchants, such as military officers, tycoons with high-ranking officials.
Mr. Seng Chhuon further described that due to the implementation of legal measures to get rid of overweight in accordance with the law, as well as the strict regulations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, there are high-ranking officials, powerful and powerful. Many who had been in contact before had stopped talking to him and even his face was stopped.
The officer in charge of clearing the overweight truck said that cracking down on the overweight truck was a hot and difficult task for him.
However, he will continue to work hard, transparently, fairly and without discrimination between the powerful and ordinary people to contribute to reducing road damage from overcrowding.
Mr. Seng Chhuon expressed the hope that senior business officials would understand his rule of law, not to use it as a weapon of detachment, friendship and communication.
He also expects that the implementation of strict legal measures will awaken all businesses to respect the law to contribute to making roads in Cambodia durable and not damaged due to overloading.
