Samdech Pichey Sena's remarks were made this morning, October 16, 2018, on the occasion that Samdech Pichey Sena led the Inter-Ministerial Committee to open a meeting on "Preparation for the inauguration of the Monument to Win-Win and Celebrate The 20th Anniversary of the "Win-Win Day" of the End of the Cambodian Civil War and the Successful Implementation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Win-Win Politics
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Receives a Delegation of Southeast Asian Youth Ship for Recommendations Before Departing Next Week
(Phnom Penh): At the Peace Palace on Tuesday morning, October 16, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, allowed a delegation of Southeast Asian youth ships led by Mr. Nai Semnarat met and received recommendations.
Mr. Nay Semnaroth informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen that the participation in this Southeast Asian Youth Ship has 29 members.
He said this is the 45th time the Southeast Asian youth ship has launched. The 52-day trip, which starts on the 23rd and starts from Japan, will travel through 11 countries, passing through Japan, Brunei, the Philippines, Vietnam and returning to Japan.
During the visit, on behalf of the entire delegation, Mr. Nay Semnaroth asked for a high recommendation from the Prime Minister before joining the Southeast Asian youth.
