Mr. Em Chanmakara said that in Cambodia, "Day of the Deaf" has been organized since 2013 between September or October. For 2018, Deaf Day is organized to encourage the use of sign language for the deaf everywhere and in all programs, especially the use of sign language in the workplace, both public and private institutions with people. C - Deaf to work with.
Mr. Em Chanmakara added that through the implementation of the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, in particular the National Strategic Plan on Disability and other legal documents, found that people with disabilities in Cambodia Full rights Discrimination against people with disabilities has also been significantly reduced.
In fact, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary Chairman of the Disability Action Council, people with disabilities have received quality education, free medical treatment by the state and satellites, and the use of a basic system. Politics for people with disabilities, poverty in the community and support in many ways.
For the 2017-2018 school year, 16 deaf students, including 8 female students, passed the high school diploma exam. Currently, there are 511 deaf students studying at all levels from primary to high school, in addition, 6 deaf students are continuing their studies at the college level. There are about 40,000 deaf people, accounting for 8.3% of the total population of more than 520,000 people with disabilities.
Mr. Em Chanmakara stated that under the leadership of Minister Vong Soth, Chairman of the Council for the Action of the Deaf and Dumb, there is a strong belief that the Royal Government will continue to promote the disability environment in all areas. Levels for the benefit of people with disabilities in Cambodia.
