(Kampong Cham): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, October 16, 2018, presided over the 38th World Food Day 2018 under the theme "Together to reduce hunger Hunger to zero by 2030 "held in Sopheas commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province.
On that occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his appreciation and appreciation to all the working groups and stakeholders who have supported and cooperated well, both technically and financially, which led to this year's World Food Day in the parliamentary environment. Good friendship, solidarity and full cooperation.
This day is held to raise awareness and recognize the important role of agriculture in solving food security, food security, welfare and rural development to end the hunger of the people of some countries across. The universe in 2030.
In response to the Rectangular Policy and Strategy, Phase 4, 6th Legislature of the National Assembly "For Employment Growth, Equity and Efficiency: Building the Basis to Achieve the Vision of Cambodia 2030" Together to Reduce Hunger to Zero by 2030 .
Minister Veng Sakhon requested that each specialized unit as well as relevant institutions, both public and private, and all development partners to pay attention to the implementation of the following policies:
First, to promote the preparation and implementation of the "Master Plan for Agricultural Development towards 2030" and the "Strategic Plan for Agricultural Development 2019-2023" effectively.
Second, increase productivity, quality and diversification by increasing investment in research and development of high value-added crops, animal breeds and fish farming. Promote the development of model farms, the provision of technical services, the strengthening of community farming management, contract farming, the continued reduction of prices and the improvement of the quality of agricultural inputs, as well as the promotion of the use of intelligent and digital technologies.
Third: Participate in promoting the processing industry by promoting private investment in potential agricultural products such as rice, cassava, mango, cashew, banana, rubber, vegetables and so on. Improving the business environment aims to facilitate trade, reduce costs, and increase investment and credit for development and research to support job creation and boost local SME growth.
Fourth, continue to promote the cultivation of all kinds of vegetables instead of imports and facilitate the establishment of wholesale markets and distribution of vegetables with high standards and hygiene.
Fifth, diversify agriculture according to the potential of each geography, not just one field, and professional officials must help disseminate appropriate agricultural techniques, taking into account market needs, avoid following each other without a clear plan.
Sixth, to promote agribusiness by continuing to strengthen sanitation and phytosanitary systems, investment in laboratories for export. Banteay Meanchey Provincial Commissioner Publicly Apologizes to Svay Chek District Police Officer for Violent Citizens and Promises Discipline
(Banteay Meanchey): Banteay Meanchey Provincial Commissioner Major General At Cam has publicly apologized on his official Facebook page to police officers in Svay Chek district for using violence against innocent people. In addition to apologizing, the Banteay Meanchey provincial commissioner also claimed that police officers who commit wrongdoing will be disciplined according to their actions.
"I publicly apologize to the people for the actions of a small number of individuals at the Svay Chek District Inspectorate that have been done to the people of Chamkar Kor village in the past. "Police commit wrongdoing and will be disciplined according to their actions."
Despite the policy of dealing with officials who use violence against citizens during their work at the Svay Chek District Inspector, there is currently no official letter of resignation and dismissal of those officials.
It should be noted that on October 8, police officers under the control of Mr. Chea Sloh, Svay Chek District Inspector, arrested a villager, handcuffed him around his back and kicked him several times in the car without working. Search for any evidence on the case of a traffic accident caused by a Thai man driving a car and hitting a house in Chamkar Kor village, Svay Chek commune, Svay Chek district, Banteay Meanchey province.
After the day of the incident on October 9, 2018, the victim filed a complaint to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner in the case of police officers using violence but no solution, only on October 12, the victim was not satisfied because there is no justice. Also decided to apply for intervention from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Minister of Interior directly.
The motorcyclist who suffered from the violence from the authorities in Chamkar Kor village said that if there are still officials who always torture the people and oppress the people like the Svay district inspector, the people will not live well and will confuse the innocent people. To good leaders with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the head of government.
