(Phnom Penh): Im Vutha, spokesman for the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia (TRC), predicted that there will be only three or four mobile phone companies operating in Cambodia in the future, with seven companies currently operating. .
He stressed that the remaining 3-4 companies do not mean that they are bankrupt, but may be due to the merger of large companies into small companies to expand their operations even more.
He said that this combination has made it important for companies to raise capital and resources to continue investing in new technologies, as new technologies are emerging and need capital to invest. There is a lot of capital, always looking for one, merging companies together to get big capital.
He added that to date, Cambodia has seven mobile phone companies in Cambodia, three of which are large and play the strongest role in Cambodia, while the other four are small companies.
"In the future, with new technology and more capital, those companies can integrate," he said. "I can predict that in the future these companies may have only three or four companies left."
(Phnom Penh): Under the shadow of cold peace in the present era, the heritage of the Khmer ancestors is more preserved, protected and disseminated to the world, such as the Sambor Prei Kuk temple, which is now being promoted on the international stage. Through the image, the meaning and the name of the national representative costume, as well as the jewelry adorned by Miss Cambodia Miss Di Leka.
This beautiful costume of the national representative of Cambodia is the costume of Tepi in Khmer culture in the Chenla period, nicknamed "Tepi Srey Sourbov Isanpura".
This set of goddesses from Isanpura is a combination of the form of the goddess and the form of the goddess of the Chenla period, in accordance with the evidence from the statues and carvings on the walls of Sambor Prei Kuk, as well as the evidence. Various came from excavations as well.
Please be informed that the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List on July 9, 2017. Since then, the Khmer capital of Isanpura, Chenla period, has become more and more known around the world, especially this cultural and historical resort always receives hundreds of thousands of visitors each year. Daily special national-international news summary for October 15, 2018
