(Phnom Penh): After seeing the difficulties and needs of farmers, Angkor Green, a company focused on agriculture, has come together to find a solution for farmers by collaborating with a Cambodian expert, industrial engineer and mechanic to produce sprayers. Modern, automatic medicine that provides convenience and low cost to farmers.
This automatic spraying machine is made with modern technology of the 21st century, which is being used in the countries with advanced agriculture in the world. Now this technology has been produced by Cambodian children and has been tested and successfully used in Cambodia.
Heang Thirado, Chief Executive Officer of Angkor Green Machinery & Technology, said: There is an opportunity to research with modern materials and equipment by practicing and making ideas and goals in the production of this modern machine in Cambodia.
He added that the other is to help farmers in Cambodia who are facing their challenges and needs. This machine will provide convenience to many people, including: saving time, saving money and getting more output.
Mr. Keo Sophannara, Executive Director of Agricultural Machinery, said that this modern spraying machine will help increase work efficiency, reduce production costs by spraying effectively, spraying quickly and many hectares in a short time. Contribute to reducing the use of labor, manage spraying work well, accurately and on time.
He added that in addition to contributing to save up to 4 times compared to the use of labor, saving 40%, reducing the risk of loss of yield by 30-50%. On the other hand, this machine is very safe to spray drugs that do not affect the health of users and do not waste spray ink.
Please be informed that this automatic spraying machine can be equipped with rotary tractor and tractor power from 35 horsepower, equipped with modern technology to control the ink to be sprayed with leaves, plants, crops, all parts. Inside and outside the leaves, which optimizes the use of fertilizers - pesticides.
(China): Since January, China's overall stock market has weakened. However, many analysts believe that the Chinese stock market will recover as Chinese A-Class shares are now more visible on international exchanges, allowing more foreign investors to trade in Chinese stocks.
During the first nine months of this year, the Chinese Stock Exchange authorities also tightened controls on the Chinese stock market, reducing the number of shares that could be publicly traded for the first time to 55 percent. As of the end of September this year, the number approved by the authorities in the first nine months of last year is close to 80 percent.
Also later this year, the Shanghai-London Stock Exchange will officially launch, which will boost A-Class trading.
