(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 15, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen paid a courtesy call on His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia and Samdech Mey. Norodom Monineath Sihanouk during the dedication ceremony of the late King Norodom Sihanouk for the 6th anniversary at the Royal Palace.
On his Facebook page, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "People all over the country, as well as civil servants at all levels of the Armed Forces, express their deepest gratitude to His Majesty the King for his sacrifice and sacrifice." The biggest body for the motherland of Cambodia.
Samdech continued, "Children of the people all over the country and civil servants, please pay your last respects to His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk. May the King be welcomed in his death."
It should be noted that His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, was born on Tuesday, October 31, 1922 in Phnom Penh. He passed away on Monday, October 15, 2012 at 1:20 pm in Beijing, China at the age of 90. The body of the former King was flown on a special flight from China to Cambodia on October 17, 2012 at 3 p.m.
In return for His Majesty the King's gratitude and Brahma for his devotion to the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the Royal Government of Cambodia has designated October 15 as a national holiday and a day of mourning for the people. The whole Khmer. On this day, the royal family, leaders, civil servants at all levels, all ministries, institutions and people across the country always celebrate the death of His Majesty the King.
