Activities of the Cambodian National Assembly delegation at the 139th General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) in Geneva, Switzerland
(Switzerland): A Cambodian parliamentary delegation led by Ms. Khuon Sodary, Second Vice President of the National Assembly, is attending the 203rd Board Meeting of the National Assembly and the 139th General Assembly with 135 members and chairmen from 50 countries. And 40 deputies, including 700 members of parliament, with 20% of young MPs and 33% women.
The 203rd Meeting of the Board of Directors focused on the review of membership, the review of the financial situation, the report on the activities of the President and Secretary-General of the IPU Parliament, which has been completed for one year of the organization, the report of the meeting organized by the IPU on the IPU Strategic Plan 2017- 2021 and the organization of upcoming meetings.
On October 15, 2018, the 139th General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union will vote on two of its urgent agendas, including four proposals:
* Second: Contact Palestinian refugees
* Third: related to climate change and
* Fourth: Related to democracy in Venezuela.
Following the election of the emergency agenda, the 139th General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union will discuss the topic of "Parliamentary Leadership in Promoting Peace and Development in the Age of Innovation and Technological Change." The head of the delegation is scheduled to deliver a speech on the occasion as well.
In addition, the parliamentary delegation also attended the second meeting of the Standing Committee on Sustainable Development, Finance and Trade related to:
* Parliamentary Contribution to the 2018 United Nations Conference on Climate Change
Discussion on the role of free trade and investment in achieving sustainable development, especially in relation to economic equality and sustainable infrastructure
