His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the King Father of Independence, Territorial Integrity and Khmer National Unity, was born on Tuesday, October 31, 1922. Phnom Penh will pass away on Monday, October 15, 2012, the 15th day of the lunar month of Rong Chatva Sak at 1:20 pm (Cambodian time) in Beijing, China at the age of 90. By old age.
His body was flown from Beijing to Phnom Penh by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni and Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on October 17, 2012 at 2:30 p.m. The funeral procession from Phnom Penh International Airport to the Royal Palace through the Independence Monument was attended by a large number of people.
His body was laid to rest at the Royal Palace for at least three months. Three months later, on February 1, 2013, the body of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk was paraded from the Royal Palace to Veal Preah Meru for the cremation ceremony.
