(US): The discovery of evidence of the presence of a large moon outside the solar system is giving scientists more hope to reach the discovery of the moon can sustain life as in the past. This is according to a quote from the website Space.com on Monday afternoon, October 15, 2018.
However, the moon still needs scientists to verify through further observations, and it is likely to be rich in gas, so it is not favorable to sustain life. But there may be other life-saving Exomoon moons waiting for us to find them in the near future.
Surrounding the discovery, scientists are increasingly hoping that one day humans may find a moon with Earth-like environmental conditions, such as Pandora or Endor, which we have all seen in movies. Imagine that.
It should be noted that the moon that can support life refers to a place that is about the size of the planet and has the most suitable atmosphere. Although it orbits a large planet, if it has the right loops and orbits from its parent planet, it can absorb enough starlight during its orbit in conjunction with the parent planet.
Cambodia to send more than 200 Blue Hat troops to Central Africa by end of November
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of National Defense, at the end of November 2018 will send more than 200 of its Blue Hat troops to Central Africa to replace the old engineers who are currently on mission. . This is according to Ms. Kosal Malinda, spokesperson for the National Center for the Management of Peacekeeping Forces to clear mines and unexploded ordnance, which was confirmed this morning, October 15, 2018.
Ms. Kosal Malinda said that by the end of November, Cambodia will send an additional 216 peacekeepers under the United Nations (UN) to Central Africa at the request of the United Nations.
"We are ready to replace the old forces who will be completing their one-year mission in Central Africa, and the force will be trained," the spokesman said. They are all gone. ”
Countries to which Cambodia has sent Blue Hat troops include Central Africa, Sudan, South Sudan, Syria, Chad, Lebanon, Cyprus and Mali. The Royal Government of Cambodia is determined not to give up on the deployment of the Blue Hat Force at the request of the United Nations, despite the fact that the Cambodian Blue Hat Force sacrificed many lives during their mission. That.
Youth Association for Comfort in Cambodia declares full support for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's firm stance in defending sovereignty
(Phnom Penh): The Youth Association for Comfort in Cambodia, headed by Oknha Phasok Dr. Keang Seng and its leaders and all members, has declared their full support for the firm stance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in Defending the sovereignty, independence and peace of Cambodia without giving in to any foreign threats or warnings.
The announcement of support of the Youth Association for Comfort in Cambodia was made after Samdech Techo Hun Sen during a meeting with students and people in Japan on October 7, 2018 during Samdech Techo's visit. The visit to Japan proclaimed its firm stance on maintaining Cambodia's sovereignty and independence, not allowing any foreigners to step on it in exchange for aid or any warning.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized, "I say again and again, do not trade national sovereignty for aid, do not trade the country's peace for aid. Now, who wants to manage Cambodia in any way, but Cambodia must be strong in defending its sovereignty and independence. If Cambodia can not implement Cambodian law, it is necessary to go and do what Cambodia needs to do, what needs to be done as a country. ”
In the petition in support of the Youth Association for Comfort in Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on October 15, 2018, stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's firm stance is the most courageous patriotic heroism. And is historically relevant to the entire Cambodian nation and has been carried out in the most accurate manner in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution of Cambodia.
Through this petition, the Youth Association for Comfort in Cambodia has announced its commitment to strictly implement the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and commit all sacrifices to absolutely protect the independence, peace, sovereignty, territorial integrity and interests of the Cambodian nation.
The Youth Association for Comfort in Cambodia has also stated that it strongly does not support the position of some individuals with opposite tendencies who agree to bow to foreigners as an excuse to interfere in the internal affairs of the sovereign state of Cambodia.
