On Sunday morning, October 14, 2018, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, led a professional officer and a road repair team from the Ministry and the engineering team to inspect and start repairing this road. During December, before the Sea Festival to facilitate the travel of people traveling across this road, as well as to visit the Sea Festival in Koh Kong.
Minister Sun Chanthol claimed that the damaged road is 63 kilometers long, divided into 91 places. He claimed that he had now installed 114 vehicles from both the ministry's construction team and the engineering team to speed up work to repair the road before the Sea Festival later this year.
