Samdech Sar Kheng Leads Inter-Ministerial Delegation to Return to Cambodia After Attending Conference on Illegal Wildlife Trafficking in London
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, led an inter-ministerial delegation to return to Cambodia this morning, October 14, 2018, after visiting and attending a conference on illegal wildlife trafficking in the city. London for 2 days.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng leads a high-level inter-ministerial delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to attend the 4th Conference on Illegal Wildlife Trade in London, United Kingdom on October 11-12, 2018 at the invitation of the Royal Government United Kingdom. The conference is attended by heads of state, government, the private sector and international organizations from around the world.
The first conference on illegal wildlife trafficking was held under the initiative of Prince Charles of the United Kingdom in 2013 in London with the aim of mobilizing the conservation and conservation of natural resources and strengthening law enforcement. And prevent the illegal trade in rare wildlife and wildlife products such as ivory, rhinoceros horn.
One of the key topics that will be discussed at the 4th Conference is related to the impact of the scope of illegal wildlife trafficking, with the proceeds of the illegal trade also leading to Serious crimes include other organizations such as money laundering, terrorism, human trafficking, illegal arms trafficking, etc.
