(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's young national badminton player Vat Vanthun has teamed up with players from seven other countries to win a gold medal in the multi-national team event at the 2018 Youth Olympic Games in Phnom Penh. Argentina this morning, October 13. This is according to Lt. Gen. Ly Kosal, President of the Badminton Federation of Cambodia.
Lt. Gen. Ly Kosal confirmed that for Vat Vanthun's individual discipline in the above mission has failed. Then, the International Olympic Committee and the International Badminton Federation set up a program to compete as a multi-ethnic team in the sense of friendship and solidarity between young men and women around the world, requiring badminton players from all countries to work. Pair in groups of 8, with 8 countries in each group.
It should be noted that this multi-national team competition is not an official discipline in the 3rd Youth Olympic Games in Argentina, but the President of the Badminton Federation of Cambodia considered the gold medal as a multi-national team. A great achievement for the Cambodian badminton family to motivate athletes to work harder to achieve the goal of winning official Olympic medals for the nation in the future.
