South Korean government lends more than $ 66 million to build health university hospital
The South Korean government, through the Economic Development Cooperation Fund (EDCF), will provide about $ 66.57 million in loans for the construction of a university hospital, according to the South Korean Embassy in Phnom Penh. Health.
In a press release obtained by Fresh News on October 12, 2018, the South Korean Embassy noted that the lack of adequate hospitals in Cambodia has steadily increased the need for a systematic and inclusive clinical curriculum. Combined to provide a more therapeutic experience with greater patient growth for physicians such as medical students in training.
The statement added that once the University of Health Sciences (UHS) hospital construction project is developed with the support of the EDCF, it will be possible to develop high-quality medical professionals in a systematic way.
The South Korean government expects Cambodians to benefit from modern medical services through the supply and installation of state-of-the-art medical equipment and hospital information systems.
The Economic Development Cooperation Fund (EDCF) was established by the Korean government in 1987 to promote economic exchanges with global development and to assist developing countries in achieving industrialization and economic stability. Providing long-term, low-interest loans. The Export-Import Bank of Korea is currently in charge of managing the fund.
The project aims to train a professional workforce with good quality of education as well as to provide high quality health services by establishing a 200-bed hospital with high-tech medical equipment.
Since 2001, the South Korean government has provided a total of $ 766 million in EDCF loans to support 22 projects in Cambodia.
