National Bank of Cambodia, ASEAN finance ministers and IMF discuss economic war
(Indonesia): Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, together with the ASEAN Finance Minister and the Managing Director of the International Monetary Fund (IMF), met to discuss economic warfare and find a solution.
The issue of economic warfare was discussed at the 2018 General Assembly of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and the World Bank (WB) in Bali, Indonesia, held for 3 days from 10-12 months. October 2018.
The 2018 General Assembly was chaired by Indonesian President Joko Widodo, and was attended by leaders of a number of ASEAN countries, including Cambodian leaders, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as the Prime Ministers of Laos, Vietnam and Myanmar. .
The conference aims to provide a global forum for leaders in the financial sector, including: the governors of the central banks and finance ministers of IMF and WB member countries meeting to discuss progress, challenges and policies. Solve to support economic growth as well as provide information on the latest IMF and WB policy programs.
A delegation from the National Bank of Cambodia attended a meeting of the 12-member International Monetary Fund (SEAVG) of the International Monetary Fund (SEAVG). The meeting highlighted regional challenges, especially trade wars and the tightening of international financial market conditions due to the normalization of central bank policy in developed countries such as the United States.
The meeting raised the issue of trade wars that could benefit countries in the region as the diversion of production from China to these countries would boost exports. However, countries in Southeast Asia must also strive to compete with other regions such as: Europe, Japan, Korea, and Mexico.
In addition, the tightening of international financial market conditions could lead to a depreciation of the regional currency and put pressure on lending rates on regional financial markets, which could also affect the regional economy.
The meeting highlighted three main policies for the region to maintain sustainable growth, including: 1. Building a cushion and supporting potential growth. 2. Strengthening the resilience of the financial sector. 3. Promoting and promoting the system. Multilateralization of trade, addressing external imbalances and climate change and tariffs.
Ms. Neav Chanthana, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, was invited as a speaker at the Political Dialogue on Regional Cooperation for Innovation, Environment and Stability in Asia.
In addition, the delegation of the National Bank of Cambodia met with the representatives of the Capital and Monetary Department of the International Monetary Fund to discuss the need for technical assistance for the National Bank of Cambodia in the future. Delegates also attended meetings, especially on trade wars, financial technology, monetary policy regulation, financial environment and financial stability, and women's financial environment.
