(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chheang Vun, Chairman of the Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation Committee on Propaganda and Information of the National Assembly of Cambodia, called on the European Commission (EU) to remove the Cambodian Preferential Tariffs (EBAs) on the grounds of human rights and democracy. Only the excuses of Italy and Sweden to eliminate the presence of Cambodian goods in the European market.
Mr. Chheang Vun made this statement while attending the General Assembly of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) in Geneva, Switzerland on the afternoon of October 12, 2018.
Chheang Vun, who has served as an ambassador to the World Trade Organization, claimed that Cambodia has been enjoying preferential tariffs on imports to the EU for more than 10 years. Italy and Sweden have lost a lot of benefits.
According to Chheang Vun, Cambodian goods on the European market with these tariffs have cost Italy, Europe's largest rice supplier, a huge market, while Sweden, a sugar producer, is also affected. Chheang Vun said the two countries were unhappy with Cambodian goods on the European market with preferential tariffs.
Mr. Chheang Vun considered the efforts of the two senior EU officials to remove Cambodia's preferential tariffs as one of their excuses to eliminate Cambodian goods from the European market alone, not as an effort. To save the process of respecting human rights or the process of democracy in Cambodia, as they say.
Mr. Chheang Vun also expressed regret to some Cambodian politicians that he criticized the former opposition politicians because for their own benefit, trying to achieve the ambitions of other nations, betraying the interests of their own people.
However, Chheang Vun said that while attending the IPU meeting in Geneva, Switzerland, which would be attended by EU lawmakers, he would try to further explain the real problems and situation in Cambodia.
Mr. Chheang Vun said that of the 27 or so EU lawmakers, many had good relations with Cambodia, and only a small number were in conflict with Cambodia because Cambodian goods harmed their interests. Mr. Chheang Vun: Representatives of the Cambodian Parliament will make a statement to tell the IPU to understand the will of the Cambodian people after the election
