Cambodian Minister of Agriculture asks China to support fisheries, especially modern freshwater aquaculture
During the meeting, Minister Veng Sakhon thanked the Government of the People's Republic of China for its continued support and good partnership in the socio-economic development of Cambodia. In fact, hydropower infrastructure and irrigation systems have been supported by the Chinese friends.
At the same time, Mith Chet has also contributed to supporting the process of agricultural development in Cambodia, in which some private sectors have also been investing in cultivation as well as processing agricultural products in Cambodia.
The Minister made a number of proposals to the Chinese side to support the production of hybrid rice varieties to increase the productivity of rice production in Cambodia, as well as to consider the support to support the infrastructure and cultivation procedures in a responsive manner. According to the requirements of the Chinese side, Cambodia can export some fruits to the Chinese market, such as mango and dragon fruit.
At the same time, Minister Veng Sakhon also requested the Chinese side to support the fisheries sub-sector in Cambodia, especially the modern freshwater aquaculture to promote the export of fishery products to international markets.
In addition, the Minister requested the Chinese side to provide support for meat quality and animal health analysis equipment to the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production so that Cambodia can effectively strengthen food safety.
In addition, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Cambodia has been studying the plan to modernize agriculture in Cambodia with the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs of China and hopes that through this meeting, Mr. Maigu will help promote the implementation of this project to proceed quickly.
In response, Maigu said that the Chinese Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs will cooperate with the China Agricultural Research and Development Institute to support the production of hybrid varieties in Cambodia, as the institute currently produces a wide range of hybrid varieties. Suitable for cultivation in Cambodia.
Mr. Maigu also supported the sharing of experiences to Cambodia related to animal health management and animal hygiene through support for staff capacity building. He also promised to encourage more Chinese investors to invest in Cambodia's agricultural sector, and the Chinese side also welcomed Cambodian agricultural products intended to bring to China.
He added that in the process of planning to modernize agriculture in Cambodia, he will help urge the Department of International Cooperation to continue to accelerate the implementation and regularly monitor the progress of the implementation of this project.
