SAN FRANCISCO (Reuters) - Washington's Supreme Court has overturned the death penalty for the third time, making it the 20th state in the United States to ban the death penalty. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday afternoon, October 12, 2018.
The Supreme Court of Washington has ruled that the death penalty is not valid because it is arbitrary and racist and does not serve the purpose of imposing any legal punishment.
Washington Governor Jay Inslee, meanwhile, welcomed the decision, saying the state Supreme Court's decision to end the death penalty in Washington was an important step forward. Towards the implementation of an equitable and transparent justice system.
Officials of Kampong Speu Province will never forget the noble merits of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of Friday, October 12, 2018, the Kampong Speu Provincial Administration held a ceremony to honor the late King Bhumibol Adulyadej. Yes, Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King Father of the Khmer Independence, on the 6th anniversary of his death.
The event was attended by provincial leaders, the armed forces, departments, units, civil servants, monks and the people, held in front of the provincial hall.
His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk was born on October 31, 1922 in Phnom Penh. He was the son of King Norodom Suramarit and Queen Sisowath Kosama.
He passed away at 1:20 a.m. on October 15, 2012 (Cambodian time) at the age of 90 at a hospital in Beijing, China. October 15, 2018 marks the 6th anniversary of the death of His Majesty the King Father of Khmer National Independence, Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, leaving his beloved people and territory, and also the day when Khmer children and the Khmer nation The whole is very sad.
Samdech Preah Borom Ratanakoth is considered by the whole Cambodian people as the King and the Great King of Cambodia, who sacrificed his body and mind throughout his life for the cause of the motherland and bring great benefits to the people. His people, especially the Royal Crusade for independence from France on November 9, 1953. Samdech Prime Minister Hun Sen: Japan is a model for Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, told a well-known international journalist that he considered Japan as a model for Cambodia in strengthening democracy and national development.
Prime Minister Hun Sen has made it clear that Cambodia will continue to move towards democracy, even if his ruling party wins all the seats in the National Assembly in the July general election.
In an exclusive interview with Japan's Kyodo newspaper last week, Hun Sen said, "Japan is a model of democracy that we should learn from and the only country we can learn from."
The Prime Minister said that Samdech is willing to promote the relationship between the two countries into a "comprehensive strategic cooperation partnership", while appreciating Japan for its enormous assistance for economic development and infrastructure in the Kingdom of Cambodia. .
"Cambodia would like to express its deep gratitude to the Government of Japan for its significant contribution to peace in Cambodia and for providing substantial technical assistance, grants and concessional loans for the rehabilitation and development of Cambodia's economic and social infrastructure," he said. "Such as transport infrastructure, health, education and training of human resources."
Japan has the potential to become Cambodia's second most comprehensive strategic partner after China in 2010. It should be reminded that in 2013, Cambodia-Japan relations reached a "strategic partnership" and in 2018, this is also the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Japan and Cambodia.
It should be noted that Mekong-Japan cooperation aims to reduce the development gap among ASEAN member countries and promote ASEAN integration. The cooperation aims to achieve sustainable economic growth, taking into account the environment and health, as well as ensuring lasting peace and stability in the region. Engineering Command declares full support for Samdech Techo's firm stance in defending sovereignty
(Phnom Penh): General Kwan Seam, Commander of the Engineering Command, as well as all officers, deputies and soldiers, express their full support for the firm stance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in defending its sovereignty. And the peace of Cambodia without compromising on any foreign threats or warnings.
The statement of support of General Kwan Sam came after Samdech Techo Hun Sen during a meeting with students and people in Japan on October 7, 2018 during Samdech Techo's visit to Japan has declared its firm stance on maintaining Cambodia's sovereignty and independence, not allowing any foreigners to step on it in exchange for any aid or warning.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized, "I say again and again, do not trade national sovereignty for aid, do not trade the country's peace for aid. Now, who wants to manage Cambodia in any way, but Cambodia must be strong in defending its sovereignty and independence. If Cambodia can not implement Cambodian law, it is necessary to do what Cambodia needs to do, what needs to be done as a country. ”
