(Phnom Penh): On October 11, 2018, Learning Jungle International School collected charitable donations to the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia. This is the fourth time that this international school has continued to save the lives of Cambodian children.
Learning Jungle International School is the only Canadian-licensed international school in Cambodia to provide the highest level of education and is accredited by Learning Jungle Canada and the Ministry of Education. Youth and Sports Cambodia and the school has organized a fundraising program for Kantha Bopha Hospital to encourage students to have a spirit of helping each other and solidarity.
To contribute to saving the lives of children in need of medical treatment, Mr. Ly Virak, Chairman of the Board of Learning Jungle International School, initiated the idea of organizing a fourth charity fundraiser to help Kantha Bopha Hospital through ticket sales. Participate in the graduation ceremony and art performance of students at Sofitel Hotel on June 24, 2018.
Funds raised from all ticket sales from the parents and guardians of the students and the school administration totaled $ 8,000,000 (US $ 8,000) and were donated to the Kantha Bopha Foundation on the 11th of this month. So far, Learning Jungle International School has so far donated a total of more than $ 25,000,000 (twenty-five thousand US dollars) to Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Mr. Ly Virak also called on the public to continue to help Kantha Bopha Hospital and Cambodian children in need to receive free treatment, because healthy children are the bamboo shoots of our country in the future. .
Meanwhile, the Director of Kantha Bopha Hospital, Mr. Ky Santy, thanked the Learning Jungle International School for its continued support to the hospital. The hospital team will continue to work together to maintain high standards. The quality of health services is more effective for Cambodian children.
"Every day, at least 2,000 children come to Kantha Bopha Hospital for treatment," he said.
