(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will lead a high-level delegation to return home this afternoon, October 12, 2018, after attending a summit in Japan and Indonesia for more than a week.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen leads a delegation to attend the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit in Tokyo, Japan for 5 days from October 6 to 10, 2018. The meeting discussed and approved the new Tokyo Strategy aimed at improving connectivity, promoting people's well-being and protecting the environment. The strategy focuses on sustainable development and bridging the development gap between the Mekong and other ASEAN members.
