(Phnom Penh): A defender was shot several times by a man, causing serious injuries to his legs, causing a surprise at 12:55 pm on October 12, 2018 in a dirt road No. 345 is located in Sangkat Toul Sangke 2, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
The injured victim said that before the incident, he was chasing the suspect on two motorcycles, who fled from the People's Defense Force and the intervention force of Russey Keo district until they chased him to Road 345, suddenly heard a sound. The gunman realized that he had been chased by a man and fired about 10 shots, injuring his right leg.
After the incident, the police arrested the perpetrator for further questioning at the Russey Keo district inspector. ASEAN-US Business Council sees high demand and potential for animal feed market in Cambodia
This statement was made by the ASEAN-US Business Council during a working meeting with Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture and Forestry on priority policies and opportunities for agricultural investment in Cambodia on October 11, 2018 at Hanoi, Vietnam.
Minister Veng Sakhon welcomed and expressed his pleasure that the ASEAN-US Business Council has invested in Cambodia in the past and plans to expand investment in agriculture in Cambodia.
The Minister stressed that Cambodia is in need of investment in the development of modern agriculture to promote agricultural growth in line with the turn of economic growth and can keep up with the development situation in the region.
The ASEAN-US Business Council noted that the feed market in Cambodia has high potential and demand, as well as investment in modern technology, which is attractive to members of the ASEAN-US Business Council.
In addition, USABC is interested in strengthening food security and promoting the productivity of agricultural products, which are important issues that ASEAN countries have been paying attention to.
The General Department of Health and Animal Production has expressed a willingness to work closely with private partners. The General Department confirmed that Cambodia has laws and regulations to control and supervise animal husbandry, animal health and public health, animal feed and veterinary medicine.
However, Cambodia still needs to prepare more regulations to make management more effective, especially on food safety. In this case, Cambodia requested the private sector to support the training of officials and infrastructure for the analysis of wastes in meat and animal products.
USABC also plans to partner with the US Embassy in Cambodia to launch a food safety awareness campaign in Cambodia in early 2019. The USABC plans to hold workshops on quality standards to promote high-quality exports to international markets and develop climate-resilient varieties.
