Phnom Penh Governor Inspects the Surrounding of Victory Monument to Prepare for the Opening Ceremony on December 29
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh inspected the area around the Victory Monument in the Ly Yong Phat Development Zone in Chroy Changvar District to clear the forest and drain the sewer to prepare security and order for the inauguration of the Victory Monument by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Presiding.
On the afternoon of October 11, 2018, Mr. Khuong Sreng, the Governor of Phnom Penh, said that “Prey Treng around the Victory Monument will be cleared. The water behind the Victory Monument and to the west of the monument must also be drained by drains into the Tonle Sap.
He stated that this arrangement is for the sake of beauty and convenience in arranging security and order for the people, senior leaders, as well as security for Samdech Techo.
Phnom Penh Governor Khuong Sreng confirmed that the inauguration ceremony of the Victory Monument will be held on December 29, 2018, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen presiding over the event. In addition to the inauguration program, the commission also organized a three-day exhibition, which was attended by all state institutions, especially in the field of defense of Cambodia.
He stated that in addition to organizing public order, the Capital Hall will decorate the street lighting from the base of Prek Pnov Bridge to National Road 6 and will open to the public and international visitors to see the results and success. Peace to Cambodia and progress in all areas until today.
At the same time, the governor also installed 20 ambulances and two emergency booths.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, said that the department will install electricity along all the Chan Kiri trees along the road, install a drainage system nearly 500 meters and engrave on the inscription "As a boulevard. "Win, win" at the beginning of the road. He said that for this work, the Department of Public Works has already done something, such as laying sewers.
He added that the Victory Monument is decorated with sculptures on Memorial Day sculptures dedicated to the overthrow of the genocidal regime and sculptures of the Cambodian national movement in the 1980s and early 1990s on display on the ground floor outside the palace.
It should be noted that the construction of the Victory Monument started in February 2016, which is built on an area of 15 hectares with a height of 54 meters in the development area of Ly Yong Phat in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh. Japan urges Cambodia to support selection of Osaka for World Expo
