Introductory Plan on Organizing the 6-Year Anniversary of the Honor of His Majesty the King "His Majesty the King"
(Phnom Penh): In 2018, the Royal Government of Cambodia, together with the Royal Family, leaders, civil servants at all levels, all Ministries, Secretaries of State, Capital and Provincial Institutions, and the people throughout the country will celebrate the 6th anniversary of His Majesty the King "His Majesty the King". On October 15, 2018 in the future.
In return for His Majesty's merits and noble Brahma, His Majesty the King sacrificed his body, intellect and wisdom in his actions for the cause of national independence, territorial integrity, national reconciliation, national unity and development in all fields.
According to the National Committee for Organizing National and International Festivals, signed by His Majesty the King of Cambodia, President Srengkar Kong Sam Ol, recently launched the following guidelines:
1: The Ministry of the Royal Palace organizes a ceremony to honor the late King "His Majesty the King" according to religious traditions, national traditions and at the will of His Majesty the King of Life on the Stone and His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia as a sacred place. The highest.
2: The National Committee for Organizing National and International Festivals shall organize a program for all Ministries, Secretaries of State, Institutions and Administration of Phnom Penh to pay homage to the late King "His Majesty the King" in the garden east of the Independence Monument on October 15, 2018.
3: All Ministries, Secretaries of State, Institutions and Administration of Phnom Penh shall assign a delegation to present wreaths in honor of His Majesty the King "His Majesty the King" at the East Garden of the Independence Monument on October 15, 2018 at 7:30 AM. .
6: The Ministry of Information organizes a wide-ranging program on private national radio and television about the royal biography, royal activities and works of His Majesty the King "His Majesty the King" as the highest reverence for the nation, religion and people.
7. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation instructs all embassies and consulates of the Kingdom of Cambodia abroad to celebrate the 6th anniversary of the death of His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej.
8. The Office of the Council of Ministers and the Ministry of Economy and Finance must be prepared to handle the budget for the preparation of the ceremony to pay homage to the late King "His Majesty the King" in a timely manner.
It should be reminded that His Majesty King Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King Father, the father of independence, territorial integrity and national unity of Khmer, was born on Tuesday, October 11, 2465, which is on October 31. 1922 He passed away on Monday, October 15, 2012, at the age of 90, receiving the posthumous title of "Preah Borom Ratanakoth". Quote AKP
This presentation was made while Samdech Techo Hun Sen attended the forum of ASEAN leaders in Bali, Indonesia on the afternoon of October 11, 2018. The event was also attended by the Secretary-General of the United Nations, the President of the World Bank and the President of the International Monetary Fund.
In front of the ASEAN leaders and the leaders of the world's top institutions, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that ASEAN is one of the fastest growing economies and societies in the world, the sixth largest economy in the world. With an estimated population of 640 million, it is a major force for global trade and growth.
Along with this positive development, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed concern over the current development of the world, which could adversely affect ASEAN member countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the world is currently moving towards a new polar framework, a shift in strength and balance, as well as facing geopolitical, terrorist and regional and global issues, as well as climate change and climate change. Global economic and financial uncertainty due to protectionist politics, trade wars, violations of multilateralism and vulnerabilities in global and regional financial sectors.
In addition, ASEAN also faces some of its own real challenges, such as the aging and declining labor force, the skills gap in the Industrial Revolution 4.0, the development gap between member countries, and the distribution of fruits, equitable growth, and sustainability issues. Utilization of natural resources.
In this context, Samdech Techo stressed that ASEAN needs to further strengthen cooperation with existing partners, restore the global trading system on the basis of international law, and continue to integrate connectivity in all areas to strengthen resilience. ASEAN to the evolving political, economic and social situation, so we need to ensure macroeconomic and financial stability, support environmental growth.
Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, October 11: 564 illegal vehicles were found and 385 fines were imposed.
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for October 11, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 3,151 vehicles and found 564 vehicles violating the law (89% motorcycles), 179 education vehicles and 385 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 2,133 helmets and goggles were inspected on October 11, 110 education helmets and 358 helmets were fined.
