Heng Sour's claim comes after the European Commission announced that it was continuing its proceedings on the removal of Cambodia's preferential tariffs on Cambodian goods on the pretext that it violated human rights and democracy. That is a fact that leaves the technical basis of the conditions and the actual situation in Cambodia.
Mr. Heng Sour emphasized that the decision of the European Union (EU) could undermine the role of the ILO and the various projects of EU partners in the field of employment, and that other countries may withdraw from participating in both projects. "This is because the European Union does not take the results and realities of the improvement of working conditions as a basis, but rather the policy of interfering with the sovereignty of other nations."
The manifestation of the European Union will make Cambodia stronger, more united and united as a whole by strengthening public institutions, strengthening productivity and human resources, as well as reducing some unnecessary administrative barriers, all of which are fundamental. Sure of Cambodia's long-term competitiveness.
Heng Sour also warned journalists and opposition politicians abroad to be careful in their analysis and commentary on the EBA order, as it could anger workers as whistleblowers. Smoke. He stressed that if the opposition has national ideals and loves the Cambodian people, they should not bow down to the European Union to abuse workers and their families because of the benefits of exporting clothes and shoes.
The European Union is directly in the pockets of workers and their families. The Royal Government has exempted many garments from the garment sector, reduced the price of electricity in order to increase the minimum wage for workers, and has not levied taxes on the minimum wage and other benefits of workers.
It should be noted that in the face of the threat of the European Union, the Royal Government of Cambodia has shown a firm position, not surrendering to this threat in exchange for sacrificing national sovereignty, renouncing the implementation of the country's laws.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's commitment to stand firm is fully supported by all ministries, institutions, the armed forces, government officials and the Cambodian people.
At the same time, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia on October 11, 2018 also responded to the decision of the European Union, considering that this decision was made unjustly without studying the reality of Cambodian society and does not recognize To the valuable development efforts of the past 20 years that the Royal Government of Cambodia has tried to lift millions of men and women out of poverty.
The Royal Government has expressed its strong position that if European institutions decide to impose sanctions on Cambodia, it will make the Royal Government of Cambodia more determined to protect and maintain its legitimate and legitimate actions.
The ministry stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia is committed to building a democratic state by respecting the rights of all citizens in accordance with its values and traditions, but within the framework of the rule of law, no one can be above the law, even activists. Political or a member of a civil society group.
