Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin came out in support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen during a meeting with students and people in Japan on October 7, 2018 during his visit to Cambodia. Japan has declared its firm stance on maintaining Cambodia's sovereignty and independence, not allowing any foreigners to step on it in exchange for any aid or warning.
Samdech Techo said that once bowed to a foreigner, there will be a series of bowings that cannot be recovered, and bowing to a foreigner in exchange for aid or in exchange for something is a violation of sovereignty. And Cambodia's national independence as well. As the person responsible for the nation's destiny since the liberation of the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, Samdech Techo asserted that he would not bow to foreigners in return for anything.
In a petition in support of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which was received by Fresh News on October 11, 2018, the Deputy Prime Minister stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's firm stance is patriotic and patriotic. Strictly abide by the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia in Article 52.
The ministers and officials of the Office of the Council of Ministers have also stated that they do not support the position of some individuals with opposite tendencies who have bowed their heads to foreigners as an excuse to interfere in the internal affairs of the sovereign state of Cambodia.
