(Kampot): An 8-year-old girl went missing while crossing the canal with her family and was found in the middle of Prek Kamchay River in the resort area of Bat Kbal Damrey village, Mak Prang commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province. 07:30 pm, October 10, 2018.
According to local police, prior to the incident, a family member rented a mobile ferry to cross to the other side to visit relatives on the north side of the creek. On the way back, there seemed to be negligence on the part of both drivers and passengers.
In addition, the bus was small enough to carry up to nine people, and all of the nine occupants without airbags were five children, four adults, and the driver upon arrival. Half of the canal was also exposed by the ferry.
At that time, the workers in the huts on both sides of the canal saw and shouted and took the boat to help rescue the eight people who were in the incident, but one girl was missing and the bus disappeared forever. By the afternoon of October 11, 2018.
Despite the water border police in cooperation with the relevant authorities to intervene in the search, they have not yet found the child victim and a bus that appeared.
The same police officer added that the missing girl named Vav Ang, 8 years old, resides in Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh. Her father is a police officer.
