The bridge connecting central China's Henan Province and northern China's Shanxi Province is a two-story bridge, with the upper layer being the expressway and the lower layer being the railway.
"Right now, the height of the bottom of the steel bridge is about two meters higher than the height we planned," said Lin Jiazhi, a fourth-team engineer with China Railway Bridge Engineering. "We should reduce the height of the bottom of the bridge by using the bridge supports and bridge supports to bring the bottom of the bridge back to the height we planned."
The bridge will open to traffic in October 2019, and once completed, it will be an important transportation network for northern and southern China.
The bridge crosses a significant section of the Yellow River, as well as a number of lakes, which are important habitats for migratory birds. For this reason, the bridge builders were very careful to reduce the noise and light of the bridge, as well as to change the color of the bridge to reduce the impact of the bridge on birds.
"We have been very careful about the equipment we build, and we have chosen low-noise equipment," said Xu Xingyuan, a fourth-team engineer with China Railway Bridge Construction Engineering. "We have sent some of our teams to specialize in monitoring the volume of our machines along the tracks in order to reduce the noise to the geese here."
Birds that move like geese are very sensitive to light at night. Therefore, the bridge builders have chosen LED lights, especially for lighting the site at night. The company that built the bridge changed the color of the bridge from orange to blue, according to the opinion of bird conservation experts.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Leads a High-Level Delegation to Arrive Safely in Bali, Indonesia
(Bali, Indonesia): The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, at 4 pm on October 10, 2018 (Cambodian time) led a high-level Cambodian delegation to Bali, Indonesia safely to attend the meeting. ASEAN Leaders Meeting from 10-12 October 2018.
"Today, I and my delegation left Tokyo, Japan for Bali, Indonesia after a 10-hour flight," he wrote on his Facebook page. "As planned, I and my delegation will meet with the Heads of State, Heads of Government of ASEAN, the Secretary-General of the United Nations, the President of the World Bank, the Director of the International Monetary Fund and other stakeholders focused on the economy."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further confirmed that Samdech will lead the high-level delegation of Cambodia back to the motherland on the afternoon of October 12, 2018 tomorrow.
At the same time, the head of the Royal Government wished his compatriots from afar and posted a photo of Samdech at the age of 26 to compare the young and the old.
Please be reminded that on the island of Bali, like other ASEAN leaders, Samdech Techo Prime Minister will address two interventions, the first in the forum of the ASEAN Leaders Meeting and the second in the opening ceremony. Annual Meeting of the International Monetary Fund and the World Bank 2018. The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training fully supports Samdech Techo Hun Sen's firm stance in defending national sovereignty
