To know more, please watch the video of General Meas Virith's explanation as follows: This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen left Japan to attend the ASEAN Leaders' Forum in Bali, Indonesia.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 10, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, left Japan for Indonesia to attend the ASEAN Leaders' Meeting from October 10-12, 2018. In Bali, at the invitation of Joko Widodo, President of the Republic of Indonesia. This was confirmed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen through Samdech's official Facebook page.
The ASEAN Leaders' Meeting will be held under the theme "Achieving Sustainable Development Goals and Successfully in Reducing Development Gap through Regional and Global Cooperation Activities" in conjunction with the Plenary Meeting. Annual Meeting of the Board of Directors of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and the World Bank (2018).
Samdech Techo Hun Sen was accompanied by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Senior Minister Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, senior members of the Royal Government, as well as business leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
On the occasion of the ASEAN Leaders' Meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will deliver a keynote address on the resilience of ASEAN economies, potential markets, the fourth industrial revolution, the building of the ASEAN Economic Community and the Millennium Development Goals.
