Drinking alcohol to take selfies near slippery waterfalls, falling head-on with dead rocks at Thmar Da Toch waterfall, Pursat province
(Pursat): A man slipped and fell into a waterfall about 10 meters high and died while preparing to take a selfie on Pchum Ben Day. This incident caused a surprise at 12:35 on October 9, 2018 at Thmor Da Toch natural waterfall in Ekpheap village, Thmor Da commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
Veal Veng District Police Inspector Theang Leng said that the victim was identified as Koy Sros, a 28-year-old Cambodian man currently living in Dey Krahorm Village, Anlong Reap Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province.
The inspector said that before the incident, the victim drank alcohol and went to the selfie at the scene, immediately did not take selfie, the victim slipped and fell into a ravine that is about deep. 10 meters and hit the head with a stone into the water, also caused a surprise, they searched for almost an hour, only to find a miserable death at once.
After the incident, the competent authorities searched the scene and handed over the body to the relatives to accept for the traditional ceremony.
