(Tokyo, Japan): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has told Japanese businessmen that Cambodia welcomes all Japanese investments and assures all investors a favorable environment and encourages special investment. Peace, security and political stability, as well as macroeconomics, effective legal and institutional frameworks, transparency, accountability and predictability.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia welcomed and assured Japanese investment in Cambodia during Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech at the Mekong-Japan Business Forum on "Asia's Value Concentration Zone" Tokyo, October 9, 2018.
Samdech Techo stated, "On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, I would like to welcome all the wise decisions of all investors, especially Japanese investors who have selected and intend to select Cambodia as a potential investment destination to start or Expand its business.
The Prime Minister called on Japanese investors who have not yet come to Cambodia to study and explore the investment potential and opportunities in Cambodia, and decided to invest to maximize the achievements of the Royal Government of Japan to support Cambodia. .
Along with calling on Japanese investors to do business in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted many potentials and opportunities that are conducive to investment. The potential and opportunities that Samdech Techo presented at that time include:
Second, Cambodia is strategically located in the ASEAN region, which has been becoming the "factory of Asia" and on the other hand, Cambodia is in the middle of the Mekong region, a region with higher economic growth and connectivity. They. At the same time, the shift of the center of economic growth to Asia, especially East Asia, continues to be a "golden opportunity" for Cambodia to develop and modernize its manufacturing and service industries with other countries in the region.
Third, a rich and young workforce, in which the population under the age of 35 accounts for 72% of the total population, combined with an increase in the middle-income and upper class population. The center will create opportunities for Cambodia to achieve high economic growth for the next three decades.
Fifth, Cambodian-made goods are not only supplied to the Cambodian market with a population of over 15 million, but can also supply the Mekong sub-region market with about 250 million customers, the ASEAN market with about 630 customers. Millions of people and the regional market of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RECP), which has about 3 billion customers and access to other major markets in the world.
