After the end of the war, King Chan Reachea ascended the throne to rule the entire Khmer Kingdom, and he managed to build a pagoda according to the oath, including Wat Traleng Keng, which is located in the new capital.
In Longvek, you can visit an ancient temple in Wat Traleng Keng called the Four-Faced Temple, built in the Khmer style of the Phnom Kingdom period. In this ancient temple, there is a reclining Buddha statue standing in four directions.
To the northeast of the four-faced temple, there is another ancient temple, Preah Ko Preah Keo, which houses the Buddha statues, Preah Ko Preah Keo and other small and large statues.
In the temple of Wat Traleng Keng of Longvek is rich in cultural, historical and other heritage, such as Neang Pov pond, which at the bottom of the pond when the water recedes in the dry season, found the remains of the pillars known to the locals as the pillars of the temple Neang Pov is just called Prasat Neang Pov.
