The full text of the statement of the Cambodian Social Advisory Agency is as follows: After 20 years of peace! Baray District, Kampong Thom Province Organizes First Boat Race to Celebrate Pchum Ben
(Kampong Thom): Because the country is peaceful under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government has made the country developed in all fields and favored the people to work and live happily, especially the people have the opportunity to For family reunions, for example, now the Baray District Administration of Kampong Thom Province has organized the first flower boat race to celebrate Pchum Ben and for people to enjoy.
The event was held along the Chhouk Khsach canal in the O'Kach area with the participation of 15 flower boats and 172 athletes.
Speaking at the flower boat race, Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Governor of Baray District, said that this traditional Khmer Pchum Ben Festival is the first time that started from peace, development, especially in Baray district town in Kampong Thom province. Receive a large canal of the Royal Government to serve the interests of the people in both agriculture and tourism.
The district governor said that the boat race lasted for two days, on October 8 and 9, with the initiative of the people, youth in the commune, village chief, commune chief and the Baray district command forces to celebrate the festival. Pchum Ben, Khmer tradition and strengthen solidarity. It is also a new tourist destination in Baray district.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot added that next year, the ceremony will be more solemn because some communes want to participate, but they are not ready. Next year there will be more races than this year, with other boats and units coming to race.
The district governor thanked the people and philanthropists who have supported for the Water Flower Festival, now it is the participation of pure philanthropists, the coordination team of the commune and the forces.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mekong-Japan Leaders Start the 10th Summit
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Shinzo Abe, who hosted the meeting and was attended by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Dr. Thongloun Sisoulit, Prime Minister of Laos, Aung San Suu Kyi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs. Of the Union of Myanmar, Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha, Prime Minister of Thailand, Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, Prime Minister of Vietnam.
During the meeting, the "Japan-Mekong Regional Partnership Program" was announced, the first step towards the establishment of the first Mekong-Japan Foreign Ministers' Meeting in 2008 in Tokyo, Japan, Cambodia, Laos and Myanmar. Thailand, Vietnam are members.
Mekong-Japan cooperation aims to reduce the development gap among ASEAN member countries and promote ASEAN integration. The main goal of this cooperation is to achieve sustainable economic growth, taking into account the environment and health, as well as ensuring lasting peace and stability in the region.
