(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Planning and the United Nations Development Program in Cambodia on October 08, 2018 issued a joint official press release stating that the proportion of Cambodians living below the poverty line is 13. 5% calculated on the basis of consumption expenditure using the 2014 Cambodia Socio-Economic Survey data.
Ms. Da, a spokeswoman for the Ministry of Planning, told Fresh News that the release of the statement came after a meeting between Ms. Pauline Thames, Country Representative of the United Nations Development Program in Cambodia. And Senior Minister Chhay Thorn, Minister of Planning, on October 5, 2018, to clarify the poverty rate in Cambodia on the Phnom Penh Post.
The statement also said that Senior Minister Chhay Thorn and the UN Country Representative agreed that Cambodia has achieved great achievements in reducing poverty over the last two decades.
Both sides also added that the multi-component poverty assessment method has not yet been accepted by the Royal Government of Cambodia as the official method for assessing poverty in Cambodia, and that the United Nations Development Program in Cambodia has not been developed. This data as well.
In the future, the poverty rate in Cambodia, calculated from the concept of consumption expenditure using socio-economic survey data, will continue to be the official poverty figure of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
