(Tokyo, Japan): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has told Japanese businessmen that countries in the Mekong region, including Cambodia, Thailand, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam, have high investment potential. Cambodia is implementing many procedures for the benefit of investors.
The statement on the potential and attractiveness for investment in the Mekong region as well as Cambodia was made at a luncheon organized by the Japan-Mekong Business Group on October 9, 2018.
During the ceremony, Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that the Mekong is an area with strategic economic location and a combined gross domestic product (GDP) of about 800 billion US dollars and a total population of 240 million. The region is currently shifting its role as a strategic geography, a market and a major manufacturing hub.
"The Mekong countries have the potential to complement each other based on competitive advantage in the industrial production chain," Hun Sen said.
In order to attract Japanese businessmen to seek investment opportunities in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the potential and attention of the Royal Government to foreign investors. The Prime Minister stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia is always proactive in preparing and launching specific economic plans and policies that meet the specific needs of the private sector.
Samdech Techo stressed that the Royal Government is implementing a number of measures, including: Promoting trade facilitation by preparing to implement the OWSO, simplification and automation of customs procedures on both pricing and disclosure. Goods reduce fees, both formal and informal, and adjust institutions at international gates and international ports to facilitate and expedite exports and imports.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the Royal Government of Cambodia is paying attention and increasing investment in physical infrastructure by expanding all national roads to four lanes. In particular, national roads connecting to neighboring countries and are building deep-sea ports up to a depth of 14 meters, which can accommodate large cargo ships and the construction of expressways, which will be completed soon. Face.
In addition, the Royal Government has further reduced the price of electricity from 2019 onwards, as well as improving the stability of supply to improve investment attractiveness in the manufacturing industry.
Find out about: What is the procedure for withdrawal or suspension of the EU preferential system?
What are the procedures for withdrawing or suspending this preferential system?
The removal or suspension of the EU's preferential treatment differs from the economic sanctions, which are complicated procedures that must go through the decisions of the European Commission, the European Parliament and, in particular, the unanimous approval of the Council. Europe, represented by all 28 member states (27 after Brexit).
To officially begin the process of suspending the preferential treatment, the European Commission must issue a resolution and then notify the Parliament and the Council of Europe of the commencement of the proceedings, as well as to the countries where the suspension is to take place. This tax preference. The process takes a total of 12 months and is divided into two phases.
The European Commission then has to decide whether or not to suspend the preferential treatment, and this decision must be made by a majority vote of all 27 members of the European Commission.
In order to be able to oppose the commission's decision, the parliament needs an absolute majority, while the European Council needs a majority that obeys two conditions: 55% of the member states, and the supporting party must have a population. The combined population accounts for 65% of the EU's total population.
