The Prime Minister of Japan Shinzo Abe expressed his pleasure at welcoming Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Japan, which marks the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe has said that 25 years have passed since the UNTAC elections in Cambodia. Cambodia, which has inherited a negative legacy from the civil war, has struggled until it is on a path to real economic development. Abe once again paid tribute to the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Abe added that Japan has accompanied Cambodia and Japan expects Cambodia to further develop through the unity of the Cambodian people and continue to promote the democratic process. The Prime Minister of Japan is strongly committed to assisting in response to Samdech Techo's efforts with this goal.
The Prime Minister of Japan continued that 2019 is the year of Mekong-Japan based on the results of the meeting in Japan now, and he has the idea to expand bilateral relations between Cambodia and Japan by shaking hands with Samdech Techo Hun Sen. And work together to bring progress and prosperity to the entire Mekong region.
The following are the key statements made by the two top leaders at the press conference:
Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe
The Prime Minister of Japan expressed his pleasure at welcoming Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Japan, which marked the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
* The Prime Minister of Japan stated that 25 years have passed since the election in Cambodia was held by UNTAC (UNTAC). Cambodia, which has inherited a negative legacy from the war, has repeatedly struggled until there has been real economic development.
* Mr. Abe expressed his deep appreciation for the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which has made Cambodia's economy grow continuously.
Abe said Japan has accompanied Cambodia and Japan expects Cambodia to continue to grow with the democratic process and the unity of all its people. We agreed to continue cooperation on this goal.
* Prime Minister Abe stated that he is determined to cooperate with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who will lead the meeting tomorrow to a smooth success.
"We have agreed to continue to cooperate on important regional and global issues," he said.
* The Prime Minister of Japan stated that 2019 is the year of the Mekong-Japan, I plan to expand our bilateral relations by joining hands with Samdech Techo Hun Sen and working together to bring progress to the entire Mekong region.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia,
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his gratitude to Mr. Abe and was pleased to visit again with the 65th anniversary of Cambodia-Japan diplomacy. Samdech stated that it is very important.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Samdech and Abe had in-depth discussions on international relations, international issues and regional issues.
* The Prime Minister of Cambodia stated that he was pleased that Abe invited young people from various political parties from the Ministry of Justice to visit Japan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked Mr. Abe to continue to support the election in Cambodia, because the election does not end in 2018, we must follow the schedule.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to say that the process of registering to vote in Cambodia now is a continuation of the democratic process.
