The statement of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia was made during Samdech Techo's invitation to talk with Cambodian students and people living and studying in Japan on October 7, 2018.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that during the negotiation of the minimum wage for 2019, the employer agreed to increase the workers to only $ 177, and Samdech directly ordered the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training to demand an additional $ 5.
In response to this demand, the employer asked the Royal Government to reduce the price of electricity and the Royal Government also agreed. Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that "the Royal Government is willing to reduce the price of electricity to increase workers' wages to $ 182. Thus, the profit from electricity next year will be reduced because it will be given to the factory owner, the factory owner will open it to the workers. The real beneficiaries are the workers. ”
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also confirmed that whether the increase or decrease for the workers' wages is to increase every year.
It should be noted that the wages of workers in the garment and footwear sector have increased from just over $ 30 in 1997 to $ 170 in 2017. The wages of Cambodian workers are ahead of some countries in the region as well.
Currently, Cambodia has more than 10,000 registered garment and footwear enterprises and about 1 million workers working in this sector.
During the meeting, which was attended by about 350 Cambodian students studying and living in Japan, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded of the current information pollution on social media, including information related to Samdech. Samdech Prime Minister said that in the past, information was posted that Samdech was dead and that he had stolen Samdech's Facebook to control and post false information.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that there is currently no barrier to finding true information from Cambodia. In this sense, the head of the Royal Government wants Cambodian students and citizens in Japan to have a clear verification with the local news before they believe something posted on social media.
Regarding the issue of fake information, the Prime Minister also said that many countries in the world are currently fighting against fake information to make laws against this false information. In particular, France is one of the leading countries and has started to implement anti-fake news laws.
