Siem Reap Provincial Governor Leads Civil Servants to Hold the 13th Ben Ceremony at Wat Tang To, Angkor Thom Temple
(Siem Reap): Mr. Khim Bunsong, Governor of Siem Reap Province, and his wife and family and subordinates attended the Kan Ben Ceremony at Wat Tang To at Angkor Thom with Buddhists on October 7, 2018.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Khim Bunsong said that Pchum Ben is one of the big festivals of our Khmer national tradition that the Cambodian people celebrate without interruption every year from the 1st of Roch Sex until the 15th day of Roch. He added that now our Cambodian people are happy to do almsgiving in all seasons without restrictions, because our country is peaceful.
He also stated that at the end of the Pchum Ben season, the Cambodian Buddhists hold a Solidarity Kathina to collect donations for the monks to build achievements in the pagoda and also organize the Royal Water Festival. Also. On the other hand, our historical tourism province also organizes this Water Festival along the historical river of Siem Reap to serve the main tourism sector, national and international tourists who come to visit Siem Reap.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Japan has made unremitting contributions to the search for peace, rehabilitation and development of Cambodia
(Japan): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, stated that Japan has made unremitting contributions to the search for peace and the rehabilitation and development of Cambodia.
The Prime Minister said this during a working lunch with Ms. Fumiko Hayashi, Mayor of Yokohama on October 7, 2018.
During the working dinner, the Mayor warmly welcomed the presence of Samdech Techo and the delegation selected for Yokohama for an official visit before Samdech and four other Mekong leaders attend the Mekong Summit. The 10th Japan will be held on October 9.
On that occasion, the Mayor highlighted the excellent relations between Japan and Cambodia. She mentioned that Yokohama, especially Yokohama International Port, has strong cooperation with the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port. She also reminded that 2018 is the 65th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan, and for the past 65 years, Cambodia and Japan have always helped each other in the interests of both countries.
The Prime Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the leaders of Yokohama City for hosting and having a working lunch for Samdech and the delegation. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded of the role and important contribution of Japan in finding peace, restoring and developing Cambodia after recovering from the flames of war.
In terms of economic and trade relations, Japan imported to Cambodia in 2011 amounting to 307 million 69 thousand US dollars, in 2012 amounting to 602 million 74 thousand US dollars and in the first six months of 2013 amounting to 85 million 17 thousand US dollars. America. Meanwhile, exports from Cambodia to Japan in 2011 amounted to 204 million 87 thousand dollars, in 2012 amounted to 197.7 million dollars and in the first six months of 2013 amounted to 129 million 70 thousand US dollars.
In terms of tourism, the number of Japanese tourists visiting Cambodia has also increased. In 2012, there were 179,327 Japanese tourists to Cambodia, ranking sixth, and in the first nine months of 2013, there were 150,347 Japanese tourists to Cambodia, an increase of 15 , 3% compared to the same period in 2013, which is still the sixth largest number of foreign tourists visiting Cambodia.
In rebuilding and developing Cambodia, Japan has contributed the largest amount of grants to help rebuild Cambodia. In 2012-2013, Japan provided 112.4 million US dollars in grants for human resource development, health, flood disaster, small hydropower plant, education, water supply and sweeping program. Clear mines.
On the close relationship and cooperation between the two sides, Cambodia and Japan have signed a number of important agreements, including the Technical Cooperation Agreement signed in 2003, the Agreement on Liberalization, Promotion and Investment Protection signed in 2007 Agreement on Cooperation in the Field of Education and Training within the United Nations Peacekeeping Operations Framework, signed in 2013.
