To help reduce people's expenses when visiting their hometowns on the occasion of Pchum Ben, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has ordered Phnom Penh Capital Hall to release buses to transport people to their hometowns free of charge. Phnom Penh Capital Hall has arranged up to 120 vehicles deployed at various destinations in Phnom Penh to transport people to all provinces along the national road from October 6 to 11.
Through the buses of Phnom Penh Capital Hall, it is observed that many people have stopped to take these buses to visit their hometowns. Preventing the use of this car because it has helped them reduce the cost of car tickets to spend on other occasions during Pchum Ben.
People in remote provinces such as Battambang and Banteay Meanchey, they have to pay at least 30,000 to 50,000 riel for a car ticket, and if there are 3 to 4 people, it costs up to more than 100,000 riel. Therefore, the release of Phnom Penh Capital Hall's car to transport them to their hometown has saved them a lot of money.
People who came to use Phnom Penh Capital Hall to their hometowns were happy and thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for initiating this free transportation program. The people consider this gesture as a high attention to the lives of the people from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
