(Kandal): Oknha Try Pheap, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, spent a total of 200 million Riels, equivalent to about 50,000 US dollars, as an incentive for students to pass and fail in 2018. The award ceremony for students who participated in the 2018 bankruptcy exam in Kandal Stung district, Kandal province was held on October 6, 2018.
On the occasion of awarding prizes to the students who passed the exam as well as the failed exam, Tycoon Try Pheap expressed his happiness and pride to the children of the people of Kandal Stung district who worked hard to study until they passed the exam at a high rate. However, the tycoon regretted that students in Kandal Stung district could not get an A grade this year.
Tycoon Try Pheap also reminded all failed students to continue their efforts in higher education to absorb knowledge as capital for life, contribute to the development of their hometown, as well as contribute to the development of the Royal Government. Cambodia to grow even more.
Drugs are a social poison and a serious threat to human resources in Cambodian society today. Tycoon Try Pheap reminded students who failed the exam and had to continue their studies in Phnom Penh to be very careful not to let their friends entice them to use drugs to ruin their future.
For those who failed the exam, the tycoon encouraged them to continue their efforts, not to be discouraged and drop out of school. The tycoon reminded them that failure is common in the lives of people, whether academics or business people, but the important thing is to know how to build their failures to the light of success.
In this regard, Tycoon Try Pheap warned students to fail this year that if they do not go to study for an associate's degree or learn any other technical skills and must continue to study 12th grade to prepare for the exam in 2019, must strive to study from the beginning of the year Go. The tycoon expressed confidence that if they study hard, they will be successful, especially do not spend too much time with Facebook.
The tycoon also reminded teachers to make efforts to train students to excel in A to honor teachers as well as the people of Kandal Stung district as a whole.
On that occasion, Mr. Oknha also reminded of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's efforts to develop the education sector by increasing teachers' salaries and building schools. Mr. Oknha emphasized that the new government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to consider training as the main work for building human resources in the development of the country to grow.
The students who were stuck in the bankruptcy were very happy and satisfied with the gesture of Duke Try Pheap. They mentioned that the Duke Try Pheap Award was an additional incentive for their studies.
In addition to supporting students, the tycoon also provided an incentive of 92 riels to 92 teachers.
In front of the students, teachers and the people of Kandal Stung district, Mr. Oknha promised to bring the prizes to the students in Kandal Stung district every year and if they get A grade, they will also distribute motorcycles. He said that these gifts are part of the motivation and for them to use in further study.
