The Royal Government has continued to implement the policy of providing opportunities for people to find satisfactory jobs abroad, especially Cambodian workers in Thailand who have found legal employment, struggling to provide income, providing families with outstanding Cambodian citizens who are patriotic. Homeland through work, relatives send back a total of about 2 billion dollars a year, which also contributes significantly to the development of the national economy.
He added that in order to protect Cambodia's jobs and incomes and to continue the cooperation in the field of labor and labor between the two countries, four years ago, Cambodia and Thailand have succeeded in resolving labor issues, especially the provision of legitimacy. To more than half a million people, so far, 1.8 million people in Thailand are all legal.
On this occasion, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, also called on people to live and work respecting the law, maintaining Khmer-Khmer solidarity between Khmer and Thai, living happily in the community and in the workplace, taking into account issues. Health first and take time to visit hometown during festivals and holidays as well.
