The Sambor Prei Kuk temple site is located in Sambo village, Sambo commune, Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province. It can be said that the Sambor Prei Kuk temple area is located in the center of Cambodia.
The Sambor Prei Kuk temple site, the Khmer capital of the Chenla period, is called "Isanpura", meaning the city of Isu or Shiva, which was built in the late 6th and early 7th centuries AD, during the reign. Isanvarman I to dedicate to Shiva or Iso, because at that time the capital of Isanpura was also a major center of Brahmanism in Southeast Asia.
The Sambor Prei Kuk site resort is divided into four main groups: the northern group, the central group, the southern group, and the Kraol Romeas group, each of which is built of solid brick and laterite in the form of design. League.
After being inscribed on the World Heritage List, this historic cultural site has flourished with tens of thousands of visitors. In that, Mr. Seng An, Director of the Department of Tourism of Kampong Thom Province, said that the Sambor Prei Kuk temple area is becoming more and more known and visited more and more. Interpol arrested and interrogated by Chinese authorities while no news has been released!
