(China): Chinese tech companies are finding ways to expand the growing livestock sector in the country. At the same time, farmers need to buy more pet food and the market for this sector is constantly evolving.
As urbanization is accelerating, livestock and pet-related industries are growing in more and more areas with the same number of livestock.
People in China are starting to raise animals, and their owners are increasingly concerned about the health, well-being and safety of their pets, which makes smart animal husbandry technology in high demand.
PETKIT has launched an intelligent pet product that allows both owners and animals to enjoy the benefits of technology.
"We are currently looking for ways to make animal husbandry easier and to help pet owners spend less time with their pets Spend more time playing with your pets. Therefore, the company focuses on the development of automatic feeders and health control products.
He added that China is the latest country in the livestock industry compared to the United States, Europe and other developed countries. "When I was young, I used to think of this industry as a small market, but after getting involved in this field, I see that many young people today have a different perspective and ideas," he said. I am completely alone.
The rapid development of the pet sector not only provides an opportunity for pet technology to grow, but also helps pet supplies stores to grow and develop as well.
Petsknow is a pet technology company in Beijing that provides business management services to pet stores using an integrated online business management system and helps connect them to the Internet.
Italy's new Chinese business entity has opened its first meeting, aiming to nominate Italy as a "privileged partner" in China's One Belt One Road initiative.
The Chinese business entity was recently announced in August 2018. Italy set up the unit to boost its economic ties with China.
The first meeting of the group highlighted Italy's efforts to expand bilateral cooperation with China in trade, business and investment.
The Deputy Minister of Economic Development of Italy, Michel Chirasi, presided over the opening ceremony, which was attended by more than 300 people from political institutions, companies, universities and the press.
Chinese Ambassador to Italy Li Ruoyu praised the Italian government's focus on strengthening ties with China.
He said that in terms of expanding bilateral ties on economic and cultural ties, it was a difficult task for the two countries due to differing views at the grassroots level. This is the first time that China has set up a business unit.
He added that the Chinese business community has pointed out that Italy has developed a special system for dealing with various countries using a number of relevant government institutions. He expects Chinese businesses to act as a way to build mutual trust and give Italy easier access to China's food market.
It should be noted that more and more Chinese people are now consuming high quality products, and this is a great opportunity for Italy to attract business people to invest and export many products such as Italian food, machinery and clothing. (China CCTV) What is the Mekong-Japan Cooperation to be Held in Japan This Weekend?
