Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on October 5: 1,175 Illegal Vehicles Found and 833 Fined
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for October 05, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 5,117 vehicles and found 1,175 vehicles violating the law (81% motorcycles), 342 education vehicles and park 833 fines, according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 2,486 helmets and goggles were inspected on October 5, 106 education helmets and 297 glasses were fined.
Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will lead a high-level delegation to attend the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit in Tokyo, Japan.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will lead a high-level Cambodian delegation to attend the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit in Tokyo on the morning of October 6, 2018. Invitation of the Government of Japan.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit will be held from October 6 to 10, 2018. Accompanying Samdech Techo Hun Sen were Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs, as well as senior government officials and business leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
