(Phnom Penh): The Public Financial Management Reform Steering Committee held a meeting on "Monitoring the Progress and Evaluating the Implementation of the Implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase 3, Quarter 1 and 2 2018 ”at the Ministry of Economy and Finance on October 4, 2018.
Also present were the leaders and members of the Public Financial Management Reform Working Group of the Ministries and Institutions, the Secretariat of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development, and the Secretariat of the Public Administration Reform Committee. , Representatives of development partners and representatives of non-governmental organizations, a total of about 250 people.
The meeting on "Monitoring the Progress and Evaluating the Implementation of the Implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase 3, 1st and 2nd Quarter 2018" is the first meeting for the 6th legislature of National Assembly to monitor the progress and evaluate the achievements of the implementation of the public financial management reform program.
Overall, the main achievements in the first and second quarters of 2018 include:
* (Overall revenue is better, as national revenue declines slightly and sub-national revenue increases due to some tax transfers from national to sub-national, such as property and property taxes). In a situation where the target can be achieved is 40%.
This result can be concluded that the cash situation is more reliable and there is no debt congestion in the National Treasury (60 days from the payment term entered the National Treasury until the payment date). The core mechanism of financial accountability is also Progress has also been made, with 10 ministries and 25 additional Departments of Economy and Finance announcing the implementation of the FMIS project and receiving FMIS awareness raising.
As of the first half, 911 budget units and 39 ministries and institutions have been prepared for implementation. At the same time, seven budget categories have been implemented in the FMIS system.
The preparation and negotiation of the budget has been strengthened and improved to a higher level, better reflecting the main priorities of the ministries and institutions to achieve the objectives and policies of the Royal Government.
Taking this opportunity, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth highly appreciated and thanked the efforts of the Public Financial Management Reform Steering Committee, as well as all ministries and institutions that have participated in the implementation of the reform program in the past. Achieve this great achievement.
