Industrial towers are a collection of local factories that provide easy access to industry and interconnection, and do not allow those factories to relocate to other countries.
As of now, there are 19 special economic zones in Cambodia that are producing and exporting products, including 377 factories, creating 114,173 jobs for Cambodians. Of the nearly 400 factories, 90 are from Japan operating in the SEZ.
"Apart from diversifying the local economy , we have also diversified sources of investment capital," he said. Cambodia has a special economic zone with investment from all over Hong Kong, Singapore, China, Malaysia, etc. "More from Asia than from Europe, until we have a special economic zone, Japanese companies come to invest in factories in special economic zones, so far Japanese factories in special economic zones up to 90 factories."
