Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Lead a High-Level Delegation to the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit for 4 Days from October 6-10 in Tokyo, Japan
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will lead a high-level Cambodian delegation to attend the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit from October 6 to 10, 2018 in Tokyo, Japan. Invitation of the Government of Japan. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on October 5.
Accompanying Samdech Techo Hun Sen were Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs, as well as senior government officials and business leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
Leaders of the Mekong-Japan Summit will bow to the Emperor of Japan
The 10th Mekong-Japan Summit will discuss and adopt a new Tokyo strategy aimed at improving connectivity, promoting people's well-being and protecting the environment. The strategy focuses on sustainable development and bridging the development gap between the Mekong and other ASEAN members.
The Prime Minister will deliver a speech focusing on the future direction of Mekong-Japan cooperation.
Mekong leaders will have a working breakfast hosted by the Japan-Mekong Parliamentary Friendship Association, a working lunch hosted by a business group and participate in a Japan-Mekong Investment Forum organized by the Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO). Samdech Techo will highlight the key to attracting Japanese investors to do business in the Mekong region.
On the sidelines of the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit, the Prime Minister will hold bilateral talks with HE Shinzo Abe, Prime Minister of Japan on various issues of common concern of bilateral, regional and international cooperation. The two prime ministers will then hold a joint press conference.
The Prime Minister will also take the opportunity to meet with the Cambodian community and students living and studying in Japan.
