The Secretary of State continued that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has transformed from a war-torn country and a killing field into a country of peace, stability and development to become a world-class tourist destination with warmth. With millions of national and international tourists visiting each year.
In the above meeting, the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism also presented a lot of experience and information related to tourism to the delegation of Southeast Asian youth in Cambodia, especially many important tourist destinations in Cambodia, including articles Pictures, videos, music files, tours, as well as a lot of relevant content to share with friends from other countries on the ship and discuss and exchange experiences.
Please be informed that the 45th Southeast Asian and Japan Youth Ship Program 2018, the youth group will leave the ship from Japan to Brunei, Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam. A total of 330 ASEAN and Japanese youths will first meet in Tokyo, Japan to attend the official opening ceremony. Ministry of Interior Receives New Complaints and Evidence from Former Members of the Khmer Rouge Party on Party Claims
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of October 4, 2018, the Ministry of Interior met and received complaints, including additional new evidence from the founding members, members of the Political Council and members of the Board of Directors representing the capital-province of the relevant Khmer Rouge party. And the claim to take back the Khmer Rouge party from Mr. Suong Sophorn.
The meeting was held at the Ministry of Interior with the composition of the former Khmer Rouge party led by Mr. Tep Virak, Mr. Pen Sap and Mr. Mak Ratana. The composition of the Ministry of Interior is led by Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, Director General of Administration of the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. Pen Sap, Vice President of the Khmer Rouge Party, confirmed that the Ministry of Interior has not yet decided which party will be the winner to control the ruling Khmer Rouge Party. Mr. Suong Sophoan.
Mr. Pen Sap said: "The Ministry of Interior has not decided yet, he is working and also decided that this party went to who or who is wrong, who is right? The Ministry of Interior is But work. "The Ministry of Interior will act according to our additional complaints filed by the Ministry of Interior and will continue to review the evidence with the minutes of the meeting with all the political councils that attended," he said.
However, Mr. Pen Sap continued that there was nothing wrong with the founding members of the former Khmer Rouge party, it was Mr. Suong Sophoan who stole the party to steal the party they tried to build from scratch. Alone, they can not get these.
He confirmed that the Ministry of Interior has received new evidence and is conducting an autopsy on the letter that Mr. Sophoan's group held a congress to submit to the Ministry of Interior.
It should be noted that on September 14, Mr. Pen Sap wrote a letter to Samdech Chakra Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, requesting that Mr. Suong Sophorn be summoned for questioning, alleging that Mr. Suong Sophorn falsified the report. That he resigned.
He considered that the writing of Mr. Suong Sophorn's report to the Ministry of Interior about the Congress and the resignation of the Vice President of this party is a lie of the Ministry of Interior, falsifying documents and using fake documents to become party president and form separatist factions. In the party, it is different from the original statute of the Khmer Rouge party.
Separately, Mr. Suon Serey Ratha, former President of the Khmer Rouge Party, also accused Mr. Suong Sophoan of forging a letter and forcing party members to sign and acknowledge this letter to control the entire Khmer Rouge Party. Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth chaired the meeting. Economic and Financial Policy Committee
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, and Chairman of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee (NRPC) this morning (October 3, 2018) chaired a meeting. With the participation of senior leaders and technical officers of relevant ministries and institutions to discuss the main agenda, such as:
1: Review and develop incentives for solid waste recycling and waste disposal projects, and request for technical support and micro-credit to local communities to:
* In line with population growth and increasing daily needs of the population, solid waste and garbage increase day by day. In 2017, it is estimated that throughout Cambodia, the amount of urban solid waste generated was about 3.65 million tons per year, or more than 10,000 tons per day, of which 3,000 tons in Phnom Penh. In one day.
* Along with the collection, processing, and storage of garbage is limited, as well as the lack of landfills in urban areas, especially the participation of all stakeholders is limited, waste management and solid waste in the area. Citizens have not yet fully responded to the actual situation.
The meeting agreed that solid waste processing and management requires a comprehensive package management mechanism, taking into account the major principles, including: waste storage, collection and recycling, which is required. Legal framework, legal documents, policy framework, measures and action plans.
The meeting requested the Ministry of Environment to cooperate with the relevant ministries and institutions to review the policy framework, legal framework and relevant documents in force, prepare a package of measures and practical action plans to be submitted to the meeting. Review and discuss again in the first quarter of 2019.
At the same time, the income from each community in the provinces, cities, districts and Khans can be used to develop the locality itself.
2: Promoting the implementation of key measures related to the economic and financial sectors set out in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4.
3. The Economic and Monetary Policy Committee plays an important role in monitoring and evaluating the implementation of key measures related to the economic and financial sectors, which have been outlined in the recent "Rectangular Strategy Phase 4".
In this regard, the meeting decided to have a working group with the participation of direct input from ministries and institutions to implement, set out key indicators, measure the achievements of a specific implementation time to set out measures to address the challenges. Period of regular review meetings every year and mid-term.
3: Discuss on the draft framework for the Sustainable Development Goals of Cambodia 2016-2030:
* The meeting continued to review and discuss the document of the Cambodian Sustainable Development Framework 2016-2030, which was submitted to the NEC in the past.
