(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on October 4, 2018, issued an official announcement on the participation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in the 73rd Session of the General Assembly. United Nations in New York, USA.
As the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia of the Sixth Mandate, Samdech Techo Hun Sen addressed the General Assembly, highlighting Cambodia's new face in the process of democratic stability and remarkable socio-economic achievements. After achieving complete peace and stability throughout the country.
The Prime Minister highlighted the Royal Government's commitment to continue to improve the well-being of the people in line with the "Sustainable Development Goals of Cambodia" which will be adopted in the near future.
Regarding international affairs, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed concern over the threat of unilateralism, which has undermined the multilateral system and hampered global efforts to achieve sustainable development goals and Address climate change and other common security challenges.
The head of the Royal Government called for respect for the UN Charter and for avoiding interference in internal affairs under the pretext of protecting political rights. The case of Cambodia, where some outsiders still nurture their ambitions, interfere in Cambodia's internal affairs and ignore the quality and integrity of the Cambodian electoral process by issuing statements against or attacking the results. Of the election.
Please read the full text of the Foreign Ministry's press release below: Today! Russey Keo Police Crack Down on Drug Trafficking Suspect and Seize 17 Packets
(Phnom Penh): After completing the investigation, Russey Keo district police raided and arrested a suspect on drug trafficking charges, confiscating 17 packages of drugs, including a large package at Group 1, Village 1. Sangkat Chrang Chamres 1, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh. This was confirmed by Colonel Koul Yi, District Police Inspector on October 4, 2018.
According to the Russey Keo District Police Inspector, the suspect who was arrested in the drug trafficking case was named Chang Tai Leang, male, 24 years old, Khmer nationality, false occupation, living in Ta Prum Village, Kom Pong Os Commune, Punh Leu District, Kandal Province.
According to the Russey Keo District Police Inspector, prior to the crackdown on the drug trafficking suspects, the district police force cooperated with the police force to determine the location and time of the arrest. During the operation, 17 packages of suspected drugs were confiscated, including 1 large bag, and the suspects were also detained.
The district inspector said that after the arrest, the suspect, along with the exhibits, was brought to the district police inspectorate for questioning in order to build a case and send it to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for processing. Minister Vong Soth: Peaceful country, Cambodian people have full freedom of religion
Mr. Vong Soth's remarks were made while he and she and the leaders of the Ministry of Social Affairs attended the 10th Ben Ceremony at Wat Tuol Keo Ampok, also known as Wat Kirinaram, in Ampok Village, Krek Commune, Ponhea Krek District, Tbong Khmum Province on the morning of the 4th. This October 2018.
Speaking on that occasion, Minister Vong Soth said that the holding of Pchum Ben is a tradition from Khmer ancestors and the purpose of Pchum Ben is to allow all monks to remember the rain in the temple. In other words, to commemorate the souls of ancestors who passed away to the next world.
The Minister continued that the merits performed on the 10th Ben Day contributed to the merits of the merits as well as dedicated to the souls of patriots of all generations who sacrificed their lives for the cause of defending and building the motherland and people. Let the souls of those born in hell not be wasted.
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, this morning, October 4, 2018, accompanied by Mr. Huot Wutty, Prosecutor of Kampong Cham Provincial Court, disseminated the effects of drug accidents to the suspects as drivers. 18 truck drivers and truck workers arrested on October 2, 2018 in Kampong Siem district.
Speaking on that occasion, the Governor of Kampong Cham Province told the authorities to take legal action against the above suspects and asked the traffic experts to check the relevant documents for the vehicles that were detained and fined.
In addition, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun advised the specialized police force to continue to carry out the campaign to test the water for drugs on the driver of the truck 3 to 4 times a month.
Please be informed that the Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Kampong Cham Provincial Drug Control Committee, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, has strictly ordered the provincial police to launch a large-scale drug inspection operation on the drivers of trucks passing through the base. Kampong Cham Province.
In fact, after this order, on October 2, 2018, Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Em Kosal, assigned Brigadier General Ith Dara, Deputy Commissioner for Anti-Crime Work, to lead the Anti-Drug Bureau, Road Traffic Bureau and Kampong Siem District Police Inspectorate inspected, inspected and tested water for drugs on the driver of a large truck at Trakoun village, Krala commune, Kampong Siem district.
For the full day operation, the specialized police force called 106 trucks to inspect and tested the water for a total of 203 people (68 in the province, 135 outside the province), including 106 drivers. 96 truck drivers and one worker.
As a result, 18 people were found to be in possession of drugs, including nine drivers, eight truck drivers and one worker. Separately, 9 large trucks were temporarily stored at the police station in Kampong Siem district.
Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Camcontrol Branch Continues to Search for Defective Goods at Teuk Thla Market, But No Defective Products Found
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of Pchum Ben Festival and to ensure the well-being and protect the interests of the people on October 4, 2018, CamControl Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Branch in cooperation with the Department of Commerce and the Teuk Thla Market Commission in Sangkat Teuk Thla Khan Sen Sok continued to disseminate food quality, safety and inspection of pre-packaged food and 21 samples of daily food.
As a result, all 21 samples inspected were found to be in compliance with safety standards, and no defects were found in the pre-packaged products, according to CamControl.
During the inspection of the quality of goods, Camcontrol Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Branch also educated, introduced and disseminated by distributing posters to traders and customers as consumers.
CamControl officers also instructed all vendors on hygiene and how to properly display the goods in accordance with each type of goods to avoid bacterial contamination, and advised the vendors in the market. And at home to help inspect the goods themselves for the expiration date of the goods and prohibit the display of goods that have expired.
