October salary and Pchum Ben allowance of 50,000 Riels for civil servants have already been transferred to the personal accounts of both national and sub-national administrations!
(Phnom Penh): As of October 4, 2018, the General Department of National Treasury has completed the transfer of salary for October 2018 and Pchum Ben allowance (50,000 Riels) into the personal account of each officer of All national administrations (ministries, institutions and central units) are fully accounted for by the sub-national administrative agents (capitals and provinces).
Through its official Facebook page, the General Department of the National Treasury has also confirmed that in case civil servants still do not see the cash in their bank accounts, please contact the opening agent of the relevant unit.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, recently issued a sub-decree on the provision of salaries in October and November and allowances on the occasion of Pchum Ben for 2018 to all civil servants.
The sub-decree stipulates that ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations must pay the October salaries, salaries and allowances of civil servants, staff, armed forces, retirees, council members and other officials in the first week of October. And November to be completed in the second week of November 2018.
It should be noted that the Royal Government will spend more than 7 million US dollars, with each civil servant receiving 50,000 riels on the occasion of Pchum Ben. Health Minister Urges Doctors to Continue Paying Attention to Patients, Especially the Elderly
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bun Heng, urged doctors across the country to continue to pay high attention to the treatment of patients, especially to improve the well-being of the elderly because the elderly. More prone to depression and depression than other ages.
The Minister said this on the occasion of the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly on October 1 under the theme "The Association of the Elderly is an important mechanism to preserve the culture, family and society" held on October 4, 2018. This is at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital.
"As a doctor, we must adhere to our profession, our knowledge, our skills, our ethics, especially to be united and take care of patients like our family members," he said. Incentive care is an important part that people need as a first step.
In addition, in order to pay more attention to the elderly in Cambodia, the Royal Government has established the Cambodian National Committee for the Elderly, carrying out its roles and responsibilities, including: formulating policies to improve the well-being of the elderly and organizing days. Older people in Cambodia by setting October 1 every year.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, pays attention to the Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly, which is a day to commemorate the merits of the elderly and the day of the elderly. Old Cambodia, ancestors, grandparents, parents, Oum Puming, who built and left a precious legacy for this generation and future generations.
Minister of Labor recommends Southeast Asian youth to study the progress of each country in order to apply good experiences in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of meeting with a delegation of 29 Southeast Asian youth from Cambodia at the Ministry of Labor this morning, October 4, 2018, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, made many good recommendations to young people. The above aims to encourage them to study the progress of each country to bring good experiences to participate in the development of their country.
The Minister advised that Cambodian youth should strive to learn more about general knowledge related to regional and international institutions to which Cambodia is a member, including ASEAN, the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly and other international organizations, as well as the benefits of cooperation. Operating with those organizations for Cambodia.
Mr. Hor Samnang, Acting President of the Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association of Cambodia, said that all youth delegations are working hard to learn and strengthen friendships, share the culture of each country to help society.
He said that during the 52 days, the Southeast Asian Youth Ship Program, which includes young people from ASEAN countries and Japan, which is the creator of the program, will travel by ship from Japan through Brunei, the Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam. .
Please note that the Southeast Asia-Japan Youth Ship Program was established by Japan in 1974. The Association of Southeast Asian Youth Ships Cambodia was established in 2004, which so far has 560 young Cambodians and has participated in the Southeast Asian Youth Ships - Japan.
