Officials strictly forbid the sale of expired goods after finding more than 100 cans / bottle of defective drinks at Chi Paing Market and Dar Market in Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province
The above transaction took place on the morning of October 4, 2018, led by Mr. Meas Mora, Head of Camcontrol Branch, Tbong Khmum Province, inspecting the signs, usage dates and sales of vendors in accordance with the technical specifications.
Mr. Meas Mora said that under the guidance of the General Department of CamControl, all CamControl branches across the country have implemented their action plans to ensure food safety and health for consumers, especially during the Pchum Ben festival. He, along with provincial CamControl officers and relevant authorities, regularly inspects.
The head of CamControl branch educated and advised the traders before selling the goods to check and know the source clearly and put up for sale good quality goods with the right label. He strictly forbids the sale of any goods that do not have a specific date, especially after the expiration date, which is different from the provisions of the law to put up for sale.
At the same time, CamControl officials posted a poster explaining how to choose food that is safe for people to eat. Workers' minimum wage for 2019 will be officially decided tomorrow afternoon, employers dare $ 177 while unions down to $ 182
(Phnom Penh): The working group to discuss the wages of garment and footwear workers this morning, October 4, 2018, continued the fourth meeting at the Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Som Oun, a member of the Tripartite Minimum Wage Negotiation Task Force who attended the meeting, said that the result of today's meeting was that the employers (factory owners) had reached $ 177. Reduced to $ 182. The tripartite meeting decided to vote on one of the two figures.
He said that the result of the election was overwhelmingly in favor of the figure of 177 US dollars to submit the last meeting of the Labor Advisory Committee on October 5, 2018 at 2:00 pm tomorrow. Therefore, the minimum wage for workers in 2019 will be officially announced before the upcoming Pchum Ben season.
Mr. Som Oun added that the mechanism for raising Cambodia's minimum wage has matured and has a clear formula and the right principles have facilitated the smooth running of the talks.
He also cited research data from Vietnam, which has divided the minimum wage of workers into four regions. He said that in 2018, in Vietnam, the minimum wage in the first region will be 171 US dollars, and in 2019, Vietnam plans to increase the minimum wage by 5.3%. Therefore, the minimum wage in Vietnam for 2019 will be increased to 181 US dollars.
Mr. Som Oun emphasized that the unions have always wanted higher wages, but also to compete with other countries in the region to maintain investment and maintain job security. He hopes that the current wage increase will be welcomed by all parties involved.
