(Phnom Penh): Cellcard, with Duke Kith Meng as Chairman of the Royal Group, has organized a special conference for the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on the success of its 5G test in China and will bring the 5G technology. Coming to Cambodia soon.
The ceremony was held at Cambodiana Hotel, Phnom Penh on the afternoon of October 3, 2018 with the participation of Mr. Sok Puthyvuth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, Mr. Chea Manit, Undersecretary of State and Director of the Cabinet of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, Mr. Mov Chakriya is the President of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia and other senior officials as well as the management of the leading mobile phone company Cellcard.
There will also be a presentation of the Royal Group's vision for Cambodia to become one of the leading digital economies in Southeast Asia, and the results of 5G testing conducted in China. Last week. Key cases using 5G in Cambodia will also be shared.
Speaking at the event, Mr. Sok Puthyvuth also expressed his support for the 5G technology to be implemented in Cambodia with quality, along with achieving the best results for the people of Cambodia, as well as growth in the sector. This as a whole, as well as Cellcard's vision and plans for 5G technology.
With this new 5G technology, it can be at the forefront of providing the latest technology in the telecommunications sector, and Cellcard has shown that it is ready to lead this change and bring Cambodia to the forefront. Digital resources are more useful and easier to access the internet faster than ever before.
Mr. Sok Puthyvuth stated that all enterprises can lead without limit with this new 5G technology. 5G technology can improve lives, create jobs and boost the economy to a digital economy.
Congratulations! Cambodian students win 2nd and 3rd place in Asia-Pacific Entrepreneurship Project
About 20 groups of candidates from four countries in the region, including Vietnam, Laos, Thailand and Cambodia. From the qualifiers in August to the finals in late September, there are currently only five teams left to compete on general knowledge and defend their respective projects in French.
In this final, there are 3 teams from Vietnam and 2 teams from Cambodia to win the regional championship. The second and third place winners in the region are all students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, Department of French, 3rd and 4th year. Separately, the second winner is the one who studied in two colleges, the Faculty of French and the Faculty of Health Sciences in the third year.
Similarly, Duong Po Huot expressed his happiness and pride that he was very excited, did not expect to reach the final stage, and he did not expect to get results like this. On the other hand, studying in the third year, going abroad to compete, is very proud, both for himself and for his family, especially for standing on the international stage to represent Cambodia.
This is the second time that a local university has organized a competition for creative projects under the auspices of the AUF Asia-Pacific Agency for Higher Education in Asia-Pacific with the aim of encouraging young people to be creative in Creating entrepreneurship projects in response to the realities of Asia's growing economy.
The Asia-Pacific Higher Education Agency (AUF) project in the Asia-Pacific region encourages member universities in the region to hold this annual Volunteer Entrepreneurship Competition to encourage students to study. At universities that study in French to be creative, innovative, courageous and able to defend their projects through the use of French language skills.
Chan Sereyvath also pointed out that if there is a next competition, even if he does not participate, he will encourage Cambodian students to participate in the competition to gain experience and get information, as well as build relationships with friends in the region through French. To develop oneself.
The Ministry of Health stressed that "the selection exam was attended by the Ministry of Public Works and the Observatory of the Anti-Corruption Unit. "In order to avoid rumors that undermine the honor and dignity of the Ministry, please solemnly declare that the bribe-taker and the bribe-taker must be punished equally."
The Ministry of Health also advises all candidates to study hard and strengthen their capacity to compete fairly and fairly, not to take bribes or commit other corrupt acts. In case of the above inactivity, please complain to the Anti-Corruption Unit with concrete evidence or to the Ministry of Health to take legal action.
Kratie Municipality Authority Organizes Order at Samaki Market and in Kratie City
(Kratie): Kratie City Authority, led by Mr. Seng Pina, Deputy Governor of Kratie City, on October 3, 2018, yesterday organized order and road marking at Samaki Market, Kratie City and around the market.
Mr. Seng Pina said that the participating forces include: City Hall, Municipal Armed Forces, Police, Provincial Police Office, Provincial Public Works and Transport Department, Sangkat Force, Village Chief, and Village Defenders.
The Deputy Governor continued that the implementation of this authority has the following five principles:
First, mark the road of Samaki Market, Kratie City and the area around the market.
Second: Introduce traders according to the regulations of the municipal authorities that have been marked.
Third: Introduce parking of motorcycles on public roads in good order to avoid traffic jams.
Fourth, if any person does not comply with the authorities, he will take action and fine as a model for the next generation.
Fifth, the authorities continue to maintain order forever so that this tiny city has a beautiful and clean environment to attract national and international tourists.
