(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, and Ms. Chea Sina Khuong Sreng, together with officials under the supervision of Phnom Penh Capital Administration, on the morning of October 4, 2018, attended the 10th Ben Ceremony at Wat Moni Prasit Vong, also known as Wat Samdech. Muong Ra is located in Sangkat Prek Phnov, Khan Prek Phnov.
The ceremony is held in accordance with the Buddhist tradition by offering food to monks to dedicate merits to the ancestors who have passed away to the next world and to collect some suffixes to build a pagoda for development. At the same time, Cambodia as a whole is growing rapidly. During the ceremony, Mr. Khuong Sreng and Ms. Chea Sina Khuong Sreng donated 12 million 470,000 Riels to the monks to build a pagoda.
It should be reminded that Pchum Ben is celebrated by Khmer Buddhists every year from the 1st of Roach to the 15th of Roach. Khmer Buddhists celebrate this festival by bringing various gifts such as food to supply the monks in the pagoda who are waiting for the rain for only 15 days.
As Buddhists are busy with daily chores and to ensure that monks are regularly supplied, they take turns to give alms to the monks for 14 days from the 1st of Roach to the 14th of Roach. Sex and name it the first shift until the 14th shift. These 14 days are called Bon Kan Ben or Bon Dak Ben.
As for the 15th day of Roch, which is the last day, Buddhists from all shifts come together to give alms to the monks together to end the Kan Ben festival called Pchum Ben or Pchum Ben Day. Battambang Provincial Governor Meets and Distributes Budget to 58 Urban Gardening Workers
