Cambodia, Vietnam agree to crack down on tax evasion and transnational crime
(Svay Rieng): The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia and the General Department of Customs of Vietnam on October 2, 2018 held the third bilateral meeting on border customs to further strengthen cooperation and mutual assistance on customs. In particular, the work of cracking down on tax evasion, transnational crime, promoting trade facilitation, especially transit goods, and updating cooperation between the two customs administrations.
The meeting was held at the Customs and Excise Office of Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province, led by Mr. Keut Sotheara, Director of the Department of Crime Prevention and Suppression of the General Department of Customs and Excise.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed and agreed in principle on key points, such as reorganizing liaison officers in charge of exchanging information from national to local levels related to the fight against tax evasion and transnational crime through mechanisms. One that ensures fast, timely, accurate and highly confidential communication.
At the same time, the two sides will examine the possibility of exchanging specific statistical data on exports and imports, including transit goods from third countries, in order to effectively fight related customs crimes.
The two sides praised the importance of the bilateral meeting, which will be a turning point in cooperation and mutual assistance, especially in the fight against tax evasion and transnational crime. Recent developments of the two countries, the region and the world to help promote economic development, trade, investment and revenue collection of the two countries' respective states.
