Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Receives Cambodian Youth Delegation of Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association and Japan
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on the afternoon of October 2, 2018, received a courtesy call from 27 Cambodian youths who will participate in the annual Southeast Asian Youth Ship Program.
These young people have been selected to participate in the "45th Southeast Asian Youth Ship Program" in Japan, which will take place from October 23 to December 12, 2018.
The purpose of this program is to strengthen the relationship and mutual understanding between the youth of Japan and the youth of the 10 Southeast Asian countries, expand their perspective on the world and, in addition, to strengthen the spirit of cooperation. International operations and practical skills for international cooperation.
These goals can be achieved by participating in their daily life on board, getting to know each other about their country, engaging in discussions and many other exchange activities while sailing and According to the countries they have to visit.
