Before the occasion of Pchum Ben arrives! CamControl officers inspected goods at the depot and found damaged noodles, coffee and fish cakes and burned them.
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the upcoming Pchum Ben festival, in order to protect food safety for the people, CamControl officers at the end of Phnom Penh on October 2, 2018, inspected many kinds of food and fruits and vegetables at the market. The depot found damaged noodles, coffee and fish cakes and decided to confiscate them from traders to destroy immediately.
After confiscating these defective goods, Mr. Kong Vuthy asked the traders to sign a contract to stop selling defective goods, which will affect the health of consumers, and if there are more exhibits, legal action will be taken.
He also called on traders, wholesalers, wholesalers, retailers, manufacturers, importers and distributors to have a clear source before accepting sales and confirm the addition of chemicals to food products that affect the health of consumers.
According to Mr. Kong Vuthy, in this search operation, it was done according to the order of the head of the delegation in charge of the General Department of CamControl and the head of the Phnom Penh Dry Port Branch, who thought about the safety and health of the people, and this was done like rain. So early.
