Separately, Ms. Mom Chandani, Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that "according to the 2017 statistics, the number of elderly people in Phnom Penh from 61 years old is 133,363."
She stated that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has made it a priority for the Capital Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation officials to include the program and manage the Association of the Elderly in the meeting program of the Phnom Penh Capital Council so that the Sangkat in Phnom Penh can continue to implement, compile, strengthen and expand. The association currently has a total of 20,162 members, including 11,574 women.
Ms. Mom Chandani added that the main problems of the elderly are mental health, poor memory, low income opportunities, difficult to travel, especially responsible for looking after the house and children.
She pointed out that some older people, due to the poor situation, go out to find money to support the family economy, and a small number of elderly people are abandoned by their children, their children are forced to migrate abroad or leave. From a long-term home, leaving the elderly to take care of grandchildren and find money for daily living.
Ministry of Education warns to take legal action against those who take the opportunity to promise to run for teacher exams and calls on parents not to cheat
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on October 2, 2018 issued a press release warning to take legal action against those who take the opportunity to promise to run for the teacher entrance exam.
The reason why the Ministry of Education issued this press release is because there are reports that some individuals have promised to help candidates for the exam to become teachers at all levels to pass the exam in exchange for some money.
"The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports would like to emphasize that the teacher recruitment process at all levels will be conducted in accordance with the principles of law, justice, transparency and acceptable results," said a press release from Fresh News. .
At the same time, the Ministry of Education calls on all parents, guardians and candidates not to be deceived by the lies of those who take any opportunity that leads to loss of money and property in vain, and calls on all candidates to strive to show their ability and comply with the regulations. In the selection exam process.
