Mr. Chheang Vun's request was made on October 1, 2018 in Pailin Province on the occasion of Mr. and Mrs. Ban Srey Mom, Deputy Chairman of the 5th Commission, leading a delegation to meet and discuss with the Thai delegation led by Ms. Bilaibhan Sampatisari Chairman of the Foreign Affairs Committee of the Thai National Assembly to strengthen ties and enhance better cooperation between the two countries' legislatures.
Chheang Vun said the two countries need to increase friendly cooperation between parliamentarians and along the border to serve the interests of the people and the nation honestly and fairly.
At the same time, Ms. Ban Srey Mom also requested the Thai side to help make it easier for Cambodians to cross the border to seek medical treatment or to travel in Thailand, especially Cambodian workers who are working in Thailand and traveling across the border. Visit your hometown for festivals or participate in elections.
In response, Ms. Bilaibhan Sampatisari promised to work hard to cooperate and resolve all requests of the Cambodian side within its jurisdiction, among other issues. She also promised to discuss with relevant officials and leaders as well as the Royal Government of Thailand to find possibilities and solutions to enhance cooperation between the two countries.
Please note that this is the first time that the High Commission of the National Assembly of both Cambodia and Thailand has met in Pailin to strengthen ties and enhance cooperation between the legal institutions. Provisions of both countries.
