The Ministry of Education announces the selection of candidates for the ASEAN Award to participate in building the ASEAN Community
Applicants must be a citizen of an ASEAN country or an institution in an ASEAN member country. Candidates must present their achievements between April 2017 and March 2018, which can be verified as true or false in promoting cooperation between ASEAN countries.
For the competition, candidates must write a form describing their work to the jury to decide which one is the best, and the announcement and award program is scheduled to take place at the 33rd ASEAN Leaders' Meeting. In Singapore in November 2018 or in a ministerial meeting.
Upon winning, the winner will receive a cash prize of $ 20,000 and the winner may be invited to participate in a number of ASEAN events.
Candidates should also share their future plans to continue this effort after receiving the award.
This is the first competition ever held and will take place every year.
The Ministry of Education has confirmed that the announcement of the ASEAN Awards is based on the initiative of Singapore as the Chair of ASEAN, which requested each ASEAN member country to select the candidates (candidates / institutions) who have Outstanding and outstanding achievements in the efforts to participate in building the ASEAN Community.
