Regarding the agricultural sector in Cambodia, the US Ambassador to Cambodia, William Hedd, who also attended the meeting, informed Samdech Techo that at present, there are about 6 to 10 US agricultural companies that have come and are discussing. Seek investment opportunities and cooperation in Cambodia.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed and informed the entire delegation that agriculture was a key issue that could not be overlooked. Regarding the issue of climate change, Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that it causes floods and unseasonal rains and creates problems not only in Cambodia but all over the world.
Samdech Techo continued that rice varieties, crops that used to be exposed to heat that used to be present now need to be reviewed due to the increase in heat. In this regard, Samdech said that the United States really has the technology and asked investors to consider using these technologies in Cambodia as well as in the region.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked the company to consider investing in the processing of Cambodian agricultural products into semi-finished products or finished products that can serve both domestic and foreign markets. .
He hoped that the United States would play a key role in tackling climate change and other investment issues such as economic, energy, infrastructure development, human resource and cultural development. To find a solution and in case it can not be solved, please bring those problems to Samdech immediately.
