Shares held by foreign investors have risen sharply this year to 6% and are expected to rise further in the next few months.
Foreign investors now hold as many Class A shares as the number held by Chinese insurers. Soon, the number of shares held by foreign investors will be equal to the number of shares in the national budget.
Foreign investment in China through the mainland-Hong Kong stock exchange has reached nearly 3 billion US dollars so far this year, more than three times as much. Compare that to the amount of capital that mainland Chinese investors invest in the Hong Kong Stock Exchange.
The Chinese government has officially set up a national financial insurance fund in Beijing to help boost small businesses and the agricultural sector.
In March, China's central government, also known as the National People's Congress, approved a plan to launch a financial insurance fund with an initial budget of at least $ 8.7 billion. The fund provides financial assistance to various financial insurance projects funded by local governments.
Initiated by the Chinese Ministry of Finance and supported by a number of financial institutions, the fund aims to eliminate the financial barriers faced by small and micro businesses to enable them to contribute to growth. The economy has improved.
"The national financial insurance fund set up today is an important link for perfecting our entire policy system," said Liu Wei, China's deputy finance minister. "It is also an important measure to support the development of the national economy."
It is estimated that the fund will be able to provide about $ 73 billion in financial assistance to lending services over the next three years, equivalent to one-third of the current national financial insurance services. Already. The fund will effectively address the financial problems of small and medium-sized businesses in the agricultural sector, as well as support the development of key emerging industries.
Wang Yi, director of the Ministry of Finance of the People's Republic of China, said: "By working through renewal insurance and capital investment, the central financial insurance system set up by the central government supports regional governments in their work." "Provide financial insurance funds that will be able to provide more benefits as well as lead to more lending to small and medium enterprises."
