(Phnom Penh): After seeing the demand for affordable housing for civil servants, Dr. Kim Heang, President of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors, requested the Royal Government of Cambodia to consider the possibility of building a house worth only $ 10,000 for sale. To civil servants.
Such remarks by the president of the Association of Appraisers and Real Estate Agents in the sense of facilitating the lives of civil servants, because they can not rely on salaries to buy expensive houses.
Speaking in an interview with "Fresh Guest of the Week", a new program on Fresh News TV on October 1, 2018, Dr. Kim Heang, President of the Association of Appraisers and Real Estate Agents of Cambodia, explained in detail about the "need for development Build low-cost houses for people and civil servants in Cambodia.
