"I can say that state-owned houses are state-owned land, and the Royal Government of Cambodia will complete the infrastructure, which means that the Royal Government will build all kinds of sewerage and electricity systems for private companies to bid," he said. "Investment."
He added, "The state house that I am talking about is for sale only to civil servants ... In Cambodia, there are about 1 million civil servants, but that does not mean that the Royal Government is required to build houses for sale. 1 million civil servants, but can make 1,000 to 10,000 apartments, depending on the actual process and sell to civil servants according to the set, this is to ease the burden of civil servants to some extent.
