Minister Vong Soth: In this sixth mandate, the Royal Government continues to strengthen the elderly associations in communes more widely.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly on October 1 were held in order to promote the protection of the elderly in order to improve the welfare of the elderly. To better and show the important role of the elderly in society.
Mr. Vong Soth added, "We all know that the elderly are the ancestors who created useful resources and play a very important role in building families, communities, education, providing knowledge, culture, traditions and experiences. Innumerable for the next generation. In general, the elderly always take the pagoda as a place to meet and stay according to the ability of each family.
Minister Vong Soth stated that in the last three years, the Ministry of Social Affairs has established 1,646 senior associations in communes and sangkats throughout the provincial capital, including 394 in 2016, 1242 in 2017 and 2018. 10 more communes / sangkats.
Mr. Vong Soth's remarks were made at the celebration of the 20th anniversary of the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the International Day of the Elderly on October 1 under the theme "The Association of the Elderly is an important mechanism for preserving family culture and society." »Held on October 1, 2018 in Svay Rieng province.
Minister Vong Soth said that the social sector, veterans and youth rehabilitation have also achieved many new achievements to contribute to the implementation of social policies aimed at increasing public services to help vulnerable and vulnerable groups in society. Then the welfare work of the elderly is continuously improved in line with the actual situation of Cambodia.
