Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a delegation to fly from Cambodia to New York, USA on September 27, 2018 to attend the 73rd General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly.
In the United States these days, Samdech Techo Hun Sen made a statement at the United Nations, highlighting the progress of the Cambodian nation, the election issue and the issue of the world. In that statement, the Prime Minister highlighted the importance of human rights and democracy, which are now used by some major powers as a shield to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries.
In addition to making statements on behalf of UN member states, Hun Sen also held bilateral talks with the Prime Minister of Nepal, the Prime Minister of Bulgaria, the US-ASEAN Business Council and the Secretary-General of the United Nations. Nation, too.
Despite the busy schedule of missions in the United States, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also had a face-to-face meeting with some 2,000 Cambodians throughout the night. The gesture of the leader who always cares for Cambodians everywhere Samdech Techo was warmly welcomed, respected and supported by Cambodians in the United States.
In that meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the development of the nation in terms of economic, social and political work. In particular, Samdech reminded of the commitment and priority policies of the new government, which is paying attention to promote national development.
Overall, Samdech Techo's mission to the United States is seen as raising the nation's prestige and prestige on the international stage and is also considered a journey that brings high honor and pride for the Cambodian nation. The whole as well.
