(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has established an understanding program on the 2018 voter list and voter registration to make people more aware of the voter list and registration. Its vote.
In fact, on October 1, 2018, the voter registration offices for the 2018 voter list review and registration in communes across Cambodia have started to allow people to check the list.
According to the NEC, for Cambodians who are on the 2017 voter list, check their names posted at the commune hall to make sure they have the correct name and data in Voter list. In case their name or data is incorrect, they must ask the voter registration team to make the correct correction according to the clear reference documents.
The 2018 voter list and voter registration review will last for 18 days, starting from today until October 18, 2018 at commune halls and in some villages in communes across the country.
