General Department of Taxation Disseminates Tax Culture and Tax Regulations to Taxpayers in Battambang Province
(Battambang): The General Department of Taxation disseminated information on tax culture and tax regulations to taxable traders in Battambang province and encouraged citizens to fulfill their obligations in paying taxes to the state.
This dissemination workshop was held on the morning of October 1, 2018 at Khemara Hotel, Battambang 1, Battambang City, in the presence of Mr. Oeur Samrith, Deputy Director of the Department of Small and Medium Taxpayers of the General Department of Taxation, Mr. Hoeung Sokun, Deputy Governor and officials Relevant around the province, some traders and co-organized by the Battambang Provincial Tax Branch.
Mr. Hoeung Sokun spoke and urged all business owners, enterprises and companies in Battambang province to fulfill their obligation to pay taxes to the state on time so that no penalties or fines will occur.
Mr. Hoeung Sokun stated that those who are obliged to pay taxes to the state must make efforts to study, understand and ask more professional officials on this issue to better understand the procedure for paying taxes to the state.
"Once we have understood the explanations of the officials and we have the knowledge to pay taxes to avoid mistakes, to apply correctly, without fines, to lose more money, and after understanding that people "Citizens will have a clear understanding of the law and the observance of the law related to paying taxes properly and regularly."
Participants, business owners or representatives of enterprises participating in the workshop, stated that they are committed to fulfilling their tax obligations to the state in accordance with the law, without resorting to tax evasion.
Trade Minister urges Thai business delegation to invest in SEZ development
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, urged the Thai Business Council to consider investing in the establishment of small and medium enterprises in special economic zones throughout Cambodia to diversify the value chain, industry and create job opportunities for people. In particular, enhance the effectiveness of the implementation of the fourth phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak informed the Thai side about the goals of the new Rectangular Strategy, which is the agenda for socio-economic development in the sixth term of the Royal Government and Cambodia's key priority products, as well as the benefits of investing in Special economic zones, such as 100% legal occupancy rights and preferential tariffs for export to third countries.
The Minister also requested Mr. Channit Chanchai Narong to inform the Thai government, especially the Thai Ministry of Economy, to expedite the signing of a memorandum of understanding on tax exemptions along the border to facilitate trade between the two countries to reach 15 billion. Dollars as planned by 2020.
In response, the Chairman of the Thai Business Council, Mr. Channit Chanchai Narong, thanked the Minister for sharing important information and good recommendations to promote economic and trade cooperation between the two countries. Regarding tax exemptions and border trade facilitation, he promised to bring the minister's request to the Thai government to expedite the matter.
It should be reminded that in March, Cambodia and Thailand held the 6th Joint Trade Commission Meeting (6th JTC) at Sofitel Phnom Penh Phuket to discuss and exchange views on various challenges. Increase bilateral trade to $ 15 billion by 2020
At the meeting, the two countries agreed to strengthen trade facilitation, open new border crossings and set up more business and investment forums. In addition, the two sides signed two important documents: first, a strategy for the growth of economic cooperation in border provinces, and second, a memorandum of understanding on trade promotion cooperation.
