Khema International Polyclinic inaugurates a state-of-the-art dialysis clinic from Japan
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 1, 2018, Khema International Polyclinic officially inaugurated a dialysis clinic with the same high quality machines from Japan as in Singapore and Thailand. Western countries as well.
Dr. Ou Sopheap, Director of Khema International Polyclinic, said, “Khema Dialysis Clinic will contribute to raising the quality and standard of dialysis in Cambodia to the level of regional and international dialysis facilities because we use state-of-the-art technology and expertise. Same. ”
More specifically, treatment in Cambodia, we do not cost as much as in other countries, the price is less than 50%, which we do not consider the cost of airfare, accommodation and food.
"The installation of four dialysis units this morning is a first step, and Khema International Polyclinic will increase between 20 and 30 units a year to be in line with the dialysis center," he said. International standards.
He stated that Khema Blood Purification Clinic has a good treatment environment, equipped with brand new and modern blood washing machine, made in Japan, always using new washing equipment (disposable, not reused), managed and operated by professional staff and has Experienced experience in collaboration with kidney professors and dialysis experts from Taiwan.
According to the experts, dialysis is a way to filter out wastes such as creatinine and urea and excess fluid from the body by using a dialysis machine instead of a damaged natural kidney. Before dialysis, patients with complete kidney failure had no hope of survival, but now patients with kidney failure can live and work normally.
