Golden FX Link shares knowledge and investment to Cambodian trainees
(Phnom Penh): Derivatives trading is gaining a lot of support around the world due to the diversity of trading products and the huge investment opportunities. For many countries around the world, including the United States, the United Kingdom, Japan, Australia and Canada, derivatives trading has been important and long-standing.
But for Cambodia, derivatives trading has not grown as much as in other countries, as the sector is new to Cambodian investors. Due to this, Golden FX Link Capital is committed to providing education and tips. To the public on sharing experiences in the field of derivatives trading to ensure that they can better use their investment knowledge.
In fact, Golden FX Link Capital has organized a series of workshops and trainings. The company has organized a workshop on "How to make money from derivatives trading without experience" held on the 29th. September 2018.
The workshop was attended by two speakers: Dr. Mam Sarith, Professor, Member of the Scientific Council of the University of Economics and Finance, and Mr. Don David, Head of Financial Advisory, Golden FX Link Capital.
Dr. Mam Sarith explained to the participants in detail about the financial perspective as well as the implementation and key economic theories. He emphasized the impact of microeconomics and macroeconomics on the volatility of financial markets, especially derivatives markets, which provided participants with a solid foundation for analyzing information and economic trends.
In that, Mr. David explained in detail about derivatives trading that trading derivatives is not very difficult, if we dare to try, it will be better for investors when they know how to use investment knowledge and be Supported by a truly professional consultant.
131 killed, 332 injured in road accidents in Cambodia in September
(Phnom Penh): At least 131 people were killed and 332 others injured in traffic accidents in Cambodia in September 2018. This is according to the report of the Department of Traffic Police and Public Order of the General Commission of the National Police.
