(Ratanakkiri): Both national and provincial authorities have been criticized for their inability to resolve a long-running dispute between Chea Kuong's garbage truck company and Banlung Market investment tycoon Oknha Salang for allowing garbage collection and storage in front of him. Banlung market has been in trouble until now.
Disputes between Chea Kuong and Tycoon Salang's concessionaires in Ratanakkiri have been going on for years, and have often been brought to court and national and provincial authorities. Still can not find a solution.
The dispute has been reported to the national and provincial authorities several times, but no solution has been found. Currently, the Ratanakkiri Provincial Court has allowed the Banlung Market Investment Company to collect and transport garbage by itself, in violation of the company's right to invest in garbage collection.
Not only that, the investment company in Banlung Market does not have a place to leave garbage, but instead dumped garbage on the land of Chea Kuong's garbage collection company. The dispute is causing inactivity in garbage collection in Banlung, which is a major impact on the aesthetics and hygiene in the city of this northeastern eco-tourism province.
This has led the people of Ratanakkiri to blame the authorities at both the national and provincial levels for their inability to control investors in the province, allowing them to do whatever they want with the power of their money. The villagers also asked the authorities at both the national and provincial levels to conduct a thorough study on this issue to solve the garbage problem at Banlung Market.
