(Kandal): Two masterminds who have been using the image of buying people's hearts to collect ID cards to sign a contract to buy and sell wind land in Leuk Dek district, Kandal province, were recently arrested by the authorities and called to make an education contract. Stop these activities immediately.
However, for the two masterminds, after the authorities signed an education contract, they were allowed to return, but if they continue to do so, the authorities will take legal action. This is according to the report from the local authority that told the news agency Fresh News on September 30, 2018.
It should be noted that in recent times, many people living in Prek Dach commune, Prek Tomlab commune and Kampong Phnom commune, Leuk Dek district, Kandal province, have been deceived and bought by land brokers through sarong funding. And rice to collect their ID cards to make contracts to buy and sell land, but in reality those lands have real owners, with some owners living in Phnom Penh and others living locally.
The reason why the traders formed such an anarchic movement is because they have already signed a contract with a Chinese company to arrange to buy land in those areas. Halfway through and facing another Chinese company, they created a new trick to buy people's hearts as a barrier, creating a contract to sell land and air.
Mr. Mao Phirun even announced that he would not take any legal action against the corrupt traders who did this to the local people. Mr. Mao Phirun stated, "Thank you for providing information on the above case. I will investigate and take action to prevent and suppress this illegal activity."
Separately, the governor of Leuk Dek district, Kandal province, Mr. Nou Samnang also confirmed that in recent days, he also received such information and assigned the commune chief to research and collect information, but has not yet received official results. No.
The district governor also told the commune chief to advise the villagers, if this happens, to explain and tell him not to be deceived by buying hearts, because if you give them a thumbprint, they will be responsible for selling the land. They.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement was made on the night of September 29, 2018 in New York City, during his meeting with about 2,000 Cambodians in the United States at a hotel in New York after the end of his mission. That's a busy job.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that when a Cambodian-American citizen commits an illegal act and is imprisoned, his relatives and family can visit him, but when his sentence is completed, he will be sent to Cambodia. That is only a waste.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia said, "Both I and the members of the Royal Government look too hard on our citizens to be imprisoned in the United States and the United States must be sent to Cambodia." "Imprisonment in the United States is already a crime, but the heaviest punishment is extortion."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued, "When you are in prison in the United States, you can visit some of them, some of you are in prison, some of you are in prison, some of you are in prison, some of you are in prison, some of you are in prison, some of you are in prison." "The prison and the United States send them to Cambodia forever, unless their families can travel to Cambodia."
The Prime Minister also stressed that in the case of the deportation of Cambodian-Americans who were imprisoned, five Cambodians committed suicide because they were upset with the US government for sending them back to Cambodia to destroy their families. .
Please note that the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the United States have signed an agreement to send and receive Cambodian citizens from the United States to return to Cambodia since 2002. Under this agreement, the US government will repatriate any Cambodian who commits an offense after serving his sentence.
But at the end of 2017, the repatriation of Cambodian citizens from the United States failed because the United States did not comply with Cambodia's request to amend some of the terms of the agreement on a voluntary basis.
The United States has decided to suspend visas for senior State Department officials and their relatives, which the Cambodian government considers to be due to the revision of the agreement. At the same time, Cambodia also decided to suspend Cambodian-US cooperation in the search for the remains of American soldiers who went missing in Cambodia during the war.
Please be reminded that during April 2018, 43 Cambodians living in the United States, including 3 women, were sent to Cambodia after completing their prison sentences, some of whom had health problems. Also.
