Senior Minister Kun Kim: The presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the United Nations is an honor and pride of the Cambodian nation
(Preah Vihear): Addressing 1,333 veterans in Preah Vihear province, Senior Minister Kun Kim said that the presence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the United Nations now is a new honor and pride. The rest of the whole Cambodian nation.
At the handing over ceremony of the National Social Security Fund to Veterans on September 29, 2018, Senior Minister Kun Kim presented a very meaningful speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the United Nations. Last night, to all the veterans who participated in the ceremony.
Mr. Kun Kim quoted the summary of Samdech Techo's speech, such as showing the situation of Cambodia, which has been at war from the past to the peace stage, from a poor country to a low-middle-income country, the election issue in Cambodia. Like the problem in the world where some great powers take human rights issues to interfere in the affairs of other countries ....
Mr. Kun Kim emphasized that through Samdech Techo's remarks, Cambodia has made a significant contribution to maintaining world peace through the core role of the United Nations.
"The presence and speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen underscored our important role in Cambodia on the international stage. Although we are a small country, as a member of the United Nations, our voice is shown to the world. "It is an honor and a source of pride for us Cambodians to have a strong leader in national development and to play an important role on the international stage." Mr. Kun Kim further confirmed.
During the ceremony, both Kun Kim and Cambodian veterans expressed their deep satisfaction with Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech at the United Nations. They said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's words show the reality of Cambodia and the world that must be taken care of to build a peaceful world for all nations.
