The Palestinian Authority made the request in a complaint filed with the ICJ against the United States on Friday. The 14-page lawsuit alleges that the relocation of the US Embassy in Israel to Jerusalem violated the Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations dated 18 April 1961.
The Palestinian Authority also called on the International Court of Justice to declare that the relocation of the US Embassy to Jerusalem violated international diplomatic law and forced Washington to withdraw all its diplomatic missions from the city. .
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports held a solidarity dinner on the evening of September 29, 2018 in the presence of Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State, Representative of Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education.
The event was attended by nearly 400 government officials from the General Department of Sports, the Department of Legislation, the Department of Health, the Department of Education, Drugs and Human Trafficking at Tonle Bassac 2 Restaurant.
On that occasion, Mr. Sar Sokha sponsored 45 disabled athletes who are ready to participate in the upcoming international sports competition in Indonesia, $ 100 each, in addition to the budget of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Support $ 200 per person. National Bank of Cambodia: Currently, 67% of Cambodia's adult population is using financial services
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, highlighted the development of the banking sector in Cambodia, in which he highlighted the rapid growth of the use of financial services by the current population. The age of using this service is up to 67%, compared to less than 10% in the past.
This statement was made by the Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia on the occasion of his meeting with 33 representatives of the 45th Cambodia-Japan Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association on September 28, 2018.
According to the Governor-General, the microfinance sector in Cambodia is currently contributing to reducing poverty and improving the lives of Cambodians. The steady increase in the financial environment is reflected in the growing number of adults using financial services.
"Currently, the microfinance sector is growing remarkably, with assets in this sector increasing to 14% of the assets of banking institutions, loans to 19.2% of loans of banking institutions and "Deposits rose to 11.1 percent of bank deposits."
He added that the growth of up to 67% of the use of financial services by the adult population in Cambodia is a very high increase compared to the same period a decade ago, which was just under 10%. . In addition, the growing population using financial services also reflects the level of public awareness of the sector.
"The microfinance sector has provided loans to 1.8 million people and 1.6 million depositors," he said. The microfinance sector has not only contributed to the expansion of the financial environment, but also provided employment to 30,000 people, and microfinance loans have been provided to various economic sectors, including: agriculture 30%, households 30.5%, business sector 18.8%, service sector 10% and other sectors 10%.
It should be noted that the National Bank of Cambodia has contributed to further economic development by improving financial infrastructure, expanding the financial services network, and improving regulations and controls to ensure a strong and efficient banking system. Efficiency: 20 poor families in O Andong, Sangkat Otavao, Pailin City received donations from Pailin Provincial Authority
