Cambridge International School of Cambodia launches joint trilingual education
(Phnom Penh): To strengthen the capacity of children as well as the current and future market needs, Cambridge International School of Cambodia has launched a language curriculum focusing on three languages at the same time.
Regarding the introduction of trilingual education, Ms. Ly Leth, Director of Cambridge International School in Cambodia, stated that it is a complete language curriculum with both Khmer, English and Chinese at the same time.
She believes that the introduction of the trilingual curriculum is a path to unlimited opportunities in the future in communication as well as in the field of employment, both nationally and internationally. It is especially important at a time when Chinese tourists and the number of Chinese investors coming to Cambodia rank among the highest.
She added that this trilingual education needs to cultivate the will of parents to understand the competitive environment for their children and also requires all children to be willing to love learning in three languages in conjunction with experienced teachers and pedagogy. Accurate and clear curriculum, internationally recognized.
Cambridge International School of Cambodia is a school that provides a truly international education, with subjects such as mathematics, social studies, as well as science subjects all being studied in a foreign language. The main purpose of the school is to build leaders for the future in a multicultural community with high morals and competencies.
