(Phnom Penh): Dialysis is a way to filter out wastes such as creatinine and urea and excess fluid from the body by using a dialysis machine instead of a naturally damaged kidney. Before dialysis, patients with complete kidney failure had no hope of survival, but now patients with kidney failure can live and work normally.
The dialysis clinic at Khema International Polyclinic, which was inaugurated on October 1, 2018, will contribute to providing high quality dialysis services in Cambodia in accordance with internationally recognized medical standards. .
Khema Blood Purification Clinic has a good treatment environment, equipped with brand new and modern blood washing machine, made in Japan, always using new washing equipment, disposable, non-reusable, managed and operated by professional and experienced staff in cooperation. With a kidney professor and dialysis specialist from Taiwan.
Dr. Ou Sopheap, Director of Khema International Polyclinic, said that Khema Dialysis Clinic will contribute to raising the quality and standard of dialysis in Cambodia to the level of regional and international dialysis because we use the same machines, the same technology. And the same expert level.
In addition, Professor Tou Chean Sai, President of the Asian Health Company, which cooperates with Khema International Polyclinic, agreed that the organization and operation of Khema Dialysis Clinic is similar to the Dialysis Center in Taiwan, Japan or Singapore.
