Preah Sihanouk Province: Police in Preah Sihanouk Province launched an operation to detain two Chinese suspects this morning, September 29, 2018, after receiving a report from the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, which reported to the police that An ethnic national was detained in the room of the Hubei Guesthouse in Group 17, Village 1, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville.
Brigadier General Kol Phaly, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning, said that after receiving this information and under the direct command of Major General Chuon Narin, Provincial Police Commissioner, the Criminal Police Planning Special Forces, in cooperation with the Sangkat 4 Police Force, conducted a rescue operation. 2 victims and arrested 2 suspects.
According to the Deputy Commissioner, this case occurred because the victim went to gamble at the New Macau Casino and borrowed money from the suspects when there was no money to pay, the suspects took the victim into the room where they stayed. In order for the victims to contact the family to find money to pay them back, they were released. The suspect is currently being prosecuted by the light criminal police office.
