Cambodia plans to reopen embassy in Bulgaria in 2019
(New York, USA): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has stated that Cambodia will reopen its embassy in Bulgaria after being temporarily closed due to the political situation in the country.
This confirmation was made during a working meeting between Samdech Techo and Mr. Boyko Borissov, Prime Minister of Bulgaria on the morning of September 28, 2018 in New York, USA. The Prime Minister of Bulgaria welcomed Samdech's initiative to open an embassy in Bulgaria, which is also an opportunity for Samdech to pay an official visit to Bulgaria.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister praised Bulgaria's role in the past, which played a role in helping Cambodia when Cambodia was liberated from the Pol Pot genocidal regime and continued to contribute to peacekeeping. In Cambodia after the Paris Agreement.
The two heads of government also agreed to further strengthen the cooperation between the two countries in the fields of economy, investment, trade and tourism.
Relations between Cambodia and the United States have been strained in recent times. But in the meeting, positive signs of improvement in relations between the two countries seem to emerge.
In response to this, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Samdech himself is the one who strives to promote the building of relations between Cambodia and the United States. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia wants to make good friends with the United States, and what he wants to see is better relations between the two countries, especially between the government and the government, as the US business community wants. That.
During the meeting, Alexander Feldman also discussed doing business with Cambodia. As the Executive Director of the US-ASEAN Business Council, he called on Cambodia to pursue a broader economic policy, as Cambodia is a member of ASEAN, and he wanted Cambodia to continue to support and promote capacity building, especially The quality of education within the ASEAN framework.
The President and CEO of the US-ASEAN Business Council also praised the current strength and capacity of Cambodian youth, which is growing in line with the growth of the digital economy, which he expects Samdech Techo to have. Highly interested in a good future with Cambodia's competition.
In response to the remarks made by the President and CEO of the US-ASEAN Business Council, Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed and mentioned the economic growth of Cambodia, which maintains economic growth of more than 7%, the economic growth in 2018. Cambodia will have an economic growth of about 7.2%.
For Samdech Techo himself, he wants to see the implementation of the 1 plus 1 formula, that is, foreign companies that are investing in ASEAN countries, including companies from the United States, can afford to set up factories in Cambodia, for example, Thailand Plus One. This means that US companies operating in Thailand can also open factories in Cambodia.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that if the United States reopens visas to Cambodian officials, the search for the remains of missing US soldiers will resume, as we have done together in the past.
Cambodia and Nepal plan to sign a number of agreements and memorandums during Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Nepal later this year
(New York, USA): Many agreements and memoranda of understanding between Cambodia and Nepal are scheduled to take place at the end of 2018, during the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Nepal requested the Foreign Ministers of the two countries to discuss the schedule of his visit to Nepal, which is scheduled to take place in late November or early December. In particular, the preparation of agreements and memoranda of understanding to be signed together.
Agreements and Memoranda of Understanding to be made at that time include: Joint Statement of Visits, Visa Exemption Agreement on Diplomatic and Official Passports, Investment Protection Agreement, Memorandum of Understanding on Political Consultations between Ministries The two countries' foreign affairs and the agreement on strengthening economic, political and cultural ties between the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also pointed out that during his visit to Nepal, in addition to attending a meeting of the Central Political Party, he also planned to visit the historical site of our Master Buddha.
During the meeting, the Prime Minister of Nepal congratulated the Cambodian People's Party on its landslide victory in the parliamentary elections, which brought good political stability for Cambodia.
Samdech Techo also thanked Nepal for sending its observers to observe the recent 6th general election and assessed that the election process was free, fair, democratic and acceptable. Yes.
