Cambodia has the opportunity to chair the Plenary Session of the General Dialogue at the United Nations
(Phnom Penh): In his capacity as the Vice-President of the 73rd United Nations General Assembly, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, presided over the Plenary Session of the General Dialogue at the United Nations on September 28, 2018.
The opportunity to chair this plenary session of the General Dialogue is a proud and prestigious opportunity for the Cambodian Foreign Minister to bring Cambodia's reputation to the world.
Please note that Cambodia has served as the Vice President of the United Nations General Assembly twice. The first time in the 56th session of the United Nations General Assembly, 2001-2002 and the second time in the 73rd session of the United Nations General Assembly, 2018-2019.
Through this role, Cambodia may have the opportunity to chair meetings of the General Assembly on behalf of the President and at the request of the President.
