Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this in a statement made at the General Assembly of the 73rd United Nations General Assembly at the United Nations at more than 1 am on September 29, 2018 This time in Cambodia, which is almost 2 pm on September 28 in New York, USA.
Human rights and the practice of democracy are seen as a popular issue in liberal countries, including the United States, often used as an excuse to impose sanctions or even to overthrow the regimes in some countries. In Cambodia today, too, the issue of respect for human rights and democracy has become an issue that the United States and some other liberals use to attack the Royal Government of Cambodia.
From the United Nations Headquarters in the United States, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the current human rights issue has become a "mission to equip civilization" for some powerful countries, or in other words, an executive norm. New, used as an excuse to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries.
"Unilateral sanctions have become a popular weapon of superpowers in governing international politics under the geopolitical agenda," he said. "These are nothing more than the arbitrary use of power by one state to impose its will on other sovereign states."
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia said that the era of imperialism and colonialism for the world, it has become a historical event. Therefore, big countries should not impose their administrative system on smaller countries, because these small countries also have sovereignty and a legitimate desire to maintain their identity.
The Prime Minister also stressed that the present era is a time when all countries in the world are interdependent and that the old coercive mindset should be ended. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that small and large countries must jointly respect and uphold the rules of international law and the UN Charter, which stipulate mutual respect and non-interference.
