(Phnom Penh): At approximately 1:03 AM on September 29, 2018, Cambodian time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen concluded his statement at the 73rd General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly. Nation.
In this speech, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the major issues facing the world as well as many of Cambodia's achievements. The following is the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech: The Minister of Health urges scholarship students to study in France and strive to acquire knowledge and experience to develop the country
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, encouraged and encouraged the medical students of the University of Health Sciences to receive scholarships to study in the French Republic in 2018. Bring new knowledge and experience from France to contribute to the development of the health sector in the country.
The professor made this warning during a meeting with students at the University of Health Sciences on September 28, 2018.
Minister Mam Bunheng said that due to the policy of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has made the country peaceful and developed, which is an opportunity for the children of the people to receive a full education. It starts from good relations and the efforts of the Royal Government to find scholarships for Cambodian students to study in France.
The French Ambassador to Cambodia, Eva Nguyen Binh, stated that France has been supporting scientific cooperation and training at the University of Health Sciences by providing scholarships to students. The mission of French experts will support international training programs and provide technical experts and international volunteers to assist the University of Health Sciences.
She said that when these scholarship students return to Cambodia, they will become members of the Alumni Association who have continued their studies in France. In addition, the French Embassy will support the launch of Espace France at the University of Health Sciences.
The Ambassador also commended all the selected students for their medical education in French. In addition, these 48 students were selected from a total of 690 students in the world to continue their studies in France this year, which shows the ability of Cambodian students.
Professor Mam Bunheng expressed his deep gratitude to the French government for its continued support for the development of the health sector. Especially training at the University of Health Sciences.
Mr. Mam Bunheng also reminded students to study in France to know how to disseminate the culture, politics, development of Cambodia's health sector to the countries there.
