At the United Nations, on behalf of the entire Cambodian nation, Samdech Techo reiterated his call for respect for the sovereignty of all nations, without interfering in the internal affairs of any country, no matter how small or poor. Case. He also called for respect for international law and the principle of pluralism, with the United Nations as the mediator for a world full of peace and development.
Please note that this time, Cambodia has been elected as the Vice President of the 73rd United Nations General Assembly (UN) of the United Nations mandate 2018-2019. Cambodia has served as Vice-Chair of the United Nations General Assembly twice, the first time at the 56th session of the United Nations General Assembly, 2001-2002, and the second time at the General Assembly. The 73rd United Nations mandate 2018-2019.
The three proposals raised at the meeting were: Problems of the Office of the United Nations Human Rights Organization in Cambodia, 2. Cooperation between Cambodia and the United Nations on the Khmer Rouge Tribunal; Deployment of peacekeepers.
Regarding the issue of the Office of the United Nations Human Rights Organization, which is due to expire in 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to extend his term for another two years in October when he will visit the city. Geneva will be signed by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, and a representative of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights.
For the second problem. Samdech Techo confirmed that Cambodia continues to provide funding for the salaries of officials and staff at the Khmer Rouge tribunal. The third issue is that the Royal Government of Cambodia will continue to be more active in the United Nations peacekeeping mission. That is, if any country needs the Cambodian Blue Hat Army to participate in humanitarian missions under the umbrella of the United Nations, Cambodia will send more.
In response, the Secretary-General of the United Nations approved the three proposals of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo for extending the mandate of the United Nations Center for Human Rights in Cambodia for two years. Next year.
For the second and third issues, the Secretary-General praised Cambodia for its genuine willingness to assist the United Nations, especially the presence of a disciplined and fully capable Blue Hat Army in humanitarian and maintenance activities. Peace under the umbrella of the United Nations.
