Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this statement in a statement made at the 73rd General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly at the United Nations at more than 1 am on September 29, 2012. 2018 is Cambodian time, which is almost 2 pm on September 28 in New York, USA.
In front of UN officials and leaders of countries participating in the UN General Assembly, the Prime Minister presented the process of the 6th National Assembly election on July 29. 2018 has been a good year.
Samdech Techo stated that in the last election, nearly 7 million people went to the polls, or 83.02 percent of the total number of registered voters. The Prime Minister added that the people of Cambodia went to the polls and decided to make their political choices freely and without any coercion or intimidation or violence.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned that 20 political parties competed in the election, which was a clear demonstration of the legitimate representation of pluralism and reflected the views of tens of thousands of national and international observers. Described as a stable democratic process in Cambodia and a free, fair and credible election.
"Through their vote, the Cambodian people have reaffirmed their desire for lasting peace, stability and sustainable development. "Of course, the free choice of the Cambodian people and the legitimate results of this election is not a subject to be questioned or debated." The Prime Minister emphasized.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that although the election was conducted in a good way, there are still some international circles who try to interfere in the internal affairs of Cambodia still do not see the good. Of this election.
