150 Japanese companies interested in investing in Cambodia after looking at economic potential and political stability (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): After looking at Cambodia's progress in terms of politics, security, order and economic growth. A total of 150 Japanese are interested in partnering with Cambodian companies in a number of areas to expand further development between the two countries' business community.
Tycoon Yin Sovanny said that the current meeting with foreign investment companies is a testament to the security, political stability and continuous development of Cambodia under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has built the country from scratch and has a policy of encouraging private sector and favorable investment, makes Cambodia an important destination for investment.
Mr. Yin Sovanny continued that Japan, the world's third largest economy, recently supported the 6th parliamentary election and sent many investment companies to invest in Cambodia. Today, 150 companies to further clarify that Cambodia is a country with great potential for investment in all sectors.
Mr. Oknha Yin Sovanny stated that among the above 150 companies, there are 3 main companies, including: 1: Agriculture, 2: Tourism and 3: Transportation.
Mr. SHOJI YUSUNOKI stated that Japan and Cambodia have a deep relationship with each other. Therefore, for today, representatives of 150 Japanese companies have arrived in Cambodia, and all Japanese investors are also very interested in investing in Cambodia.
Please be informed that after Cambodia held the 6th National Assembly Election 2018, it ended with transparency and fairness, with national and international observers participating in the process of observing and inspecting the votes that the victory went to the CPP. All 125 Cambodians in the National Assembly saw that many foreign companies have come to invest in Cambodia more than before and are not as worried as in previous mandates.
