This regulation was made when the governor chaired the meeting of the Provincial State Land Management Committee on September 28, 2018. The meeting was attended by leaders from relevant institutions, municipal authorities, district chiefs, commune chiefs at Kampot Provincial Hall.
The governor of Chiao Tai province said that the relevant departments, units and authorities must take action and identify those behind the encroachment on state public lands as their property, such as canals, lakes, canals, forests and so on. Notify or make a contract to stop the action immediately and if the person remains stubborn, legal action must be taken.
"The provincial administration must do this because now the law-abiding people are still obeying and the abusers are still abusing, and today there are more violators of the land-related issues than the law-abiding people," he said.
With this, the provincial governor also warned all government officials to work together and find out who is right between those who break the law.
