(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, in the morning of September 28, 2018, led a team to distribute rice seeds to 336 families in Pdao Chum Lech village, Pdao Chum commune, Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province. 40 kg of rice seeds.
On that occasion, the provincial governor said that during this year's flood season, the people who were inundated the most were the people in Koh Sotin district, but they only damaged more than 4 hectares of rice because they were affected by the floods. Last year, they did not plant rice before the season.
In particular, people living in districts far from the river, although not flooded, but flooded many acres of rice, such as Cheung Prey, damaged more than 200 hectares of rice, and therefore when the authorities The province has considered distributing rice seeds so that people can continue to grow and grow crops.
The provincial governor said that when the water was flooding, the provincial authorities considered distributing emergency aid to the people living along the river, but when the district water, the provincial authorities brought rice seeds to distribute to those living far away from the river.
Mr. Kim Savoeun, Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that this year's floods affected a total of 7,914 hectares of rice fields, of which 6,407 hectares were irreversible. 6,392 ha and affected 8,039 farmers.
