Break the law! Although the district governor and director of the Department of Land Management issued several letters suspending construction, the owner of a gas station in Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province, continued to build.
(Kampong Cham): The owner of a gas station in Dai Buon village, Chrey Vien commune, Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province, has started the construction process without permission. Despite the ban from the Prey Chhor district governor, the owner continues to build aggressively. Do not intimidate the local authorities at all.
Regarding the above case, Mr. Lor Chanly, Governor of Prey Chhor District, told Fresh News on the afternoon of September 28, 2018 that the construction owner had initially applied until the Cadastral Officer came to inspect. With the district authority. The land department then told the district authorities that the gas station could not be built because there was already an old one at that point.
Experts also recommend that new stations be allowed to be built only if there is a distance of 200 meters or more, so for the new station is opposite to the old station, that is, professional officials are not allowed to build.
The district governor said that he had previously issued three prohibition letters. Moreover, when the district officials took the letter to ban the construction owner did not accept, but the construction was suspended for 4 to 5 days and then resumed the construction process. After notifying all the procedures, the governor sent a letter to the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Kampong Cham for further action.
On the same day, Mr. Thuon Chetha, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Kampong Cham Province, also said that he had issued a letter banning the construction owner and had already invited the construction owner to make a contract for him to dismantle the building. However, construction was not allowed to continue.
The director of the department also confirmed that the problem of construction of illegal gas stations is under the action of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Kampong Cham province in accordance with the procedures of professional officials.
Mr. Lor Chanly, Governor of Prey Chhor District, said that in the case of illegal construction, as mentioned above, if the ban is not revoked, the competent authorities can lead the commission to confiscate the construction materials and store them for a while, and if the case is serious, the construction will be destroyed. The building was demolished with the permission of the court through the provincial cadastral officer.
