Iraq Expresses Satisfaction, Appreciation of CMAC Demining Training
(Phnom Penh): While attending demining training in Cambodia, many officials of the Iraqi Mine Action Agency expressed their satisfaction and appreciation to the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) for its training capabilities. Demining skills and unexploded ordnance.
This training program is supported by the Government of Japan through the International Cooperation Agency (JICA) provided to the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Iraq through the South-South International Cooperation Cooperation Project. The project lasts for 4 years, starting from 2016 until 2020, with 7 phases. In that, CMAC has already organized 3 episodes.
According to Fresh News on September 28, 2018, CMAC officials said that there are more than 70 professional officers of the Iraqi Mine Action Agency, including leaders and key officials in the field. Mines from the main ministries of Europe include: Ministry of Interior, Ministry of Health and Environment.
He added that during the demining training in Cambodia, the Iraqi Mine Action Agency (JICA) officials expressed their happiness and gratitude to the International Cooperation Agency (JICA) for recruiting officers. Cambodian skills with high ability and clear skills to train them.
