"Marie Stopes" Director: Every year, more than 5,000 young women around the world die from unplanned pregnancies.
The event aims to raise awareness of women's rights to access information related to safe reproductive health options and services if they decide to terminate their pregnancy.
According to a press release from Marie Stopes in Cambodia, abortion has been legal since 1997. However, many women still misunderstand that abortion is illegal. This is because they receive insufficient information as well as social discrimination, which results in women deciding to seek unsafe services.
Lack of awareness about the legal right to abortion can lead to delays in seeking health care and may lead to unsafe abortion. This "right to choose" event will provide important information for solutions to women's problems, so in the future only a few women will face this fear alone.
"We want all women in Cambodia to live a beautiful life according to their choices and let them know that they can contact Marie Stopes if they need help, information or support. " This is the emphasis of the director of "Marie Stopes International" in Cambodia.
