(China): A sari plantation in northern China's Shanxi Province is the largest yulu sari farm in China. Farmers here have developed new ways to market their fruits so that they can sell more throughout China.
Thanks to new technologies and online marketing methods, the price of sari grown here has increased three to four times compared to a few weeks ago as the Lunar New Year approached. Arrived last Monday.
The Xixian area of Shaanxi Province is a favorable place for growing sari because it has enough sunlight and the temperature fluctuates significantly during the day and night, combined with the soil rich in organic matter.
However, the area is prone to droughts and snowstorms, so farmers here have to use a variety of micro-temperature monitors to monitor the weather and maintain the temperature as needed. For example, they can use this tool to make artificial milk.
The sari grown here is known for its good shape and delicious taste, and it has become more popular in recent years due to its popularity through online shopping channels.
