Supreme Advisory Council opens the first internal meeting chaired by Mr. Nhek Bun Chhay
(Phnom Penh): The Supreme Advisory Council established in the new Royal Government met for the first time on September 27, 2018 under the chairmanship of Mr. Nhek Bun Chhay, President of the Khmer Rouge Party. National unity.
In this morning's meeting, representatives of political parties also raised various topics to discuss the understanding between the composition of 15 parties. In addition, they also support each other's activities.
The first meeting took place after some members of the Supreme Advisory Council had already visited in the past. Mr. Pich Sros, President of the most prominent Cambodian Youth Party, raised the issue of land disputes in Kandal province and the implementation of some basic work of sub-national officials in the first meeting on 27 September. This.
Mr. Pich Sros told Fresh News that the reason for the discussion came after he himself was not welcomed by the authorities during his recent visit to the victims in Kandal province. . Regarding the implementation of sub-national officials, the whole meeting is looking for ways to bring the authorities and members of the Supreme Advisory Council to a consensus.
Mr. Pich Sros said that while finding solutions, the members of the Advisory Council also announced their support for each other's activities, while some members have already done their job.
At the same time, Mr. Kong Monika, son of Mr. Kong Koam and President of the Khmer Will Party, also confirmed to Fresh News that in this first meeting, he asked the Ministry of Economy and Finance to provide standards related to the preparation. Draft the 2019 National Budget Law to the Supreme Council for review on this draft law to the Council of Ministers for the basis of suggestions for improvement in the shortcomings.
Mr. Kong Monika said that at the same time, he also raised various issues related to the administrative technical issues of the Supreme Council and consult and advise.
Please note that once a month, the members of the Advisory Council must meet before proposing to the head of government, Prime Minister Hun Sen. The head of government will meet with members of the 15-party Supreme Council every six months. This is based on the Royal Decree of the King.
