UNICEF President Kobora Komini stated that the organization's success in helping Cambodian children is due to the cooperation of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the direct implementation of the leadership and officials of all departments of the Ministry of Social Affairs.
In response, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, thanked Ms. Kobora Komini, UNICEF Country Director for Cambodia and all the working groups who have been assisting Cambodia during their tenure. The Minister added that although she has ended her tenure as UNICEF Country Director for Cambodia, the Ministry of Social Affairs and UNICEF still have many new tasks that require us to continue our efforts.
Minister Vong Soth added that Cambodia has reached a stage where it is required that the social sector play an increasingly important role to serve the people, especially the vulnerable and vulnerable. Therefore, we, including all government officials, are ready and ready to serve the people.
At the same time, Ms. Kobora Komini, President of UNICEF, thanked Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, for his successful work with the organization in the past. Ms. Kobora Komini said that UNICEF continues to support and assist both old and new children.
On that occasion, Mr. Vong Soth affirmed that the Ministry of Social Affairs has taken active steps in implementing the policy on the social security system and the national strategic development plan to help all kinds of victims and vulnerable in society, in particular. On children.
Mr. Vong Soth added that the Ministry of Social Affairs has cooperated with UNICEF to study the achievements and challenges faced by children in the community in order to shape the child welfare sector in Cambodia in line with the government's national strategic development plan and political program. Japan continues to assist Cambodia in implementing the project to improve occupational health and safety in the construction sector 2018-2020
(Phnom Penh): The Japanese Parliament in charge of the activities of the International Labor Organization in the field of occupational health and safety has agreed to assist Cambodia in implementing the second project on the promotion of occupational health and safety in the construction sector in 2018-2020.
This strong will was expressed in a meeting between Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, and Mr. Jiro KAWASAKI, Member of Parliament and former Minister of Health, Labor and Welfare of Japan and the Japanese Parliamentary Delegation in charge of International Labor Organization activities. Occupational health and safety on September 27, 2018 at the Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Leng Tong, Director of the Department of Labor Medicine, said that Minister Ith Sam Heng also praised the Japanese investors who came to invest in Cambodia and all Japanese companies are in compliance with the law and good working conditions.
Mr. Leng Tong said that the Japanese side thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Ministry of Labor for providing good cooperation and the Japanese side will continue to support the implementation of this second project to achieve the expectations of Project.
The main objectives of the second project on improving occupational health and safety in the construction sector 2018-2020 include:
1: Continue to implement the second project on improving occupational health and safety standards in the construction sector 2018-2020, using the project consulting working group mechanism and other mechanisms to achieve project expectations.
2: Development of additional legal framework and legal standards related to occupational health and safety, especially in the construction sector.
3. Strengthening labor inspections to improve working conditions at construction sites.
4: Raise the awareness of workers and employers through the organization of various training courses, such as programs to improve working conditions for small construction sites, programs to improve working conditions for small and medium enterprises.
Mr. Leng Tong added that tomorrow, both sides will visit the actual construction site to check the progress made in the past.
