(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Hil Raya, Governor of Serey Sophorn Municipality, in the morning of September 27, 2018, held a meeting of the Municipal Administrative Unity Command with the participation of the Deputy Governor, Municipal Council, City Hall officials, law enforcement forces, local authorities, villages and communes. And some other stakeholders in Serei Sophorn City Hall.
Mr. Hul Raya said that the relevant officials will take action against the landowners who split the plots for sale without asking for permission. The Ministry of Land Management has also warned to take legal action against the sellers of plots in case of sale Air lot or sale of unregistered land.
Mr. Serey Sophorn Mayor confirmed that in the past, landowners in Serey Sophorn City were worried about the sale of land and did not receive the full payment, but the traders who bought the land to split the resale for profit. Requested the law properly, resulting in a series of lawsuits.
He said that in principle, the land law gives ownership and the Royal Government has set up a registration system, first: there is a systematic registration, then the goal is to implement throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia, and second: separate registration. The mayor said that people must check before buying land that the land is really registered and is the land of those who actually sold or not?
In this regard, Mr. Hul Raya has assigned subordinates to conduct regular inspections and list the names of all legal and unlicensed plots in the city so that unlicensed plots owners can apply for a permit. Properly, otherwise the authorities will take legal action.
He pointed out that after the development of the real estate sector, especially the division of plots of land for sale, these points have caused great concern by the authorities, as some of the plots of land for sale are legal and some are not legally licensed. . In Banteay Meanchey province, especially in Serei Sophorn city, there are more than 40 locations for sale.
