Takeo-Yeay Keo Statue Renovated by Takeo Provincial Authorities at a Cost of More Than 30,000 USD
(Takeo): The Takeo-Yeay Keo statue, located in Rokar Krao Sangkat, Daun Keo City, in front of the dilapidated Takeo Market bus lane, was cleared by the Takeo Provincial Authority on the morning of September 27, 2018. Ask the owner of the water, the owner of the land to change the location and repair the statue of Takeo Yeay Keo.
Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province, stated that there was no construction of the new Takeo-Yeay Keo statue, the authorities only repaired the dilapidated old statue and set up a garden to improve the aesthetics of the statue. Samples only.
He continued that today, there are people and traders who are not very orderly at the place where the statue of Takeo-Yeay Keo is lost, which makes it difficult for people to come and worship the statue of Takeo-Yeay Keo. As the provincial authority, prepare to repair and renovate again.
As for the budget for the construction of the park and the repair of the Takeo-Yeay Keo statue, Mr. Ouch Phea claimed that the authorities did not use the national budget. The project's funding comes from fundraisers in the province and philanthropists, raising more than $ 30,000 for a project to build a park and renovate the Takeo Yeay Keo statue.
According to the Governor of Takeo Province, in the project to repair and relocate the Takeo-Yeay Keo statue, there is a lot of support from the people of Takeo Province by posting support on the social networking site Facebook.
In addition, the relocation is to make it easier for people to travel and make it easier for people to worship the statue.
Be careful! Two miners seriously injured in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): Considered one in a million accidents, three people survived a massive mine explosion while driving a bulldozer to the farm. This incident happened at 3:30 on September 26, 2018 at Veal Cheas point in Sen Tech village, Moratok commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
According to the district inspector, the three people affected by the mine explosion were: Tith Rithy, male, 43 years old, living in Kulen village, Kulen commune, Kulen district, slightly injured, and Kem Sopheaktra, male, 33 years old. Phoeun Sopheap, a 30-year-old man from Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province, was slightly injured.
In connection with the Minton explosion, the district inspector concluded that it may have been caused by a bulldozer hit by Minton's flowers. He said that if the floor is wrong, even if the floor is in another place, it will not explode. However, he said that this is one in a million accidents that victims can survive this horrific incident.
Mountain Crocodile Trapped in Pursat Province's Meteuk River Released
It should be noted that on the morning of September 25, 2018, in Stung Meteuk, Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary in Kandal Village, Thmor Da Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province, a man was shocked and terrified after seeing a crocodile. A large mountain next to his net that caught fish in the river.
Currently, this crocodile has been released into Stung Chhay Tamet (Stung Meteuk) in Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary and provided $ 600 in incentive money to the people who caught it, including the budget of Pursat Fisheries Administration District 20. Ten thousand riels, the budget of the governor of Veal Veng district, 100,000 riels, the budget of the 825th Border Guard Battalion, 100,000 riels and the Chinese company $ 500.
The National Police General Commission calls on private security companies and enterprises to look at their profiles carefully before recruiting security agents, lest they be harmed by the staff.
(Phnom Penh): The Director of the Private Security Management Department of the General Commission of the National Police, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, appealed to all security companies, enterprises and establishments before recruiting security agents to check their profiles for fear of retaliation. Accidents due to employees committing illegal acts and so on.
The appeal message of the Director of the Private Security Management Department, who is the staff of the General Commission of the National Police, was made this morning, September 27, 2018, on the occasion of the opening of the 7th training course for private security agents after the approval of General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey said, "I would like to call on all private security providers, enterprises and establishments to carefully review the background information of each employee before deciding to recruit for fear. "Touching employees with a bad background is a danger to the company."
According to the director of the department, some crooks have taken refuge under the label of private security, committing crimes directly and conspiring with criminals to commit crimes, causing risks to important and vulnerable targets. The worst in private institutions with private security agencies, although most companies are well managed, also suffered by some security personnel.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey also pointed out that the Department of Private Security Management recently investigated and cracked down on eight private security agents who used illegal weapons disguised as national police and soldiers stationed at banks and institutions. Some.
He stressed that private security agencies have no right to use explosive weapons and that private security companies, services and enterprises are not allowed to use the armed forces (police, military police, soldiers) who have not yet retired. Its purpose without a letter or without permission from the relevant unit.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey advised and urged all private security companies to send their agents to participate in training courses for private security agents so that their agents gain experience and knowledge to increase More authority.
Please be informed that in the past, the Department of Private Security Management has already conducted 6 training courses for private security agents, noting that the private security agents who have been trained and studied, they clearly understand the role. Duties and participation in maintaining security, safety, public order, as well as understanding the law and clear ethics.
