Telecommunication Infrastructure Service Provider Opens New Office in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): IDC Cambodia, a leading company in providing telecommunication infrastructure services, has officially opened its new office in the center of Phnom Penh.
The move to a larger, more central location now reflects the progress of the company's operations in Cambodia, as well as the one-step development. New that will make this company can serve its customers better to another level.
The new office is located in Keystone Building, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh. The brand new office with a capacity of 60 employees will be a great place to work for the whole Edith Cambodia staff.
This change will enable the ITC Cambodia team to better serve and support existing and new customers in the short term as more people are operating in the heart of Phnom Penh.
Through our new strategic location in the heart of Phnom Penh, we will be able to easily communicate with our clients and also provide them with quality services and support. High and timely too.
We are committed to continuing to provide end-to-end solutions to our clients and strive to improve connectivity across the country. This is further emphasized by the Regional Director of Marketing Expansion of edotco Group.
Please be informed that EDC Co., Ltd. has been operating in Cambodia since 2013. The company's portfolio has been growing steadily. To date, IDC has more than 3,550 towers and more than 2,250 towers are directly operated and operated by IDC.
In addition, IDC also provides management services for an additional 1,300 antenna towers. The towers that IDC directly controls account for about 25% of the total number of towers in Cambodia.
