The following is a statement from the Khmer Rouge tribunal: Venezuela strongly condemns and calls Tram's statement "interference and war-mongering" (Video inside) (Caracas): Venezuela fully condemns On US President Donald Trump's interfering and war-hungry statement. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua in the morning of Thursday, September 27, 2018.
The Venezuelan Foreign Ministry has said that a recent statement by Donald Trump was intended to provoke a military uprising in the Latin American country. Karachi's condemnation comes after Trump said the administration of Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro could be overthrown very quickly and easily if military forces choose to do so.
In addition, the US President stated that he was open to meeting with Maduro with all the options on the table, while there were both strong and weak options, and Trump said that everyone knows. And what he means by that strong choice.
Last year, Trump said the option of using military force in Venezuela could not be overlooked if necessary, despite his top officials objecting. In the past, Washington has also imposed a series of sanctions against the Venezuelan government since then.
The South American oil country has been suffering from a severe economic crisis since crude oil prices plunged into international markets. As of August, the United Nations said 2.3 million people had fled Venezuela, mostly to Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Brazil.
