Minister of Commerce: Boao Forum for Asia is an opportunity for Cambodia to attract investors and strengthen ties with regional countries
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, expressed his belief that the Boao Forum for Asia will provide a great opportunity for Cambodia to attract more investors from China and a bridge to connect with countries in the region to strengthen. Economic cooperation and address the challenges the world is facing.
The Minister expressed his belief on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the Boa Forum for the Asia-Phnom Penh Conference under the theme "Together for Development and Win-Win: Working Together to Bring Economic and Trade Cooperation Sino-Cambodian work in the new era "organized by Sofitel Phnom Penh Phokitra Hotel on the night of September 26, 2018.
On that occasion, Minister Pan Sosak outlined the common purpose of the Boao Forum for Asia and the new initiative of Chinese President Xi Jinping, which proposed to expand all-round cooperation between countries in Asia. It will be a new and huge opportunity for Cambodia and other member countries.
He noted that among the 29 countries that have agreed to establish the Boa Forum for Asia, Cambodia is one of the beneficiaries of the "One Belt One Road" project and one of the fastest growing economies in the world. Most in Asia.
He also called on representatives of the Cambodian private sector and Chinese enterprises and companies, as well as member countries of the Boao Forum, to use the opportunity to meet today to continue the culture of dialogue and sharing, as well as to strengthen and expand cooperation for the benefit of all. Common interests in the region as well as globally.
The forum was officially launched on February 27, 2001 and provided an opportunity for heads of government, industry and business leaders and intellectuals in Asia and beyond to engage in dialogue to strengthen cooperation. Joint development through regional and global economic integration
