In order to keep up with the 4th generation industrial revolution, the Federation of Employers' Associations has already determined its work activities
(Phnom Penh): As the world is sinking into another new evolution, the fourth industrial revolution, Cambodia is also a country that is developing to keep up with this global change, so in the meeting Third, the Board of Directors of the Federation of Investors has already set its strategic direction to implement the work in line with the fourth generation industrial revolution or digitalization.
The 3rd Ordinary Meeting of the Board of Directors of the Federation of Investors was held under the chairmanship of Mr. Suon Rindy, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association on the afternoon of September 26, 2018 at the High Sky Hotel in Chroy Changva.
Dr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Federation of Investors' Associations, said after the meeting that the Board of Directors of the Federation of Investors Federation summarized the results of the work achieved in the past and discussed and consulted. Some of the work between the management and the members of the special association is to determine the direction of the work to be carried out in the future.
Dr. Ley Sopheap stated that these work directions are in line with the policy as well as the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is bringing progress for the nation as well as the prestige and cooperation on the international stage by the association. The Federation of Investors focuses on investment and the economy, which is one of the most important parts for the nation's development.
Mr. Suon Rindy said that the Federation of Investors Association has identified some necessary work strategies related to a new global development that the world has just experienced, namely the fourth generation industrial revolution, which is almost entirely related. On the "digitalization" system, while the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister is also paying close attention to this issue.
Mr. Suon Rindy said that since the relationship between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the People's Republic of China has reached a comprehensive cooperation and partnership, the Association of Investors Federation has also considered this matter carefully. Also incorporated into its strategy and action plan.
According to Mr. Suon Rindy, what is more special is that the Association of Investors Federation also supports the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen wisely, while Cambodia and the people across The country is achieving complete peace and stability, which is the most important factor for the development of the whole nation.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng calls on the public to drive respectfully on the occasion of Pchum Ben (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee, on September 26. This issued a call on the prevention and control of road traffic accidents in the sense of urging the public to drive in accordance with the law during the upcoming Kan Ben and Pchum Ben ceremonies.
According to the appeal of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, in order to prevent and prevent road traffic accidents on the occasion of Pchum Ben, the National Road Safety Committee would like to appeal to the public as road users to follow the following instructions:
1: Check the technical characteristics of the vehicle before departure, especially check the steering wheel, brakes, lighting, etc.
2: Please do not load passengers or goods on the rules. For passenger cars or workers not to be allowed to ride on the roof, do not increase the fare on that occasion.
3: Always wear a helmet when traveling on a motorcycle or tricycle.
4: Always wear a seat belt.
5: Must respect the right of way, respect traffic signs and always right.
6: Do not drive faster than the speed limit.
7: Do not drive under the influence of alcohol.
8: Do not bend or overtake in a situation of risk or negligence.
9: Do not drive in a drowsy state.
10: Must drive in a spirit of caution, morality, understanding and tolerance.
The following is the appeal of Prince Sar Kheng:
