CDX Governor Attends Real Estate Appraisers Association Workshop and Shares Investment Experience
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Derivatives Exchange (CDX) participates in a workshop organized by the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors in response to its desire to promote investment development throughout Cambodia. .
The workshop was also attended by experts and investors from the real estate and financial sectors and will be held on September 25, 2018 at the Cambodia-Korea Cooperation Center.
Lawrence highlighted the growth of investment in Cambodia. He urged investors to diversify their investment products to reduce risks, protect capital and avoid relying on a single source of income, which will allow investors to have more choices and invest with confidence.
Mr. Lawrence thanked the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors for inviting him as a speaker, as well as the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding, which provides both sides with a way to jointly promote public investment education. Across the country.
Both sides look forward to working with CDX and the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors to establish more frequent forums, workshops and training sessions. CDX's participation in the workshop fully fulfilled its commitment to the Memorandum of Understanding and strengthened the relationship between the two institutions, marking the beginning of a bright future for the general investment sector in Cambodia.
