This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a delegation to attend the 73rd General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly in New York.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, September 27, led a high-level Cambodian delegation to attend the 73rd General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly and other relevant meetings. 4 days from September 27, 2018 to September 30 in New York City, USA.
The UN General Assembly is held under the theme "Making the United Nations relevant to all people: global leadership and shared responsibility for a peaceful, equitable and sustainable society." .
According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, the high-level delegation accompanying Samdech Techo Hun Sen included: Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs and other dignitaries. Some more.
In New York, the Prime Minister will make a statement focusing on recent developments and key achievements of the Royal Government and regional and international issues of common concern.
During his stay in New York, the Prime Minister will also meet with the Cambodian community living in the United States and Canada. At the ministerial level, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon will hold a series of bilateral talks with his counterparts from Australia, Canada, Georgia, Estonia, Hungary, Serbia and senior US State Department officials, the United States Department of State, the United Kingdom and other countries. More.
The Deputy Prime Minister will also sign with the Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Armenia Zohrab Mnatsakanyan a Memorandum of Understanding on the Establishment of Bilateral Consultations between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Armenia.
The Cambodian delegation will also attend the Informal ASEAN Foreign Ministers 'Meeting (IAMM), the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting with the President of the United Nations General Assembly and the Secretary-General of the United Nations (AUMM), and the Ministerial Meeting on Non-Aligned Movement. Parties, ministerial meetings of the least developed countries, the 77-nation group of China and China, and more.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has also stated that the General Assembly is also important for Cambodia because Cambodia is the Vice President of the General Assembly.
It should be noted that Cambodia, under the leadership of the Head of State, His Majesty Norodom Sihanouk, applied for membership in the United Nations during 1952, one year before Cambodia gained independence from France. After three years of Cambodian proposals, on December 14, 1955, Cambodia became a member of the United Nations.
