Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks South Korea to help rebuild the road to Koh Kong and help buy Cambodian agricultural products
(Hanoi, Vietnam): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has asked the South Korean government to speed up the reconstruction of National Road 48 from Sre Ambel district to the provincial town of Koh Kong, which was severely damaged by floods. He also proposed to examine the ability to buy and import more Cambodian agricultural products to South Korea.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's request was made during a working meeting with South Korean Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong in Hanoi, Vietnam on the afternoon of September 26, 2018.
During the meeting, the Prime Ministers of the two countries also recalled the excellent development of relations between the two countries, which was initiated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen over the past 21 years. The Prime Minister thanked all the support of the Republic of Korea in the rehabilitation and socio-economic development of Cambodia, especially the acceptance of Cambodian workers to work in the Republic of Korea, which so far has about 60,000. People.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his support for the celebration of the ASEAN-ROK relations, which is scheduled to be held in 2019 in the Republic of Korea. The Prime Minister also wants the Mekong-Republic of Korea forum to be a forum for top leaders, as the Mekong countries have done with Japan and China.
The Prime Minister of the Republic of Korea, Lee Nak-yeon, thanked Samdech Techo for supporting the upcoming ASEAN-ROK Anniversary 2019 in South Korea. The Prime Minister also asked Samdech Techo to help mobilize other ASEAN leaders to make the summit a reality.
Prime Minister Lee Nak-yeon also praised the promotion of the Mekong-ROK Summit and thanked Samdech Techo for facilitating ASEAN-ROK relations in the past.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Ly Nak Yon respectfully invited each other to visit their respective countries.
