Currently, the arrested suspects are being reported to the Chak Angre police station for questioning to search for the other two fugitives and bring them to justice. China Releases Third Report on One Belt One Road Initiative (Video inside)
The China State Information Center has released its third major data report on the One Belt One Road initiative during the annual Davos Summer Summit.
The annual report, first released in 2016, is compiled from data collected using big data technology. This year's report shows that the One Belt One Road infrastructure project has made great strides in China and in the countries participating in the project.
Since the One Belt One Road Initiative was proposed in 2013, progress has been made in policy-making, connectivity, infrastructure connectivity, trade flows, funding and exchanges, the report said. Come between people and people.
Over the past five years, the expansion of the initiative's "friendship circle" has enabled more than 100 countries in Asia, Africa and Latin America to take part in the initiative, the report added.
As the initiative progresses, Russia has become China's largest partner for three consecutive years, according to the report.
"Our cooperation on investment and trade with the countries participating in the One Belt One Road initiative is growing," said Chheng Xiaopor, director of the China State Information Center. In addition, some provinces and cities in China are also increasingly involved in the implementation of the One-Way Belt Initiative. "These factors indicate that China's level of market openness is increasing."
The report was compiled using 50,000 million pieces of data from various sectors such as online commentary, trade and cross-border e-commerce, and collected from 71 countries participating in the initiative. From the administrative units in 31 provinces of China and more than 1,000 consulting institutions and 2,400 media institutions.
This year, the report, for the first time, included a number of indicators measuring the investment climate and ease of digital network business of the Silk Road, which aims to promote mutual cultural exchanges between participating countries. (China's CCTV)
