TOP NEWS: Cambodia issues statement welcoming the outcome of the historic and successful summit between the two Korean leaders
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on September 26, 2018, issued a statement welcoming the outcome of the historic and successful summit between the two Korean leaders yesterday. September 18-20, 2018 in Pyongyang, North Korea.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated: "The Royal Government of Cambodia welcomes the outcome of the historic and successful Inter-Korean Summit held on September 18-20, 2018 in Pyongyang, especially the declaration Together, Pyongyang is another important step towards national reconciliation, lasting peace, win-win cooperation and common prosperity on the Korean Peninsula.
"The Kingdom of Cambodia fully supports the resumption of constructive dialogue that will lead to the achievement of complete denuclearization, lasting peace and peaceful reunification of the two Koreas," the Foreign Ministry said.
The announcement of the outcome of the summit between the two Korean leaders, Cambodia, was made immediately after a meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and new South Korean Prime Minister Lee Nak-yeon in Hanoi. Vietnam on the afternoon of September 26, 2018, during the two leaders' visit to pay tribute to the late President Tran Dai Quang.
