Thundra car crashes into motorcycle, killing man while rushed to hospital
(Preah Vihear): A man drove a Tundra car at high speed while arriving at the scene at a bend in the road, not yet oversteered and hit another motorbike that was crossing the road, causing a man to die. After being sent to the hospital on January 16.
This incident happened on the evening of September 25, 2018 along National Road No. 62 between km 112-113 in Kraing Dong village, Preah Khleang commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province.
Lieutenant Colonel Ruon Yet, Police Inspector of Tbeng Meanchey District, said this morning, September 26, 2018, that the victim was Khan Nhor, a 36-year-old male resident of the above-mentioned commune village, who died at 4:00 AM. September 26, 2018 at the January 16 Referral Hospital.
The district inspector said that before the accident, the car was driving in a south-to-north direction at high speed. While the victim was riding a motorcycle across the road from the right hand side to the south after the incident, the driver escaped and the victim was sent to the hospital.
