Cambodia-China allies promise to continue the 2019 Dragon Exercise to be bigger and more successful in the military field
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian and Chinese sides have pledged to continue the Dragon Exercise in 2019 to be bigger and more successful in the military field, while the specific time and place are still under discussion. This is according to General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander and Joint Chief of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The special colonel also praised the leadership of the Chinese People's Liberation Army for successfully conducting the 2016 and 2018 Golden Dragon exercises.
In particular, General Ith Sarath and Party Chi also promised to continue the Dragon Exercise 2019 to be bigger and more successful in the military.
After that, the two sides discussed the purpose of the joint exercise "Golden Dragon 2019", with both sides decided to set up a working group to discuss the topic, place and time of the exercise.
Cambodia-UN launches second phase of youth training focused on entrepreneurship
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training together with the United Nations (UN) has convened the third board meeting of the United Nations Joint Program "Together for the Career and Work of Youth in Cambodia" to Summarize the work implemented in the first phase of the program after the project has been implemented for two years and approve the second phase action plan for the next year.
The third meeting of the Board of Directors was held in the presence of Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Ms. Pauline Tamesis, United Nations Resident Coordinator in Cambodia on the afternoon of September 25, 2018 at the Ministry of Labor.
According to the Minister, the Joint Program for Youth Careers and Employment in Cambodia for the second phase focuses on the development of youth entrepreneurship and the development of modern professional skills and the fourth generation industrial revolution, expanding the system training. Information technology reaches young people, especially young people, the target group is vulnerable and poor youth.
In addition, the second phase of the program also focuses on the development of education and training in factories, especially to promote the reduction of literacy for workers and life skills in educational institutions, as well as in vocational training bases of the Ministry of Labor. .
He said that the United Nations Assistance to Cambodia for this project is in line with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia and in line with the United Nations Millennium Development Goals, also in line with some of Cambodia's policies, including National policy on industrial development, national policy on employment and employment, national policy on technical and vocational education, national policy on education and youth.
In addition, the United Nations would like to promote its policies in line with Cambodia's policies, which are beneficial to the development and training of Cambodian youth, to create opportunities for youth and to build the capacity of institutions to carry out all of these tasks. Ability to continue management throughout the country.
