The Ambassador emphasized that the Chinese assistance will now be a part of the Royal Government of Cambodia's census to run smoothly and successfully.
With the help of China, Senior Minister Chai Thorn expressed confidence that the large number of vehicles, motorcycles and census equipment would enable census officers to be able to manage, monitor, collect basic data, transport documents and process information. Typing computer data, copying census files, etc.
In addition, Senior Minister Chai Thorn also expressed his deep gratitude to China and the Chinese people, the Royal Government of the People's Republic of China, which has always supported Cambodia in its development in all fields.
These materials will not only be used for the census, but will also be used for other future censuses, such as agricultural development, the overall economic census, for the work of the entire national statistical system and for planning work. National and sub-national levels.
Please note that Cambodia will start the third census from March 3 to 13, 2019. The census is expected to employ up to 47,000 officials and cost about $ 8 million from the government. It is estimated that the population of Cambodia in 2019 could increase to 16 million.
Ministry of Interior Announces Capital-Provincial Census and Receives Census Aid
