Chinese emperor is taking even bigger steps to explore the moon!
BEIJING: China is planning to land as well as explore the South Pole and North Pole by 2030. This is according to the Chinese space agency CNSA quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday night, September 25, 2018.
China is currently planning four missions for the fourth phase of its lunar exploration mission. The lunar exploration program, named after the goddess of the moon Chang'e in Chinese mythology, began in 2003 and the first three stages of the space program include orbiting and landing on the moon. As well as bringing the specimen back to earth.
After all those missions, China is also building a scientific research station on the moon and planning to explore with robots as well as more people for the future, in addition to plans to build its own space station, which began in early 2020. .
