Senior Minister Kun Kim announces the inauguration of the President of the Phnom Penh Veterans Association, Lt. Gen. Thet, to replace the newly appointed General Chuon Sovann
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on September 25, 2018, announced the appointment of Lt. Gen. Thet as President of the Phnom Penh Veterans Association to replace General Chuon Son. Conversation and giving social security money cards to 6,288 members of Phnom Penh Veterans.
After the report of General Chuon Sovann, Senior Minister Kun Kim brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Association to all members and confirmed that with the care and consideration of Samdech Techo. Hun Sen, in particular, the implementation of the social protection policy that Samdech has announced in the previous election campaign, only today, members received a Social Security Fund for free medical treatment in hospitals.
In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his appreciation and thanks to the members of the Cambodian Veterans Association who went to the polls and voted for the CPP to get seats in the National Assembly to continue to lead the Royal Government in the sixth mandate.
According to the former Senior Minister, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Honorary President of the Phnom Penh Cambodian Veterans Association, on behalf of the President, decided to provide 200 houses to the needy veterans, now only 10 houses have been built. The district inspectors, who are the presidents of the associations at the district level, must inspect and submit proposals to solve the construction in a timely manner.
Before concluding, Senior Minister Kun Kim instructed the new President of the Phnom Penh Veterans Association to urge the leaders of the association at all levels to consider the well-being and well-being of its members.
The inauguration ceremony was attended by Mr. Seang Bunleang, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Ms. Hun Bunthoeun, Advisor to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs with the same status as Undersecretary of State and Deputy Chief of Finance Department, Senior Management Wingo's superiors, as well as distinguished guests from many countries, including: CEOs of various companies and lottery agents of many companies.
Mr. Seang Bunleang stated that in addition to the official operation of the company in Cambodia, Wingo Lottery will set up lottery sales agents in various provinces in Cambodia to make it easier for customers to buy lottery tickets and open lottery prizes at lottery agents. The closest.
He added that in addition to running the lottery business, Wingo will share some of the profits as a humanitarian and charitable fund to support the poor, the needy and the homeless everywhere without discrimination. He said that the reason why companies from other countries come to invest in Cambodia because Cambodia is a favorable country and continuous development.
"I sincerely hope that the company will provide confidence and get a lot of support from all Cambodian customers," he said. "Wingo Lottery aims to make every effort to improve the lives of its customers."
Please note that Wingo has already established a number of agents in Phnom Penh to provide convenience to customers can buy tickets and exchange prizes anywhere. In addition, the company has created four types of scratch cards with a grand prize of up to $ 10,000 to meet the needs of customers.
Today marks the 49th anniversary of the death of Prince Chuon Nath
(Phnom Penh): On September 25, 2018, this is the 49th anniversary of the death of Samdech Preah Mohasomethathipady Chuon Nath (Chot Nhano), Samdech Preah Sangkhareach, 1st Class of the Mahanikaya of the Kingdom of Cambodia Many of his works have been left to Khmer descendants to this day, including dictionaries.
Samdech Preah Sangha Reach Chuon Nath passed away on September 25, 1969 at the age of 86 at his residence in Wat Ounalom, Phnom Penh.
Please be informed that Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath was born on Tuesday, 11 Roch Phalkun, in the year of Vok Chhasak, BE 2427, which is on March 11, 1883. This is according to a document released by the National Language Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia. His hometown is Kamrieng village, Rokar Koh commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province. He has two siblings, himself and his younger brother, Oknha Mantry Chuon Nuth.
As a child, he studied national literature until he was 18 years old. He stayed there for two years before studying at Wat Ounalom, Phnom Penh.
At the age of 21, he was ordained as a monk and lived in Wat Por Prek, Kandal Stung District, Kandal Province in 2448 AD 1904. At that time, he received the name of the commandment of Chothanano.
In the field of education, he first began to study silk and the translation of the Dharma and the Dharma from the preacher Market, the Upachaya. Prince Chuon Nath learned in addition to the national language, he also learned Sanskrit Pali grammar, which at that time, between 1910, among Pali scholars, he was known as a Thera. Proficiency and proficiency in the Pali language.
He also learned many other languages, including Thai, Lao, French, English and Vietnamese. In the Buddhist era 2457 AD 1913, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath entered the sentence contest in the Uposatharatnaram Vihear Preah Keo Morakot for 4 sentences, which is the highest sentence in that period.
In 1915, he passed the second examination and was appointed a professor at the Senior Pali School, now called Suramarit Buddhist High School. In 2463, when he was a monk, Satha became an ordinary student and went to study Sanskrit and calligraphy at the French School of the Far East in Hanoi, Vietnam, with Louis Finot (l Finot). The Frenchman was the principal of that school.
A document released by the National Language Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia further confirms that Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath has performed many other duties as a member of the Khmer Dictionary Church, a member of the Church of Spelling in various books that the Pali School Highly published.
In addition, he served as a keynote speaker in the Khmer Primary Certificate Examination and the French-Khmer Higher Primary Diploma Examination in Phnom Penh.
In 1927, he was appointed a final member of the Church for the Library of Cambodia, now called the Buddhist Institute. He is also the Vice-Chancellor of the Senior Pali School and an Auxiliary Member of the Trinity Church.
On the other hand, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath was a member of the Congregation for the Study of Selection of Words in the Story of Ancient Khmer Poets in order to collect and transmit those words into the Khmer dictionary and was a member of the Congregation for the Examination of Books by the Ministry of National Education.
In the same document, it is stated that in 2478 AD 1935, he was a professor of Pali, Sanskrit, Khmer and Lao at the highest level of secondary school at Preah Sisowath High School in Phnom Penh. Samdech Preah Sangkhareach was appointed as the Chief Bishop of Wat Ounalom and presided over the Constituent Assembly, the senior church of the monks. In addition, he served as the Vice-Chairman of the Cultural Committee of the "A" section of the National Commission for Education.
In 1961, he chaired a literary interview broadcast on national radio every Friday. He is also the chairman of the Commission for the Examination of Articles on Khmer History and the Chairman of the Commission for the Examination and Determination of the Meaning of the Cambodian Flag.
Regarding his work abroad, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath led a delegation to visit Wat Khmer Kampuchea Krom and to Laos for a meeting of the Council of Buddhist Affairs there.
In 1943 he was appointed a correspondent member of the French School in the Far East. The prince also led a delegation to Sri Lanka and Burma to hold a parade there. There are still many overseas missions that Prince Chuon Nath has completed.
In 2507 AD 1963, he received the title of First Class Priest from Prince Norodom Sihanouk, Head of State of Cambodia. Then, in 1967, he received a full doctorate in literature from the Head of State on behalf of the Faculty of Letters and Humanities of the Royal University.
Prince Chuon Nath has built many decrees, both manuscripts and books, especially books translated from Pali into Khmer for Buddhists to study.
The books include: The Khmer Dictionary has two volumes and has been published several times to this day. There are two volumes of the Pali Grammar Book. Book of Practice, Book of Discipline, Patimokkha, Samvara, Summary of Poems, Dharma, etc.
Apart from this, he also composed the Pali Happiness, the 7th verse, as well as the translation for the Blessing of the King.
He has also written many other articles in the Buddhist magazine Kampuchea Sorya since 1926, and there are other dharma articles in the magazine Ponleu Buddhachak.
Another important thing to note is that Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath wrote the lyrics of the Nokor Reach song for the Khmer national anthem or the national anthem that has been left to this day. He also wrote hymns, hymns or dharma sutras.
All of his works, both nationally and morally, as stated above, to this day, those works are still held and highly appreciated by the Buddhist people. Khmer descendants from one generation to another. Because they see that all these works are important and useful in helping their studies, both secular and moral.
(Phnom Penh): After receiving overwhelming support from the people in the national election in late July, the Royal Government of Cambodia, the mandate continued to be led by the Cambodian People's Party, was officially born with the continuation of Roads to strengthen national unity.
Below is a video showing the journey of the new government of the Royal Government of Cambodia on the road to strengthen national unity: Borax was found to be sold at Dey Huy Market, Camcontrol officials of Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone confiscated and destroyed
(Phnom Penh): In order to protect the interests of consumers and participate in preventing the impact on health, which is a common concern of consumers, this morning, September 25, 2018, CamControl Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Branch in cooperation with the Department of Commerce and the Board. Market workers continued to inspect the quality of food at Dey Huy Market in Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
During the inspection, 17 samples of food items were inspected, including: frozen squid, frozen shrimp, prawns, dried fish, beef meatballs, beef meatballs, pork blood, noodles, blueberries, desserts, bean curd, and soybeans. Cooked ginger, grapes, cabbage, etc. Selected branches for preliminary analysis on site using test kit.
As a result, 16 food samples were analyzed for safety compliance.
The seller and also the manufacturer (minor production) admitted that they had added the banned chemical and were instructed by the branch to immediately stop production by adding the banned chemical. In case of non-recidivism, legal action will be taken.
For buyers, CamControl officials also advised on how to choose safe products to eat and advised buyers to consider before deciding to buy, especially unusual products such as beautiful, attractive. Etc.
At the same time, the CamControl officer of Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone also monitored the price of gasoline and diesel at various gas stations in Sen Sok district, which is in line with the notification of the Ministry of Commerce No. 3355 dated 17 September 2018, with regular petrol not exceeding R4,150 per liter and diesel no more than R4,000 per liter.
