(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, on September 25, 2018, expressed his hope and confidence that the delegation of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship will be successful for the country after returning from the "Ship" program. The 45th Southeast Asian Youth and Japan SSEAYP ”in Japan, Brunei, the Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam, especially to strengthen, expand and promote Cambodia's prestige on the international stage.
This warning and encouragement was made on the occasion that the President of the National Assembly allowed the youth delegation led by Mr. Srang Kimly, President of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association to pay a courtesy call and ask for advice and wisdom before leaving. The above application. This program lasts for 52 days from October 23 to December 12, 2018.
The President of the National Assembly said that participating in the Southeast Asia and Japan Youth Ship Program is a special opportunity for Cambodian youth to strengthen and expand friendly relations and mutual understanding between ASEAN youth and with Japan. Must study and understand the history of their country and other countries to facilitate the implementation of work and interpret for young people traveling.
Please be informed that 29 young Cambodians will participate in the 45th Southeast Asian Youth Ship Program from October 23 to December 12, 2018.
Mr. Srean Kimly emphasized that at that time, young people will have to share the art and culture of each country. Accommodation with Dharma parents, and when the ship program crosses any country, the youth delegation will also pay a courtesy call on the country's leaders.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin remarked, "You must strive to learn more about general knowledge related to regional and international institutions to which Cambodia is a member, such as the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPA) and other international organizations. "Including the benefits that come from cooperating with those organizations for our country."
Samdech recommended that all young people who are delegates should pay attention and learn from the situation of other countries and about the development of that country in order to bring good points to develop their country. Must know how to love each other like brothers and sisters by working together, working in a team and helping each other in all circumstances, as the Khmer saying goes, "At home, other mothers go to the same mother forest."
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei emphasized that all young people must be a good guide, a diplomat representing Cambodia, while preserving the honor, values and culture of the nation by trying to promote the culture, tourism and national identity as well. Good relations with young people from other countries.
The Southeast Asia-Japan Youth Ship Program was established by Japan in 1974. The Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association was established in 2004, and so far 669 young Cambodians have participated in the Southeast Asian Youth Ship Program - Japan.
Mr. Srean Kimly said that the Cambodian Association of Southeast Asian Youth Ships has been operating so far due to the support from the leaders of the top national institutions, ministries and departments, especially the high honor of the President of the National Assembly. Which represents the national legislature.
The President of the National Assembly wished all young people good health and a happy and safe journey and achieved the expected results. Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin also provided 400,000 Riels for each Cambodian youth delegate and 4 million Riels for each association.
