(Phnom Penh): AMK Microfinance Plc .'s financial statements for the first half of 2018 show that the vast majority of its borrowers are women, accounting for more than 80% of the total number of borrowers.
Most AMK clients are poor people living in rural areas. This figure clearly indicates that AMK has been working to empower women in rural areas to play an active role in family life and economic decisions.
AMK has been focusing on developing its financial products and services to be easy and hassle-free for its clients, especially women.
Kea Boran, CEO of AMK Microfinance Institution, said: “Providing opportunities for women to participate in decision-making in full-fledged family economic activity can help boost national economic growth and reduce poverty. In general, AMK always provides financial services that are suitable for consumers, especially women living in rural areas, so that they have enough opportunities to use our services.
According to the latest AMK financial statements for the last six months, nearly 300,000 AMK clients are women, accounting for more than 80% of total loan clients. They live in rural areas.
"AMK's mission is to help the majority of the poor," Boran said. Here we want to emphasize rural women and children. "Therefore, AMK is constantly developing new financial products and services from year to year to meet the needs of our customers, especially women, in order to develop their family economy."
