Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for a Wooden Dome for Monks at Indap Borey Pagoda in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): On Monday, September 24, 2018, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, laid the foundation stone for a wooden hut for monks. At Wat Indabat Borey, also known as Wat Angkor Khang Tbong, in Kravan village, Nokor Thom commune, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, with the participation of leaders and senior officials of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, as well as Buddhists under the pagoda.
The construction of the wooden huts in this magnificent historical and cultural resort was initiated by the Senior Minister's generosity in Buddhism to be preserved in Buddhism, which will be left as a historical legacy for future generations.
This wooden hut is 12m x 21m long, 10.6m high, with a concrete bottom and a wooden upper in the style of pure Khmer traditional culture, which also maintains the beauty and quality of construction in our historic resort. .
It should also be noted that Wat Indabat Borey, also known as Wat Angkor Khang Tbong, is one of the oldest pagodas in history, located in the northern part of Siem Reap. It was not until 1910 that the French authorities asked the monks to leave Angkor Wat.
The pagoda was rebuilt in 1921 but was also destroyed during the Khmer Rouge era. After the liberation on January 7, 1979, Buddhism began to revive, and the pagoda began to have a series of monks and began to build achievements for the shrine, which now has a school, a stone hut, a wooden hut. One toilet and one toilet.
At the same time, the Senior Minister brought gifts to distribute to 150 Ta Chi Yai Chi, each of whom received a piece of white cloth and 20,000 Riels, and also invited to count the bowls.
Minister of Information describes in detail the attempted assassination of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in Siem Reap 20 years ago
(Phnom Penh): September 24, 2018 is the 20th anniversary of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, was attempted to assassinate and fired up to 40 40 B rockets aimed at his convoy. Samdech, and one of the rockets that the assassins fired at Samdech's car did not fly to Samdech's car, but flew to people's houses, killing one citizen.
This assassination attempt is an unforgettable historical event. Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always mentioned the assassination, but did not elaborate on the incident.
On the night of September 24, 2018, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, who was also present at this event, came out to describe the event in detail to share with the Cambodian people about the important events of Cambodia during That the crisis of war is not over yet. The following is the full text of the assassination attempt described by Minister Khieu Kanharith:
Today, Samdech Techo commemorates the 20th anniversary of the assassination attempt in Siem Reap. I would like to remind you of this because I was stuck with this job at the time. Speaking of which, I still remember the words of Mr. Chiv Ta Kwan when he came to Cambodia during the Angkorian period. It is true that when Chiv Ta Kwan came to Cambodia, our country was starting to weaken, but one thing that Chiv Ta Kwan noticed was: "The gods keep this district very strong."
Only on the morning of the 23rd did he find out that the Black Prince pagoda was in Angkor Thom on the way to Bayon Temple. On the afternoon of the 23rd, Samdech and all elected members of the National Assembly of the People's Party took a joint bus (including me) to Wat Preah Ang Khmao.
According to the Angkor Conservation Group, this pagoda was named after Preah Ang Khmao pagoda during the post-Angkorian religious war between Brahmanism and Buddhism. This so far. After praying, Samdech Techo poured the Bible at the bodhisattva born in the dynasty, but he did not say anything like deaf until his father could not resist the order to kill him but did not die.
In the first session, the presidents of the parties with seats in the parliament all sit in the front row. At that time, Samdech Sar Kheng (still the Minister of Interior) received a phone call saying that there were 40 bullets hidden in a bunch of paper flowers along the road and controlled by a mobile phone system.
After a complete description of this shocking and painful event, Minister Khieu Kanharith claimed that today was a great day, the beginning of Ben, so the story he recalled about the assassination attempt on Hun Sen was not disclosed. Anything.
Finally, Mr. Khieu Kanharith also prayed for Cambodia to meet only peace, bad people to become able to hold festivals and let Cambodians know how to love each other.
Samdech Techo also confirmed that Samdech has already given agriculture to those who want to kill Samdech in Siem Reap, even though Samdech has the light to research. "But you have to know that when I was prime minister, I did not want you to kill me, you did not want a coup d'etat or a color revolution," he said. At all costs, I must protect the peace and protect the lives of the Cambodian people. ”
