To celebrate the 25th anniversary of the promulgation of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Prohm Vichet Akhara, spokesman for the Constitutional Council, said that Im Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, had commissioned the publication of 2,000 copies of the Constitution. Distributed to all institutions and stakeholders.
This publication integrates the understanding of the content of the Constitution, which is the supreme law of the country, into all centers of society to promote the rule of law in the Kingdom of Cambodia. The Constitutional Council will continue to publish tens of thousands of copies, ensuring that the supreme law of this nation is disseminated to all sections of society, especially to local authorities, including commune councils.
The First Constitution: The first Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia has 12 chapters and 122 articles and was adopted on May 6, 1947. The 1947 constitution is a constitutional one, but this constitution does not change the form of leadership, only some changes according to the actual situation.
Second Constitution: The Constitution of the Khmer Republic has 11 chapters and 121 articles and was adopted on May 10, 1972. This constitution changed the political system from a constitutional monarchy to a US-style republic.
Third Constitution: is the Constitution of Democratic Kampuchea, which has 21 articles, divided into 16 chapters, and was adopted on January 5, 1976. The Constitution of Democratic Kampuchea, which transformed the regime in Cambodia from a republic to a communist dictatorship, massacred its own people for three years, eight months and 20 days.
Fourth Constitution: The Constitution of the People's Republic of Democratic Kampuchea has 93 articles and 10 chapters and was promulgated by Decree No. 01, dated June 25, 1981.
Fifth Constitution: On April 30, 1989, the National Assembly of the People's Republic of Kampuchea amended this Constitution by changing the name of Cambodia from the People's Republic of Kampuchea to the State of Cambodia in Article 4 of this Constitution states: Cambodia implements a multi-party political system. This constitution has 93 articles and 10 chapters.
After the election, the Constituent Assembly was active until September 21, 1993, approving the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia by 97% of the votes, and was officially promulgated by the King of Cambodia, King Norodom Sihanouk. Royal Kram, dated September 24, 1993. Garbage in Bavet city is almost 200 tons a day! A Japanese company is currently planning to turn waste into construction materials and furniture.
