The director of the department confirmed that among the more than 3,000 tourists, there are more than 1,700 foreign visitors, the total number in September 2018 is the same as last year.
But some of you must be wondering why the event "Sunrise rises from the top of the central tower of Angkor Wat"? Why are Cambodia's Angkor temples so amazing?
The great Khmer ancestors of the Mohanakor period, who were deeply aware of Hinduism, were well aware of this phenomenon, so they jointly built a huge temple of Preah Borom Vishnu (now Angkor Wat) to match the orbit in the cause to dedicate. To Vishnu, one of the great deities in Brahmanism (the great deity in Brahmanism is Vishnu and Shiva).
As the equinox occurs twice every year, the sun rises on the top of the central tower of the temple of Vishnu, which was first built under the auspices of King Suryavarman II (1113-1150) until today. And continue into the future throughout the earth. Is not this the magnificence of Angkor Wat and the great ideals of Khmer Mohanakor?
