Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie Commander Gives a House to a Poor Family
(Preah Vihear): The Commander of the Preah Vihear Provincial Gendarmerie, Brigadier General Kang Sao Kun, and many other Gendarmerie officers handed over a house made of galvanized iron to the people this morning, September 23, 2018. A poor family lives in Po village, Po commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province.
He said that today he handed over a house made of galvanized iron with a size of 5 meters by 6 meters, with a construction budget of 6,300,000 riels to the families of the poor.
In addition to handing over a house to him, he also handed over some materials, including: 200,000 Riels, 2 bags of rice, 1 bag of fish sauce, 8 boxes of pure water, 4 boxes of noodles, 1 bag of orange juice, 4 boxes of fruit juice, 10 plates, 10 sarongs and 2 cakes. The tank and all the money and materials came from donations from military officers to participate in humanitarian activities. A vegetable farmer in Maung Russey district earns nearly $ 3,000 per year.
(Battambang): A female farmer who grows vegetables in Maung Russey district told Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, that she earns more than 2,000 US dollars a year.
Her assertion was made on the morning of September 23, 2018, when Mr. Veng Sakhon continued to inspect the vegetable production of farmers in Boeung Pring village, Prek Touch commune, Maung Russey district, who were harvesting cucumbers.
According to the farmer's report, she received cultivation techniques through the Agricultural Services Program for Climate Resilience Innovation, which is funded by the Royal Government of Cambodia and the International Fund for Agricultural Development. She continued happily that vegetables, cucumbers and other vegetables, combined with rice, her family can earn more than 11 million riels, about $ 2,750 per year.
According to this data, this farmer is considered as one of the high income of farmers in rural areas. The great achievement is due to the efforts of all stakeholders, especially from the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister, which maintains peace, stability and development. She added that the Royal Government, in collaboration with IFAD, has provided funding to implement this program in order to improve living standards and reduce poverty.
On this occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon provided additional guidance on technical work, marketing and processing to add value to farmers' products, in particular, he encouraged farmers to continue their efforts to achieve higher incomes in line with growth. Cambodia's economy is on the rise.
