(Battambang): September 24, 2018 is the third day of the mission of Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and accompanied by colleagues and leaders of the Department of Agriculture continued to inspect the cultivation and evaluation. From the damage caused by natural disasters at Otasam point in Kampong Preah village, Kampong Preah commune, Sangke district, Battambang province.
According to the report of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, 30,000 hectares of farmland were completely damaged, including more than 13,000 hectares of flood damage and more than 17,000 hectares of drought that occurred in Ek Phnom, Thmor Kol, Sangke, Bavel, Maung Russey, Rukkiri, Koas Kralor, Kamrieng and Sampov Loun districts.
More than 3,000 hectares of agro-industrial crops across the province, including corn, potatoes, beans and pepper, were damaged by natural disasters, including more than 1,000 hectares by floods and more than 2,000 hectares by drought.
