Disabled people start using Samdech Techo Hun Sen musical instruments worth more than 30,000 USD to raise funds with insistence on support
(Phnom Penh): The Chap To Music Association for the Disabled on September 22, 2018 started using musical instruments donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, bought from the United Kingdom worth more than 30,000 US dollars. Concert to support their livelihood as well as many other disabled members.
The inauguration ceremony of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's musical instrument took place at Wat Phnom Historical Resort with the participation of Ms. Nhem Morakot, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Women's Affairs and Honorary President of Samneang Music Association for the Disabled, as well as many other philanthropists. .
Chap To, executive director of the Samneang Music Association for the Disabled, said the official launch of the instrument was also the start of a concert to raise funds for more than 100 people with disabilities living in his association. He said that the location of Wat Phnom was allowed by Samdech Techo Prime Minister to take the location in the area of Wat Phnom in front of the Electricite du Cambodge in Phnom Penh to hold a concert.
"People with disabilities are always taken care of by the country's leaders, especially the authorities, who always facilitate people with disabilities to have a smooth concert," he said. My association always respects the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who advised people with disabilities to give concerts where appropriate.
According to the president of the association, people with disabilities like him have high hopes for life because they can work like people with disabilities, such as concerts and massage. He said that at the Wat Phnom site, his band had been raising funds for a week. He urged people who are traveling on the streets and in the area of Wat Phnom, if they hear the voices of people with disabilities, please support them with pure generosity.
Chet Sles, a security guard at Wat Phnom, was removed from the Phnom Penh Department of Culture. He said that his security team consisted of more than 20 people selected by the governor of Phnom Penh to be in charge of Wat Phnom. He said that in order to follow the recommendations of the leadership and to promote the disabled, he was very pleased to help such work.
The concert of the Association of the Disabled started immediately, mixed with the beautiful voices of the disabled. This tone discouraged the Cambodian people who are philanthropists to start donating money one after another. Mrs. Sieng Chanheng, President of Heng Aphivath Company, donated 5 million Riels to the Association and 1 million Riels to the security guards as a bond of the first inauguration day.
Please be informed that Samneang Music Association for the Disabled was established in 2013 by Mr. Chap To, a blind person. The association is located in Chumral village, Sangkat Kork Roka, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh and is also recognized by the Ministry of Interior.
