577 Families in Reang Til Commune Affected by the River Flood Receiving Humanitarian Donations from Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Pursat Province
(Pursat): Residents of 577 families living on floating houses in Tonle Sap Lake from 3 villages in Reang Til commune, Kandieng district, who are facing food shortage during the rising river, have gathered to receive humanitarian donations from the Cambodian Red Cross. Pursat province, with each family 25 kg of rice, 1 stick of fish sauce and 1 stick of soy sauce to help ease life for a while.
The ceremony was held on September 21, 2018 on the hill of Reang Til Primary School with the participation of Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge, High Representative, Samdech Kittipritthbandit and Mr. Mao Thor Nin, Governor of Pursat Province and Honorary Chairman of the Provincial Red Cross Branch, as well as the accompanying delegation and many other officials.
Mr. Mao Thunin and Mr. Keo Rattanak addressed the meeting of the people of Reang Til commune, bringing greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross. As always, the two Samdech always think about the hardships of the people all over the country, including the people living on the surface of the Tonle Sap Lake.
The two leaders also informed that all humanitarian donations came from the support of leaders, monks, businessmen, government officials, the armed forces and philanthropists who have resources in the province, outside the province and abroad. Help the people affected by various factors, regardless of political affiliation, in fact, in Reang Til commune itself, as well as yesterday in Kampong Luong commune.
