Ministry of Tourism trains nearly 100 subordinates on efficiency management
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has established training courses on labor efficiency management for its civil servants at the Ministry and the Department of Tourism, a total of nearly 100 people to mainstream the administration, work efficiency management, the current situation and Many work policies related to tourism.
The four-day training (September 18-21) focuses on administration and general affairs, the organization of Cambodia's civil service, the civil service quality management system, management principles and implementation reform. , Law on Tourism and Law Enforcement Promotion.
The Closing Ceremony of the Training Course was presided over by Mr. Kong Solida, Director General of Administration and Finance, Representative of Minister Thong Khon at the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia on the afternoon of September 21, 2018.
General Director Kong Solida told the participants that in 2018, Cambodia plans to receive about 6.2 million international tourists. By 2020, Cambodia plans to receive 7 million international tourists and about $ 5 billion in tourism revenue and create nearly 1 million direct jobs and businesses. By 2025, Cambodia plans to receive 10 million international tourists, and by 2030, Cambodia plans to receive 14 million international tourists.
To achieve this vision, the Ministry has prepared a strategic plan for tourism development 2012-2020, focusing on the main work, including: 1: Development of tourism products. 3: Human resource development according to the concept of "one employee, one skill". 4. Strengthening tourism promotion (both domestic and foreign).
In addition, Mr. Kong Solida advised the civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism to effectively participate in the "Clean Restaurants and Restaurants" movement, the campaign without trash under the table in restaurants - special restaurants to implement the "Clean City, Clean Resort, Good Service" movement. And good hospitality ”to be revived throughout the country.
Participants gain new knowledge, experience and ideas in addition to the existing ones related to daily work in their units, especially this course is also a good meeting opportunity between officials at the Ministry and the Department of Tourism in the capital-province. Discussion, sharing, exchanging experiences and good ideas with each other.
