Geng said the new sanctions against China over military cooperation with Russia violate the principles of purely international relations, while cooperation between the two countries, including the military, is not in violation of the law. Internationally, there is no target for any third country, so Beijing will continue to strengthen cooperation with Moscow, despite US sanctions.
