Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Regrets Short Time in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, Mr. Shongbor, has reached the end of his term in office in 2018 after serving two years. The Ambassador expressed regret that he had a short stint in Cambodia.
This expression of regret was made when Mr. Seung Por said goodbye to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on the morning of September 21, 2018.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the two-year mission of Mr. Singbor. According to the Deputy Prime Minister, the tenure of the two countries has been exchanged by the two countries' top leaders, including Xi Jinping and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang.
Prak Sokhon informed Sungbor that he hoped to pay an official visit to China after the formation of a new government.
The Chinese Ambassador also expressed his happiness and confirmed that the Chinese Embassy in Phnom Penh will arrange a visit by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon soon.
Please be informed that Mr. Song Bor was appointed by the Royal Government of China to fulfill his diplomatic mission in Cambodia in 2016, and it is now two years since he was terminated, but for the new Ambassador The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia has not yet confirmed who will continue the diplomatic mission. Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Siem Reap Meets 161 Vulnerable Families in Chi Kreng District
(Siem Reap): 161 families affected by the flooding of the Tonle Sap Lake in Anlong Samnor commune, Chi Kreng commune, who came to stay at Dam 78 and Chi Kreng commune, Chi Kreng district, Siem Reap province, by Mr. Khim Bunsong, Chairman of the Committee The Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross and the Governor of Siem Reap Province distributed humanitarian donations to the victims this morning, September 21, 2018.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Khim Bunsong stated that the gifts received by grandparents, uncles and aunts now under the care of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, which Samdech always took care of Pay close attention to the hardships and living conditions of the people, without leaving anyone to die without food.
Mr. Khim Bunsong also expressed his sympathy for the poor and helpless old people and also brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as the Head of the Royal Government. Companion to the victims in all circumstances, without leaving any relatives to die without food.
At the same time, he also advised all citizens, especially women with small children and pregnant women to take care of the health of both mother and child. On the other hand, all citizens must be very careful when the village is flooded for young children not to visit the water for fear of something bad for the family during the flood.
Mr. Khim Bunsong also instructed and instructed the affected people in both communes who came to settle temporarily in a safe place and to pay attention to health care by drinking clean water, it is important to be careful and prevent High for wild animals and clean the environment around the house after the water recedes.
He also thanked World Vision for cooperating with local authorities to provide some materials to the victims. Humanitarian donations provided to each family include 1 mosquito net, 1 scarf and clothes, 1 fishing rod, 1 box of noodles, 25 kg of rice, 2 carrying water, 1 tent and 50,000 Riels.
