Oddar Meanchey CamControl Officers Find Some Oranges and Oishi Tea Imported from Thailand Expired and Confiscated
(Oddar Meanchey): Officials from Cam Kong, Meanchey Province and Provincial Department of Commerce, in cooperation with Trapeang Prasat District Authority, inspected various shops in Trapeang Prasat Market in Trapeang Prasat District, Oddar Meanchey Province on the morning of the 21st. This September 2018.
During the inspection, CamControl officials in Oddar Meanchey province focused on a variety of food items, including some beverages, which were displayed for sale in Trapeang Prasat market after the CamControl officers inspected and found Some expired food items.
As a result, CamControl officers found overdue and expired goods, including 41 bottles of Thai orange juice, 12 bottles of Oishi tea, 30 small boxes of beans and a packet of candy, and confiscated them for destruction.
In addition, CamControl officials have educated and advised traders to consider the health of buyers first, and all goods purchased for sale must be carefully checked, especially not to buy goods at the bottom of the warehouse, which has been stored for years to resell.
Camcontrol officials also called on people before buying something to check before eating, because if we do not check clearly, it will affect health after we eat.
