(Phnom Penh): A woman who has been traditionally married for 13 years and has been living with her husband and two sons and daughters has secretly had an affair with a new man and has been having an affair with a man who is an adulteress. More than a month was broken. The husband caught up and complained to the police at Post Choam Chao 1 of the Por Sen Chey District Inspectorate to intervene and arrest him, demanding $ 4,000 in compensation.
This incident caused a surprise on September 20, 2018 around Toul Pong Market, Toul Pong Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the wife, 32-year-old N.S.N, is a factory worker living in Tuol Sleng village, Pong Teuk commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh. Separately, a prostitute named Yim Chan Vannak, 32 years old, lives in Borey Sandepheap 2, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh. The husband, who is anonymous, has two children, a 12-year-old daughter and an 8-year-old son.
According to the husband, he and his wife were legally married with a valid marriage certificate and had been living together for more than 13 years. The marriage has two sons and daughters, but recently, more than a month, his wife has been in a relationship with a new man to the point of falling in love several times together.
He said that the search continued until he saw the woman who was his wife with his own eyes, obviously dating a prostitute on a concrete road in Tuol Pong village, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Sen Chey. Unable to control his temper, the husband immediately complained to the Chaom Chao 1 police station to stop and intervene, demanding $ 4,000 in compensation to raise the children and hand over his wife to live with the prostitute.
As the victim's husband filed a complaint with the Pong Teuk Sangkat Police Station, Dangkor District, the Choam Chao 1 Police Station handed over the case to the Pong Teuk Sangkat Police Station, Dangkor District, according to the procedure.
Cambodia-Japan Investment, Trade and Tourism Sector Discussed In-Depth Meeting
(Phnom Penh): As the investment, trade and tourism sectors between Cambodia and Japan continue to strengthen and expand, the Foreign Ministries of the two countries have re-discussed these issues to exchange views on exploration. New ways and means to further expand the above three areas in more detail.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the bilateral talks were held by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, with Mr. Taro Kono, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, in Tokyo. Opportunity for Mr. Prak Sokhon to pay a two-day visit from September 18-19, 2018 in Japan.
Recalling Japan's significant contribution to Cambodia's efforts in the process of peace building, rehabilitation and development, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expressed his deep appreciation for the commitment of Japan in continuing to support socio-economic and democratic progress in Cambodia.
"The two Foreign Ministers exchanged views on ways and means to deepen and expand existing bilateral cooperation such as investment, trade and tourism," the statement said.
Mr. Prak Sokhon warmly welcomed Japan's intention to promote and strengthen cooperation in multilateral frameworks such as the Mekong-Japan Strategic Economic Cooperation, the Ayeyarwaddy-Chao Phraya-Mekong (ACMECS) ASEAN and the Asia-Europe Meeting. .
