Prudential launches first aid safety program
(Phnom Penh): The Prudential Foundation, a regional community development fund of the Prudential Asia Corporation, has partnered with the Cambodian Red Cross to organize "World First Aid Day" in Srong Commune, Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province.
Meanwhile, the Prudential Foundation, a regional community development fund of the Prudential Asia Corporation, has launched a first aid safety program in Cambodia, with support from the Cambodian Red Cross, aimed at saving lives and reducing community risks. .
During the event, Prudential Cambodia Volunteer Team distributed 600 posters and leaflets to young participants, CRC volunteers, students, local authorities, people and communities to provide basic knowledge. First aid for self-help Family and community members in the event of an accident before the ambulance arrives or before being taken to the hospital.
Mr. Touch Thavrith, Senior Manager, Development and Strategy, Distribution Partners of Prudential Cambodia, said that information related to first aid will be disseminated throughout Cambodia through social media at events and television programs for the people. Khmer people have this skill in first aid.
Mr. Thavrith said, "The first aid safety step program is designed to provide the public with basic knowledge about first aid so that they are able to reduce their vulnerability in an emergency and be prepared to save lives in case of an emergency." "An emergency has occurred."
On World First Aid Day, the Cambodian Red Cross presented three first aid skills and step-by-step rescue methods. Participants learned how to apply first aid to victims of fractures, cuts and burns.
