2,163 Families Affected by Floods in Prey Veng Receive Humanitarian Donations from the Cambodian Red Cross
(Prey Veng): For two days, on September 20-21, 2018, the Cambodian Red Cross (aka Krak), chaired by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, assigned a working group to visit and Distribute direct donations to 2,163 flood-affected families in Preah Sdach, Peam Chor and Peam Ro districts, Prey Veng province.
The ceremony was held at Prek Krabao High School in Udong village, Prek Krabao commune, Peam Chor district for 1,600 families, led by Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, Acting Secretary General, this morning, September 21. Preah Sdach District Hall is located in Krasaing Tong Village, Angkor Reach Commune. For the other 563 affected families, the working group was distributed by Mr. Yulana, Second Deputy Secretary General on September 20 yesterday.
At the same time, Mr. Oknha Sok Pheng, Permanent Vice Chairman of Prey Veng Branch Committee, on behalf of all the victims, thanked Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for always thinking about the well-being and living conditions of the people. Difficult without racism or political tendencies.
The gifts distributed to each family include: 30 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish, 1 mosquito net, 1 blanket, 1 sarong, 1 scarf and 1 T-shirt. Separately, Prey Veng branch has provided additional funds for travel expenses of 10,000 Riels.
