Senior Minister Kun Kim Distributes Veterans' Cards to Veterans and Thanks for Voting for the CPP for Continuing Peace and Development
(Kep): Senior Minister Kun Kim, in charge of the Special Mission on Veterans Affairs, arrived in Kep province on September 21, 2018 to thank the veterans who voted for the Cambodian People's Party and Distribute National Social Security Fund (NSSF) cards to veterans as well.
In front of the veterans who received the National Social Security Fund, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his condolences and consideration for the well-being of all veterans from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kitti. Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Mr. Kun Kim said, "The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always miss our veterans and send me to visit all of you. Although both Samdech are busy with the work of the nation, but Samdech never forget you.
Senior Minister Kun Kim stated that because of this attention, Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked the Veterans Association to make efforts to prepare the National Social Security Fund for all veterans to receive medical examination and treatment services in Free hospitalization, which contributes to reducing veterans' costs to another level.
After explaining the importance of the National Social Security Fund and the use of this card, Mr. Kun Kim also thanked all the veterans who voted for the Cambodian People's Party on July 29, 2018. Go there. The senior minister considered the decision of the veterans to be the right decision to choose a leader who ensures peace and national development.
Mr. Kun Kim also highlighted the policy of the new government, especially the commitment of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to redouble his efforts to bring benefits to the nation and the people of Cambodia.
On that occasion, HE Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, brought a message from Samdech Techo President of the Association to all our members, then HE also thanked our brothers in Kep. Those who went to the polls will have the highest percentage compared to other provinces.
During the distribution of cards this morning, Senior Minister Kun Kim asked the Governor of Kep to settle the land for 16 homeless veterans, and he will respectfully request Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Veterans Association to build houses for veterans. Fighters when they get land.
