Speaking to the media after the meeting with the construction team and the announcement of the countdown at the Victory Monument and the distribution of certificates to the trainees of the Victory Monument this morning, September 21, 2018 in Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changvar, Phnom Penh, Samdech Pich Sena confirmed that the celebration of the 20th anniversary of the win-win policy and the official inauguration of the Victory Monument will be very lively.
The Minister of Defense added that from today, the countdown is 100 days, must be completed in all areas, all skills to meet the deadline of the day of great meaning for the motherland of Cambodia.
Victory Monument was started in February 2016 with an area of eight hectares in Chroy Changva district, Phnom Penh. The budget for the construction of this monument is the contribution of the Royal Government. This monument is a symbol of Cambodia's peace and is scheduled to be officially inaugurated on December 29, 2018, the day the Royal Government of Cambodia celebrates the 20th anniversary of the win-win policy (1998). 2018) as well.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh said that the construction will be completed before December 29, both inside and outside, including the planting of trees.
Please note that the construction of this win-win monument is to commemorate the merits of Khmer ancestors of all times who sacrificed their lives in the cause of the motherland. Moreover, this monument is also a symbol of the peace that Cambodia has achieved after the end of decades of civil war. In addition, this monument will be a legacy for future generations.
The Cambodian American Association expresses its pleasure and support for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to the United Nations in New York (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Ik Ngoy, Secretary General of the Cambodian American Association, on September 21, 2018. He wrote a letter expressing his pleasure and support for the visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to the United Nations in New York to attend the 73rd General Assembly.
It should be noted that the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will attend the 73rd General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly and other relevant meetings for 5 days from 25 to 29 September. 2018 in New York City.
The theme of the conference is "Making the United Nations relevant to all people: global leadership and shared responsibility for a peaceful, equitable and sustainable society."
The following is a letter from the Secretary General of the Khmer American Association: General Nem Sovath: Two more meaningful words can be inscribed at the Victory Monument
(Phnom Penh): General Nem Sovath, Chairman of the Victory Monument Construction Team, confirmed that Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Chairman of the Victory Monument Construction Committee, gave an important recommendation to allow the preparation of two more inscriptions. Confirm the beginning of a life of struggle as a brave guide of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, mentioned on June 21, 2017.
The content that Samdech Techo Hun Sen mentioned was the beginning of the journey towards the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and the organization of the National Salvation Unity Force, Unit 125, and the joint formation of the 2 December Front and the 7 January National Liberation Front. 1979
It then continued to build Cambodia until the introduction of a win-win policy during 1995 and succeeded in overthrowing the Khmer Rouge's political and military organization by the end of 1998. In the process, there was an important strategy, the defensive strategy, which included integration events that turned all Khmer Rouge forces into contributing to a three-pronged win-win policy.
The event became a historical event, one of the main factors that brought complete success, brought complete peace to the country, and many philosophies were highlighted in plots to be selected as historical words. Recall the process of those struggles towards building the motherland of Cambodia.
Another last word that Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh chose and prepared for further inscription at the Victory Monument, which signifies the end of the civil war and complete peace. This is another brand new achievement to be had at the Victory Monument after two stone tablets of great significance and depth were inscribed and prepared last year.
