Authorities remove poles planted on more than 1,000 meters of state forest land that people illegally encroached on in Sdao commune, Sesan district
(Stung Treng): Mr. Chea Thavrith, Deputy Governor of Stung Treng Province, led all kinds of armed forces and officials of relevant departments to take action to remove the poles planted on state forest land anarchically. The operation took place on September 20, 2018 at the e-book point in Sdao commune, Sesan district, which is the entrance to the former land concession of Sok Heng Company.
He added that from Ibuk point in Sdao commune, Sesan district, there were 9 land encroachment points, including 3 points to build huts and other crops, which were sent to court. Find the owner, take legal responsibility and dismantle it.
Officials from the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries also said that the land was previously an economic land concession of Sok Heng Company to grow 7,400 hectares of state-owned agro-industrial crops and no development. The land was confiscated and the remaining 620 hectares Later, even though Sok Heng had 620 hectares of land remaining undeveloped, the government reclaimed the land as state property.
Mr. Minh Sichai, Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, said that the officials of the relevant departments will prepare the registration soon for the enclosure and hand it over to the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for management.
Mr. Chea Thavrith emphasized that after removing the fence posts and raising the sign to avoid further encroachment, he will use the armed forces to patrol once a week, if there is another case of illegal deforestation, he will Follow the law.
