Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon paid a two-day visit to Japan from September 18-19, 2018 at the invitation of Japanese Foreign Minister Taro Kono.
This visit, together with Taro Kono's visit to Cambodia last April, aims to further strengthen the close relationship and partnership of cooperation between Cambodia and Japan. The two are celebrating the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations.
During the visit, the Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister had a friendly discussion with his Japanese counterpart, during which Mr. Prak Sokhon conveyed Samdech Techo Hun Sen's thanks to Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe for sending a congratulatory letter. Samdech Techo after being re-appointed Prime Minister of Cambodia after the recent successful general election.
According to the statement, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon also confirmed the participation of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in the 10th Mekong-Japan Summit to be held early next month in Tokyo. He also discussed with Kono the agenda of the summit.
