(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. KHOURN Sreng, instructed the Southeast Asian Youth Ships to spread the truth about Cambodia to the ASEAN youths while the country is now peaceful and developed under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The remarks came as the Governor met with a group of more than 30 Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ships on the afternoon of September 20, 2018 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall before they embarked on a cruise across four countries organized by Japan. More than 300 young people from some ASEAN countries and Japan.
Mr. Khuong Sreng instructed a group of more than 30 youths led by Mr. Srang Kimly: "Our youth need to spread the real situation in Cambodia to the youth of ASEAN countries and the youth of Japan to better understand Cambodia. In particular, the current state of peace and development in Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister makes Cambodia a name on the regional and international stage.
The governor continued that our youth must dare to explain and explain to the ASEAN youth and the Japanese youth about the beautiful cultural traditions of Cambodia and act equally and equally.
This is the 45th time that a cruise ship has passed through four ASEAN countries, including Brunei, the Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam, with a total of ASEAN and Japanese youths. 330 people met for the first time in Tokyo, Japan to officially open the event.
The 52-day Japan-sponsored cruise program runs from October 23 to December 12, 2018, with the aim of strengthening the friendship, solidarity and cooperation between ASEAN and the United States. Japan through youth, with a focus on meetings, performances, arts, culture and travel.
