(Kampong Cham): On September 20, 2018, the joint police force of Kampong Cham province continued to crack down on two cases of illegal fishing, confiscating some relevant exhibits and releasing mixed fish into the water.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Em Kosal, said that after receiving information about illegal fishing, he ordered the Kampong Siem District Police Inspector in cooperation with the Vihear Thom Administrative Police Force, Srok Prachea Prakorn and Kampong Cham Provincial Fisheries Administration. Mr. Yi Vannak, Deputy Governor of Kampong Siem District, with the guidance of Mr. Bin Lada, Governor of Kampong Siem District, cracked down on illegal fishing.
According to the General Commissioner, the first case in Boeung Kdei village, Vihear Thom commune, Kampong Siem district resulted in three mosquito nets, a 150-meter-long barrier, and 30 bamboo poles. The exhibits were temporarily stored at the Vihear Thom Administrative Police Station to await further action.
In the second case, in front of Wat Preah Keo Uday Lpeak and at the head of the Trouy Chek Dam in Srok commune, Kampong Siem district, five mosquito nets, a 250-meter-long barrier and 3 kilograms of mixed fish were released into a natural lake. The exhibits were burned on the spot with the approval of the Prosecutor of Kampong Cham Provincial Court.
