Summary of the main content of the summit between the two Korean leaders in Pyongyang, which ended in 3 days!
(Seoul): It can be said that it is the most interesting event between the two Koreas, as the positives accumulated over the past three days have allowed the two Koreas to resume good relations in In the near future, while relations between North Korea and the United States may also improve. This is according to the summary of important events on inter-Korean issues on the evening of Thursday, September 20, 2018.
The summit between North Korean leader Kim Jong Un and South Korean President Moon Jae-in began in Pyongyang on Tuesday afternoon and ended after Moon Jae-in and his wife. Fly back to South Korea on Thursday evening after completing a three-day visit.
The most surprising thing is that North Korean leader Kim Jong Un came out to receive South Korean President Moon Jae-in directly at Pyongyang International Airport, which is very rare for a reception. World leaders.
Finally, South Korean President Moon Jae-in and North Korean outgoing leader Kim Jong-un began the first round of talks on Tuesday at the third inter-Korean summit aimed at facilitating a breakthrough. The resumption of talks on the elimination of nuclear weapons on the Korean Peninsula between Kim and Donald Trump.
On the first day of the talks, which began Tuesday afternoon, Kim Jong Un said to South Korean President Moon Jae-in, "President Moon has helped us a lot in finding historic talks. "Between the United States and North Korea ... and because of this engagement, it has stabilized the whole region as progress and satisfactory results emerge."
The second day of talks, Wednesday, September 19, officially began between Moon and Kim in Pyongyang, without delay, the young North Korean leader confirmed that he would pay a visit to Seoul in In the near future, he and South Korean President Moon Jae-in have also agreed to work to make the Korean Peninsula nuclear-free and non-threatening.
Finally, Seoul and Pyongyang have agreed to send a joint team of athletes to the 2020 Olympics and submit a joint bid to host the 2032 International Games. These are more recent positives for easing tensions and improving relations between the two Koreas, which the international community has long wanted to see.
South Korean President Moon Jae-in returned to South Korea on Thursday evening after attending a summit with North Korean leader Kim Jong-un in Pyongyang since Tuesday.
Moon Jae-in became the third South Korean president to step on Pyongyang. The two Korean leaders have already met twice, on April 27 and May 26, and Kim Jong Un also promised to pay a visit to Seoul in the future. Coming soon.
