(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the Win-Win Monument Construction Working Group, this morning, September 21, 2018, led the construction team and relevant institutions to open a meeting and announce Countdown at the Victory Monument and distribution of certificates to the participants of the Victory Monument Guide in Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
The ceremony was attended by General Neang Phat, General Nem Sovath, General Ith Sarath, General Tea Vinh, Mr. Khleang Huot, Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chroy Changva District Governor, together with the construction team of the Victory Monument. Representatives of the relevant ministries in large numbers as well.
The Victory Monument, a symbol of Cambodia's peace and under construction in Phnom Penh's Chroy Changvar district, is scheduled to be officially inaugurated on December 29, 2018, the day the Royal Government of Cambodia celebrates the 20th anniversary of its policy. Win-Win (1998-2018) also presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Please be reminded that the construction of this Victory Monument started in February 2016 with an area of 8 hectares in Chroy Changva district, Phnom Penh. The budget for the construction is the contribution of the Royal Government, however, it is not specified how much the construction cost.
