(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on September 20, 2018 issued an official press release on the resolution of the protest at Preah Sisowath High School after the Ministry met with the management and teachers to resolve The two protests were the petition in support of Mr. Moul Suy Heng, the principal of Preah Sisowath High School, and the petition to remove the new generation school from Preah Sisowath High School.
In a three-page official press release obtained by Fresh News this evening, the Ministry of Education stated that in order to resolve the protest, the Ministry has decided to hold two elections: first, to agree with the Ministry's actions; : Save Mr. Moul Suy Heng as the principal of Preah Sisowath High School and take further action.
According to the Ministry of Education, after the election, out of a total of 152 ballots, 54 were in favor of the first option, 97 were in favor of the second option and 1 was invalid.
Based on this, the Ministry will require Mr. Moul Suy Heng to reimburse the state budget for non-transparent use and accountability before the law in force and the Ministry will respect the spirit of the election by re-appointing Mr. Moul Suy Heng as the Principal of Sisowath High School. To end the protest.
