(Kandal): At least 10 families living in Prek Chrey village, Prek Russey commune, Lvea Em district, Kandal province, are upset with Mr. Phim Phira, the governor of Lvea Em district, Kandal province, who did not facilitate the signing of their land title deed. With a total area of 17 hectares, although the village chief, the commune chief confirmed that the land is not related to state land at all.
In a letter from people respecting Mr. Hun Manet asking for help, the villagers stated that their 17 hectares of farmland had been occupied since 1980 and had been recognized by the commune authorities. Due to their poor living conditions, they decided to sell and transfer ownership to solve their livelihood, so that their children could continue their education and receive medical treatment.
Unfortunately, at the time of transfer, all village and commune authorities issued letters to them, except for Phim Phira, the district governor, who refused to sign, citing the fact that their land was in a state-owned state-owned pool. Water resources, although village chiefs and commune chiefs claim that the land is not in the state basin.
Moreover, the people accused the district governor of promising to deceive them. Before the election, Mr. Phim Phira had promised that if he voted for the Cambodian People's Party in the district, he would not return to help the people. Missed. But so far he has not fulfilled his promise, especially the land is claimed to be a pool.
However, the spokesman stressed that the site is in the reservoir area of the Ministry of Water Resources, but the Ministry has not been repaired, and it has been shallow for a long time, so people have cultivated. The results are long overdue.
According to the spokesperson, in order to resolve the issue to the people, the district authority should send a request and report to the governor of Kandal province, who is the chairman of the provincial state land management committee, to send an official to assess whether it should be handed over to the people or not. ?
These people said that if they have been farming for a long time, the local authorities should have decided to cut them, and if the land is only the size of the province, the local authorities will not have a job. .
On the other hand, for commune chiefs and village chiefs who live next door to the people, they should be recognized, so the district governor should help them end their problems as promised before election day, or just a hoax. To get votes? This is an additional statement from the people.
