Nearly 500 Cambodian children receive free heart check-ups by Chinese doctors
(Takeo): The Board of Directors of the Civil Society Forum (CPC) in collaboration with a team of doctors from Yunnan Provincial Heart Hospital of the People's Republic of China visited nearly 500 children in Bati District, Takeo Province. People.
The visit was led by Mr. Kem Rathviseth, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Chairman of the Board of the Civil Society Forum, together with a team of doctors from Yunnan Provincial Heart Hospital of the People's Republic of China, led by Dr. Terlin. International Relations Department of Yunnan Heart Hospital on the morning of September 20, 2018.
This heart health screening program is a project implementation between the Royal Thai Academy of Sciences. And Yunnan Heart Hospital of China in accordance with the spirit of the Memorandum of Understanding signed by the two sides on May 25, 2018.
Mr. Kem Rathviseth expressed his deep gratitude to Dr. Terlin and the team of volunteer doctors of Yunnan Heart Hospital for visiting the heart health of Cambodian children, especially poor families who can not afford medical treatment.
A child with severe heart disease was sent to Yunnan Provincial Heart Hospital in China for medical treatment. The hospital will cover medical expenses, accommodation, meals, and travel expenses. Patients and their parents.
