Some Issues at Preah Vihear Temple Discussed at ICC-Preah Vihear Technical Meeting
(Siem Reap): Some of the work to be done at the Temple of Preah Vihear was discussed by the International Coordinating Committee for the Preservation and Promotion of Preah Vihear (ICC-Preah Vihear) in its fourth technical meeting on the morning of the 20th. September 2018 in the presence of Ms. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts and President of the APSARA Authority at the Angkor Conference Hall of the APSARA Authority.
The ICC-Preah Vihear Committee Meeting, chaired by the Co-Chairmen of China and India and six other member countries, including Belgium, France, Japan, the Republic of Korea, Thailand and the United States, was attended by national and international experts to discuss Mechanism of conservation and development of Preah Vihear and Koh Ker resorts.
The 4th Technical Meeting of the ICC-Preah Vihear Committee this year focused on the excavation work of the Preah Vihear drainage system, the preparation of the Preah Vihear mountain resort site, the planning of the development of the tourism infrastructure and the development of the community development program at the resort. Preah Vihear and Koh Ker temples and some other necessary work.
It should be noted that the National Authority of Preah Vihear and the ICC-Preah Vihear Permanent Secretariat hold this meeting twice a year, including the plenary session held in March and the technical meeting held in September. Ministry of Labor Signs a Memorandum of Understanding with Switzerland to Implement Skills Training Programs in Kratie, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear Provinces
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the Swiss Skills Development Program (SDP) to better implement skills training projects for people in Kratie, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear provinces. The main targets for this project are the poor, vulnerable, with little education, drop out of school under the ninth grade, or unemployment.
The MoU was signed by Mr. Pich Sophoan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor, and Mr. Michael McHul-Jin, Director of the Skills Development Program (SDP), which was also held on September 20, 2018 at the office. Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Pech Sophoan said that in the first step of this skill development program, there are six main skills, including: repairing small machines, repairing motorcycles, repairing electrical networks, plastering, embellishment and tailoring, where the training is all related to theory and practice. Directly at the actual site, such as in factories, enterprises, industrial centers and so on.
The Secretary of State continued that the cooperation on the implementation of this important program is in line with the human resource development policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to provide people with clear professional skills to get jobs. And a decent income aimed at improving livelihoods.
In the near future, Mr. Pich Sophoan wants this skill training activity to spread more widely in Cambodia, especially in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap, which are Cambodia's major economic centers and tourist cities.
Mr. Michael said that the main reason for Switzerland related to the SDP Skills Development Program is to contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia in providing skills to vulnerable youth in the three provinces so that they can get jobs and increase income. And also to contribute to Cambodia's human resource development policy.
According to the SDP, young Cambodians still lack skills in industry, tourism, etc., while some young people already have enough skills but no recognition from any department to be used as an excuse for the boss or employer. Reasons for failing to get a decent job.
The SDP President also stated that when the trainees graduate, the SDP also has a special program to help the trainees get a decent job, such as helping them find a job. They want to start their own business, SDP will also help them. In addition, the SDP also helps to match the skills to the needs of employers.
Please be informed that this SDP Skills Development Program has been implemented in Cambodia gradually from 2016-2020, which aims to train 5,400 people, and by 2018, the project has provided training to about Nearly half. General Mak Chito announces crackdown on nightclubs that smuggle, distribute and use drugs, regardless of whether they belong to the rich or powerful
(Phnom Penh): General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police for Drug Administration, this morning, September 20, 2018, announced the crackdown on all clubs related to drug cases, regardless of whether the club belongs to the rich. Money or all power.
He also stressed that in the event of a crackdown on drug-related clubs, and that someone comes to block or intervene, legal action must be taken without tolerance.
During a meeting on counter-narcotics work at the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command this morning, General Mak Chito said: "Whoever we do this work does not happen, we must do this work well, and if someone comes to prevent us from following the law."
Similarly, the Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, also pointed out that the drug problem is a big problem, so the 12 Sangkats and Khans have to inspect the complex area and the area that has never been visited, and if not, must report to the authorities. Phnom Penh for further action.
The governor of Phnom Penh continued that the crimes are caused by the drug problem, and if the competent forces do not crack down on drugs, other crimes will be reduced to make the village safer. Director of Forestry Administration and Director General of the new General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture have been officially announced.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, September 20, 2018, presided over the inauguration ceremony of two new Chiefs of Forestry Administration and Director General of the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture. Recently, the Acting Head of State, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, issued a Royal Decree on September 19, 2018.
Minister Veng Sakhon congratulates the two newly appointed leaders: Mr. Keo Omalis, the Royal Government of Cambodia Delegate in charge of the Forestry Administration, and Mr. Ngin Chhay, the Royal Government of Cambodia Delegate in charge. Director General of the General Department of Agriculture.
Taking the opportunity, the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries said that the two men are a new leadership, a new force with the knowledge and experience to lead the ministry and the local past better.
In order to achieve the reform policy of the Royal Government and succeed in accordance with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategic Plan Phase 4 and the Strategic Plan for Agricultural Development 2019-2023 of the Ministry of Delegation, it is necessary to pay close attention to the implementation of points Some important points are as follows:
First, fully follow the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to be more active, more comprehensive, and more effective so that all people can benefit more from the Royal Government. Before.
Second, implement the strategic plan and policy of the Royal Government and the Ministry, as well as the full implementation of the legal documents and statutes of civil servants.
Third, strive to research and organize modernized agriculture with an intelligent planet, an environment that is resilient to climate change, innovative and competitive.
Fourth, to strengthen internal unity and solidarity in order to strengthen work efficiency (collective leadership, responsible individuals).
Fifth, to adhere to the professional ethics of civil servants who are public service providers and transfer knowledge to farmers with high efficiency.
Sixth, to continue to promote good agricultural practices in both animal production and animal health and community forestry.
Seventh, encourage and encourage the private sector and build partnerships to participate in the development and dissemination of new technologies in the agricultural sector, along with the use of agricultural machinery and agricultural equipment, seed production, fertilizers and pesticides, processing, packaging and promotion. Domestic market and export.
