Start a new mandate! Minister Mam Bun Heng Disseminates the Royal Government's Fourth Rectangular Strategy to Health Officials
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, this morning, September 20, 2018, organized a program to disseminate the fourth phase of the Royal Government of Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy to health officials at the Ministry. This outreach aims to give all health officials a clear understanding of the goals of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy to better prepare for the development of this sector in the sixth term of the National Assembly.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has successfully implemented the Rectangular Strategy for Employment Growth, Equity and Efficiency in Cambodia in three phases, which has led Cambodia to achieve the most proud transformation. The third corner of the first rectangle talks about the promotion of public health and nutrition services, and the Ministry of Health has done this work most effectively.
Mr. Mam Bunheng emphasized that although the Royal Government has achieved such great achievements, Cambodia still faces some problems, including: the primary health care services are not yet fully and timely, the quality of health care services and Treatment is limited, and the number of doctors and health workers in each category is still insufficient.
According to the Minister, the health insurance system is not yet covered for everyone. Awareness of drug, tobacco, alcohol and food hygiene and safety awareness remains limited, and maternal and infant mortality and malnutrition among women, infants and children among poor rural households remain a challenge.
Phnom Penh Capital Council Holds a Course on Good Governance for Councilors and Khan Council Chairmen
(Phnom Penh): On September 20, 2018, Mr. Mop Sarin, President of Phnom Penh Capital Council, announced the opening of a two-day training course for 20 Capital Councilors, 12 Khan Councilors, 3 Governors and Capital Hall officials. About 90 people on two lessons: 1- The universal principles of good governance and 2- Orientation to the newly elected council.
Ms. Mom Krasal, Chairperson of the Capacity Development Committee of the National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils, said that the training on both lessons was held at the 25 Capital and Provincial Councils in order to raise the awareness of 393 councilors across the country on the theory and practice. Reflects on practicality.
The training was held at Phnom Penh Capital Hall under the technical and financial support of the National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils, coordinated by Ms. Prak Puthy, Member of Tbong Svay Rieng Provincial Council and Trainer from National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils and Mr. Van Then. Independent trainer.
Preah Vihear Malaria Eradication Task Force Meeting to Solve Malaria Eradication by 2025
(Preah Vihear): The Malaria Eradication Task Force in Preah Vihear Province on the afternoon of September 19, 2018 held a special meeting to find ways to eradicate malaria in Preah Vihear Province in accordance with the instructions of the Ministry of Health. As well as the commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The special meeting was attended by Ms. Chak Heng, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, on behalf of Mr. Un Chanda, Provincial Governor, and was attended by Dr. Kuong Lo, Director of the Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department, the Governors of the eight districts and other relevant officials.
"We should strengthen our health system again, not that we have not done this work, but we need to strengthen our health services at all levels to communicate with health and volunteers," she said. "We also need to strengthen to treat malaria in our brothers and sisters when they arrive at the hospital or health center."
At the same time, Ms. Chak Heng also requested the provincial health department to take care to supply medicines and equipment related to malaria. The Department of Health needs to continue to spread the word about malaria and dengue fever so that they can clean the environment around their homes, such as cans, tires and anything related to mosquito nets, clean up.
And if there is malaria or fever, bring her children to the health center, not to treat private doctors in the village who do not have the proper profession, open without rules, just know the injection.
Dr. Kuong Lo said that we need to work together to eradicate malaria in accordance with the national policy set by 2025.
At the same time, Mr. Kuong Lo also expressed his happiness that our country is committed to eradicating malaria by 2025. He said that compared to neighboring countries, we are doing faster than Laos, Thailand and Vietnam is committed to eradicating malaria by 2030.
Mr. Kuong Lo continued that regarding the problem of malaria and the way we need to eradicate the disease, the Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department is always active in all districts throughout the province, such as distributing mosquito nets, bed nets, hammocks, soaking medicine, as well as promoting Clean the environment around the house in order to eliminate tiger mosquito nests as well.
