Arrested 5 masterminds and their accomplices and confiscated more than 2 kg of drugs in Banteay Meanchey province
(Banteay Meanchey): Police in Banteay Meanchey province have identified a total of five suspected ringleaders and drug traffickers and more than 2 kilograms of drugs after police launched a crackdown operation under the direct command of Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Ace Cam. Banteay Meanchey in the area of Serei Sophorn and will continue to crack down on the suspect's rented house in Siem Reap by finding drugs hidden in the room on September 19, 2018.
Brigadier General Chap Sophearth, Deputy Commissioner for Crime Prevention, said that the police force cracked down on the five drug suspects, who were partisans and the masterminds of the drug bust, after a period of police investigation. One month ago, he used secret measures to crack down on drug suspects who have been cracked down on in Banteay Meanchey province.
The deputy commissioner said that the suspects were involved in drug trafficking in three provinces: Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap and Battambang. During the crackdown, the police confiscated 8,764 methamphetamine tablets weighing 799.94 grams, 1,995.01 grams of frozen methamphetamine, 8.51 grams of ketamine and 2.96 grams of ecstasy. 4 drug scales, 4 small arms, including 1 air weapon, 2 cars.
According to the commissioner, the police have continued to search for and arrest some suspects involved in the drug bust.
Mr. Meas Chanpiseth said that the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Prosecutor's Office is highly committed with the authorities to effectively crack down on drugs, reduce and eliminate drugs in the territory of Banteay Meanchey.
He added that drugs have a serious impact on Cambodian society, especially drug users can go to commit acts of theft, robbery, violence, affecting social security.
