Two Suspects Seize Chinese Bag in Tonle Bassac Sangkat, Chamkar Mon District
(Phnom Penh): Two suspects, one a student of Phsar Doeum Thkov High School and the other a carpenter, who seized a Chinese bag on Street 294, Village 4, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh, were arrested by the police force of the Bureau of Serious Crimes. The Criminal Police Department cooperated with the Chamkar Mon District Police Force to crack down.
Colonel Cheav Vibol, Director of the Office of Serious Crimes, said this morning, September 20, 2018, that the crackdown operation on September 19, 2018 was carried out under the direction of General Dr. Neth Savoeun Akka. National Police Commissioner, Director of the Central Department of Judicial Police and under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department, in collaboration with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
According to the confession of the suspect, who cracked down when he saw two Chinese people walking on the street with a long bag, they saw it, so they rode a motorbike to the scene and snatched the bag from the victim and rode the motorbike. Escape to Wat Toul Tompong to check the shocking material.
The suspects are currently being processed by the specialized police force to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
Jack Ma's promise to create jobs in the United States came during a meeting with US President Donald Trump more than two years ago. But due to the current trade war, the Chinese billionaire claims that his company can no longer fulfill this promise.
"The commitment is based on the friendship between the United States and China, as well as cooperation and bilateral trade between the two countries," Jack Ma said in an interview with Xinhua on Wednesday. "But the current situation has destroyed this promise, and there is no way to fulfill this promise."
Despite ongoing talks, a trade war between the United States and China remains unresolved. Not only that, the current conflict is exacerbated after the United States announced a $ 200 billion tariff increase on Chinese products, while China retaliated with a $ 60 billion tariff increase on US products.
But the tax increase is not over yet, with US President Donald Trump warning of an additional $ 267 billion if Beijing dares to retaliate against the United States. This morning, the Minister of Education visited the teachers at Preah Sisoth School to solve some phenomena and for the teachers to vote on whether to change the principal.
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, this morning, September 20, 2018, met with teachers at Preah Sisowath High School to solve some problems, especially these days, which are protests that do not want to have. The change of principal as well as the issue with the unfortunate word that this school will be transformed into a private school.
According to Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, in the opening meeting, which allowed the media to listen for a while, he concluded that today there will be a secret ballot to decide whether to keep the principal of this school. Or have to change out? He said that the exchange will be decided by a majority vote of teachers who teach at Sisowath Quay.
It should be noted that during these two days, teachers at Sisowath Quay and some students came out with a series of protest banners against the "New Generation NGS" program in Sisowath Quay under the pretext that the program This leads to a division between teachers and teachers, students and students.
