The Minister emphasized that in the past, the Royal Government has set four priorities: roads, water, electricity and people to promote the development of the country, the order of all these priorities has been changed according to each stage of the Rectangular Strategy. For the sixth term, the Royal Government continues to focus on the four priority areas, leaving "people" as the first priority.
In addition, the Minister also informed about the priority work that the Ministry of Commerce must implement to strengthen Cambodia's capacity to promote integration into the regional and global economy, especially the preparation for the effects of trade wars. Karma and changes in the world economy.
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, confirmed that during this period, the owners of world-famous clothing brands, together with the Royal Government, employers and unions, as well as stakeholders are discussing the project. Establish a collective agreement aimed at improving the garment sector, including ensuring orders for garments from Cambodia is also an important objective.
The Minister made the remarks after a working meeting with a delegation of world-renowned apparel trade representatives led by Frank Hoffer, Executive Director of the Action Plan for Working Conditions Change in the Garment Industry (ACT) today. September 19, 2018 at the Ministry of Labor.
For the discussion of this collective agreement, it is necessary to attract more stakeholders, including buyers, because if there is an agreement to form this collective agreement, the buyers must also ensure that cooperation will continue. Long-term operations with suppliers in Cambodia can take up to 4 years or 5 years or more.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng expressed his optimism that in the future, the ACT project will continue to be discussed in order to achieve the signing of a collective agreement as described above.
The ACT project is a new agreement between a number of world-class brands, retailers and unions to transform the textile and garment industry and achieve fair wages for workers through collective bargaining at the sectoral level. With support in revising the order form and brand owners.
The purpose of the ACT is to be internationally committed to achieving a fair wage in a sector, establishing a framework in which all stakeholders, including brand owners and retailers, unions, factories, enterprises and the government, can implement their responsibilities. Responsibility and its role in achieving a decent wage.
