(Phnom Penh): The 32 former US Embassy security guards who were fired by the embassy for no apparent reason resumed their petitions to the US Embassy on the afternoon of September 19, 2018, changing from seven conditions. There are only four points to facilitate solving problems for them.
The four new points written in the petition to the embassy of this superpower include: 1. Demanding justice, presenting evidence and dropping charges, Second: Demanding 6 months' compensation in accordance with the Labor Law. 3: Complain about the violation of individual rights and 4: Claim for compensation for mental illness for defamation.
The 32 former embassy security representatives who submitted the petition to the embassy remain adamant that the US embassy's dismissal was a purely embassy-organized, not a faulty, and even more impossible. Furthermore, the embassy alleges that all 32 of them were guilty of the same offenses. They stated that if they did not want them to accuse the US Embassy of being the mastermind, show them the evidence.
However, former US embassy staffers also pointed out that after submitting the petition, they gave the embassy one week and if the embassy did not respond, they would ask Phnom Penh City Hall to protest. He also demanded that the US Embassy provide evidence of the eviction.
Please be reminded that on June 19, 2018, more than 20 out of 32 former employees who worked in the US Embassy from 5 to more than 20 years protested in front of the US Embassy on Street 96, Sangkat Wat Phnom, Daun Penh district, for the embassy of this great democracy to solve the case of firing them from work without a clear reason and without proper evidence.
