This surprise and surprise happened after the teachers at Sisowath Quay and some students on September 18 and 19, 2018 came out with a series of protest banners not wanting to have a program "School New Generation NGS ”in Sisowath Quay on the grounds that this program leads to a division between teachers and students and students.
What is NGS New Generation School? New Generation Schools is the Royal Government of Cambodia's education system reform program, a new development path in the current education system that helps establish autonomous public schools.
The idea for education system reform was initially initiated by KAPE, the largest local organization focusing on education in Cambodia, and was later approved and funded by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. Their pilot program, the Beacon School Initiative, was established in 2014 in Kampong Cham, and as the program expanded, the school became a new generation of schools.
The goal of the new generation of schools is to establish public schools that maintain the highest standards of education through large-scale investment and focus on strengthening transparency and accountability by changing the way schools are managed. This is in contrast to the traditional approach of the government, which always distributes all funds equally.
Without school management responsibilities, facilities such as science laboratories will not be used to their full potential because teachers are too busy to teach, should take money back part time, and are biased. Students should study better than students who do not have the money to study.
The new generation of schools is trying to solve this problem by completely eliminating such practices. Teachers are meticulously selected and receive many benefits, such as scholarships to strengthen teaching virtues and integrity. It has been observed that in this new environment, teachers no longer have to compete with each other to attract students who are students, and this makes this quality improvement run smoothly.
Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports spokesman Dy Campoli told Fresh News on September 19, 2018 that the new generation of schools is a new curriculum that the Ministry of Education has implemented in the pilot phase in 2015. . This practice is done in both primary and secondary schools in order to improve education in Cambodia, as in some countries in the region and the world.
The spokesman also claimed that the new school curriculum is focused on integrating technology into the education of both learners and teachers, as well as providing a wide range of learning materials. In particular, the study time is longer than the old curriculum.
What is interesting is that the new generation of school curriculum focuses on eliminating part-time or so-called learning and the sale of documents that lead students to pay informally for their studies. They.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports also responded to suggestions that the new program would require about $ 300 a year in tuition from teachers, parents and students at Sisowath Quay. According to Mr. D. Campoli, this payment is a contribution to support the implementation of the new curriculum and is based on the principle of volunteering, that is, if parents can afford to pay and parents of poor students do not have to pay.
According to the statistics of the exam, the results of the previous bankruptcy exam between the students of the old curriculum and the students of the new curriculum are very different, that is, the students of the new curriculum have a higher pass rate than the students. Learn from the old curriculum. The implementation of the new curriculum has been highly appreciated by students and parents alike, resulting in a much better knowledge base compared to the old curriculum.
Regarding the payment of contributions to support the implementation of the new curriculum, about $ 300 per year, some parents said that this amount is not much compared to the study in the old curriculum, because the old curriculum, if you do not pay the regular fee. But students have to spend a lot on part-time study and buy documents.
According to inquiries from both students and parents, the new generation school is a new curriculum under the Ministry of Education's efforts to reform towards a quality education system. But why are some teachers in Preah Sisowath High School dissatisfied with this educational program and trying to sow the unfortunate word that public school is turned into a private school?
It has been suggested that these protests are for the benefit of the nation rather than the common good of the nation, as the new curriculum will cause teachers to lose their daily income through part-time teaching as well as the sale of documents. To students and so on.
In order to make the implementation of this new generation school curriculum successful in 2016, the Ministry of Education has also launched a policy on this new generation school. This policy sets out a number of points to ensure a high quality and effective education.
