According to the report, 2,091 helmets and goggles were inspected on September 19, 189 education helmets and 377 glasses were fined.
For the results of the 19-day inspection from September 1 to 19, the police inspected 54,680 vehicles and found 11,227 offending vehicles (74% motorcycles), of which 4,356 were educated. And fined 6,871 units. CamControl Officers Find Petrol Stations and Depots in 4 Dangkor Districts
As a result of checking the quality and quantity of fuel of 6 stations at the above location, there are 2 locations selling fuel compliant in terms of both quantity and quality, 2 locations that do not comply with quantity and 2 locations that do not comply with quantity and quality. For the retail price, all 6 locations have complied with the notification of the Ministry of Commerce.
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia and Visa have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to continue cooperation on financial literacy projects in Cambodia through the launch of a mobile financial literacy program in Cambodia. September 18, 2018 yesterday.
This is the second year that the National Bank of Cambodia and Visa have collaborated on a financial literacy project in the country. In 2017, Visa partnered with the National Bank of Cambodia to support the publication of the financial education handbook “Let! Talk about money "30,000 copies and distributed in many schools across the country through the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Ms. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said, "Financial literacy is a key factor in boosting the financial environment and protecting financial clients, which will contribute to a more equitable economic growth." "Therefore, gaining financial knowledge is no longer an option, but it is a necessity."
She added that the project is a new step towards promoting the rights of people as financial clients in a fast-growing economy. This project is possible due to the cooperation and support of Visa. Taking this opportunity, the National Bank of Cambodia would like to thank Visa for its contribution to this project and to increase the level of financial literacy of the Cambodian people. ”
Visa, a leading private financial literacy company, has been developing educational programs for people of all ages around the world for 21 years, believing that advanced financial literacy helps people manage Budget and strengthen its livelihood.
Ms. Chum Monica added that our company is very fortunate to have partnered with the National Bank of Cambodia on this program. Community engagement and awareness of local challenges are invaluable to the success of our program, and Visa will continue this partnership.
She said that with the launch of the “NBC-Edu” mobile financial education program, Visa and the National Bank of Cambodia will continue to distribute 8,000 financial education books, 1,800 T-shirts and 1,600 bags. Published for the purpose of promoting the importance of financial literacy more widely.
