Cambodia to Host Two-Day "Bag of T-Shirts for Asia - Phnom Penh Conference"
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia will host the Asia-Pacific Forum for Asia - Conference on Joint Development and Winning "Joint Efforts to Bring China-Cambodia Economic and Trade Cooperation into a New Era" »
The event aims to help Chinese entrepreneurs who come to Cambodia to better understand Cambodia's business environment and related policies while introducing the Asia Forum to the Cambodian government and business community.
Li Baodong will lead 70 business leaders from China to attend the conference. The conference will be attended by 70 Cambodian delegates to be invited by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and about 70 executives from Chinese enterprises in Cambodia, Cambodian state and government leaders, as well as senior officials. Expect to interact with participants.
The Boao Forum for Asia (BFA) is a non-profit international non-governmental organization based in China and the most famous and important Boao Forum for Asia for leaders from government, business and universities in Asia and the Pacific. Others to share perspectives on key issues in potential areas around the world.
The Boao Forum for Asia is committed to promoting regional economic integration and bringing Asian countries closer to their development goals.
19 people die of alcohol poisoning in Malaysia!
KUALA LUMPUR: At least 19 people have been killed and many more are being treated in hospitals after suspected cases of alcohol poisoning in recent days in Malaysia. . This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday evening, September 19, 2018.
According to the Malaysian Ministry of Health, of those affected, three were Malaysians, 48 were foreigners from Myanmar, Nepal, Bangladesh and India, and 19 were killed and some were in critical condition. All of them ate different types of whiskey and beer from the shops on Monday earlier this week.
Samples of the alcohol were collected during the investigation and sent to a laboratory for testing.
