The book "Phnom Dangrek, Unforgettable" is the work of Oknha Kouch Mengly, Founder, Chairman and CEO of Mengly J. Kouch, 250 pages, published by Mengly J. Kouch University Press in May. 2018. This book is a true life story of the family of the tycoon who fled from Battambang province to a camp on the Thai-Cambodian border, intending to flee to a third country in the cause of finding peace for life.
The tycoon said that wandering in the bamboo forest, sleeping in the water, begging, combined with life from childhood and going through the black-shirt regime of his youth and family were revealed through the book. "Phnom Dangrek is an unforgettable place." He said that he always welcomes if you want to take this book to translate into other languages, because there are many Cambodians abroad who do not know the Khmer alphabet are wanting to read this historical book.
He encouraged the team to write in foreign languages, including Chinese and English, if possible after the Khmer language. According to Mr. Men Sambo, there are many tourists who come to visit Cambodia constantly, so they always want to know the history of Cambodia, and the production of other languages is one of the things that bring foreigners to know more about Cambodia.
Phnom Penh Dry Port Control Officer Continues to Inspect Goods at Orussey Market for Chemicals
(Phnom Penh): In order to protect the health of the people, Mr. Kong Vuthy, Deputy Director of Chong Phnom Dry Port Branch, led the subordinates in cooperation with the officials of the Department of Commerce, Sangkat Orussey 2 Market Commission and some shops in Khan 7 Makara to inspect goods and Research to prevent defective goods that some crooks steal to sell on the market on September 19, 2018.
During the operation, Mr. Kong Vuthy said that his professional officers conducted a preliminary test for banned chemicals on goods such as: yellow noodles, noodles, beef fiber, meatballs, beef, pork, pork, cucumber, squid, shrimp, dried fish, fish, sausage as a result. No banned chemicals were found, and after the inspection, the team took some vegetable samples and sent them to the laboratory of the General Department of CamControl to find other banned chemicals.
He also instructed all vendors to display their products in accordance with the technical specifications, distinguishing between products containing toxic substances and food, prohibiting the display of products, beverages, sun exposure and the sale of expired products. Also original.
He also called on traders, distributors, wholesalers, retailers, manufacturers, importers and distributors to have a clear source before accepting sales and stop adding chemicals to food products that harm consumers' health.
Mr. Kong Vuthy said that these activities were carried out according to the order of the head of the delegation in charge of the General Department of CamControl and the head of the Phnom Penh Dry Port Branch, who thought about the safety and health of the people, and this activity was done like rain. Exploring the significance of the North-South Korea Joint Agreement after the Second Moon-Kim Summit in Pyongyang
