Tycoon Try Pheap sues two journalists for publishing false and provocative information, the two journalists are detained by the authorities
The arrest of the above journalist was made at 2:05 pm on September 17, 2018 at Sangkom Thmey village, Thmor Da commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
Veal Veng District Police said that the two TNM journalists were arrested by the police: Min Phon, male, 39 years old, Cambodian, currently residing in Dey Krahorm Village, Thamma Or Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province, and Sarak. Dara, Male, 38 years old, Nationality Khmer, Currently living in Damnak Thom 2 Village, Sangkat Meanchey, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
The arrests of the two journalists were carried out following a complaint by the Thmor Da commune authorities and Tycoon Try Pheap's MDS company and an order from the Pursat Provincial Court. The lawsuit casts doubt on both TNM journalists for inciting and disseminating false information.
