Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this remark on September 19, 2018, when he met with a total of 27,444 workers from 24 factories in Kampong Speu province.
This re-announcement was made on the occasion that Samdech met with a total of 27,444 workers from 24 factories in Kampong Speu province in Svay Teap village, Ang Por Peul commune, Kong Pisey district on the 19th. September 2018.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government estimates that it will spend about 10 million dollars to support pregnant and maternity workers each year. But so far, the Royal Government has spent only 17 billion riels, equivalent to more than 4 million dollars to support 42,000 pregnant and childbirth workers with up to 43,000 children (some workers have children Twins).
At this point, it means that the budget to spend 10 million dollars is not spent, Samdech Techo said that the reason for not spending is because some enterprises have not been registered with the PRC because only the registration. It is only the list of the SPDC that allows the workers and staff who work in those institutions to receive financial support from the Royal Government.
Noting this, the Prime Minister continued to call on the owners or employers of factories, enterprises, and work establishments to register with the CEC so that their workers and employees can benefit. Above that.
However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who is a talented Prime Minister in leading and gaining the respect of the people everywhere, also called on stakeholders, including the people, to implement the policy. All this because the Royal Government alone can not do this work to get better results. Senior Ministry of Tourism official: Cambodia is ready to welcome at least 3.3 million Chinese tourists by 2020
(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism Somara said that Cambodia is ready to welcome at least 3.3 million Chinese tourists by 2020, with the Ministry of Tourism planning a strategic plan to attract Chinese tourists. The White Book on China Ready for Chinese tourists will facilitate travel and provide various types of visas to Chinese tourists.
The Secretary of State said this on the occasion that he led the Ministry's working group on behalf of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, to meet with the delegation of the Kunming Tourism Development Committee at the Sokha Phnom Penh Residence Hotel on the morning of September 19, 2018. The event was also attended by a delegation from the Kunming Tourism Development Committee and representatives of the Ministry of Tourism.
(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Net Pheaktra, said on September 19, 2018 that according to the report of environmental officials in Phnom Penh, about 2,700 tons of solid waste was generated. Per day.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment emphasized that the growth of waste in Phnom Penh and in other cities is our concern and it is necessary for all relevant institutions, people from all walks of life to participate in the management of waste that they create properly. Avoid damaging the environment, destroying the beauty of your community.
The increase in garbage in Phnom Penh and in other cities in Cambodia now, Mr. Net Pheaktra explained that due to population growth, changes in people's lives and customs of consumption and packaging and processing. Garbage is still low. These factors have increased the amount of solid waste.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment also pointed out that the increase in the amount of solid waste is one of the main problems in the challenges of environmental management in Phnom Penh and in the cities that require joint cooperation to prevent Reduce environmental pollution and impact on people's health by paying attention to proper solid waste management.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that in order to improve the beauty, order and hygiene of the public environment, as well as to prevent pollution of land, water and air caused by improper waste management in a technical manner, all parties must pay attention to Managing the waste it creates.
"If people and business owners, traders in markets, services, restaurants, markets and entertainment venues have to sort garbage according to technical standards, that is, separate waste between organic waste such as plastic waste and hazardous waste," he said. "And do the packaging properly."
"If everyone participates in these waste sorting methods, the rate of waste disposal will be minimal and other waste can be used and recycled, providing benefits and income," he added. "People," he said.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment stated that each factory, enterprise, handicraft and company must properly organize solid waste storage facilities and separate recyclable or recyclable solid waste from solid waste. Must be discarded.
He stressed that it is strictly forbidden to throw solid waste on the streets, public places, open fields, sewage systems or public water sources or on private land. Incineration of solid waste is strictly prohibited without the permission of the Ministry of Environment or the Department of Environment.
At the same time, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra said that in environmental protection, the Ministry of Environment has delegated power to sub-national administrations through the provision of environmental sanitation services. In the face of challenges, he said, some municipal administrations are still unwilling and unaware of the duties and responsibilities of waste management, urban solid waste, liquid waste and other environmental pollution issues. No.
The Secretary of State further stated that the quality of garbage collection and transportation of service providers is still limited and most towns do not yet have proper landfills in accordance with the technical guidelines, which requires all stakeholders to participate. Each.
Meanwhile, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra emphasized that people's participation and awareness about littering is still limited. The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment asked people to clean up the environment, pack and store garbage properly. Cleaning the environment around us is a necessity.
"If our house is clean, our village is clean, our public squares are clean, there is no garbage, no plastic bags, it means that we have contributed to building national values, enhancing the prestige and honor of the Khmer nation and for the well-being of all of us, because the environment is our problem. All together. "So we have to work together for the environment." Mr. Neth Pheaktra called for more.
