Two water wells were handed over to the communities of Kanseng Leu and Ta Tok Keut villages, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province.
(Siem Reap): Two Aphrodite pump wells were handed over to the community of Kanseng Leu village and Tatork Keut village in Chan Sor commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province on the morning of September 19, 2018 in the presence of Ms. Kuoy Nalin Khim Bunsong, Deputy Chairman Provincial Branch Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross and Associates.
In his welcoming speech, Mr. Mak Pros, District Red Cross Sub-Branch President and Governor of Sotnikum District, pointed out that in some villages, there is a shortage of clean water, which in the past, people used unsanitary water such as wells. Small hands, ponds, streams and so on.
According to the report of Mr. Su Sam An, Director of the Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, this is the 30th and 31st wells of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Siem Reap Province, which has benefited the people of both communities to use both dry and rainy seasons. No worries like before.
Speaking on that occasion, Ms. Kuoy Nalin Khim Bunsong talked and handed over water wells to the people in Kanseng Leu and Ta Tok Keut villages in Chan Sor commune who lack clean water for daily use.
In that, she also brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as Dr. Chairman of the Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, who always cares for all citizens. Regardless of caste, color, creed, religion, or political affiliation regarding health and hygiene.
Ms. Kuy Nalin Khim Bunsong also said that health is a major factor for all of us, so clean water is also a necessary factor for all of us in our daily lives to consume water permanently, water is energy. Human, animal and plant organs.
On the other hand, these two wells are also new achievements for the people in Kanseng Leu and Ta Tok villages to use for everyone, which does not cause the problem of water shortage in both the dry and wet seasons and to cultivate common crops. Combine well.
She also thanked the Chinese philanthropist Uy Sukuch for providing these two wells to the people of Chan Sor commune, Sot Nikum district, which shows the generosity to contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia. Reduce people's poverty by improving the use of clean water and for the well-being of the people "Water is the source of life".
She also encourages you to grow mixed crops near your home to facilitate your life and daily life, and we do not have to worry about the lack of water for use. She also said that this is the rainy season, please be careful about the health of young children, if you find it uncomfortable, send them to the nearest health center.
She also instructed the people in both communities to take good care of this well for the benefit of your long-term use in the future, the most important issue is the health of the community as well as the health of people with poor children. . In that, she also brought some gifts to distribute to the people who participated in the handing over ceremony, each receiving 1 sarong and 10,000 Riels.
Minister of Agriculture requested the Food and Agriculture Organization to cooperate with professional officials of the Ministry of Agriculture to strengthen the rubber sector
He informed the Minister that by noting the family rubber farmers facing serious challenges, especially on the issue of falling natural rubber prices, climate change and declining yields, FAO and CIRAD agreed. Establish a tripartite regional project between Cambodia, Thailand and Myanmar.
The senior official of the Food and Agriculture Organization stated that the project focuses on the system of observations, studies and detailed analysis of the results obtained of each country to compare and evaluate the situation as well as the effectiveness of Practice planting, harvesting rubber and making adjustments.
On this occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon thanked the FAO for supporting the Royal Government of Cambodia in the development of all sectors, especially agriculture.
The Minister also expressed his support and appreciation for the projects mentioned by the guests, increasing the capacity of professional officers and rubber farmers, reducing costs and labor, increasing yields, improving quality. Rubber, ensuring the sustainability of rubber trees and especially increasing household income is the key and goal of the Ministry.
At the same time, to implement this project successfully, the Minister requested the FAO to work closely with professional officials of the Ministry to try their best to strengthen the rubber sector in a sustainable manner.
