Leaders, Doctors, Military and Student Officers Congratulate General Dr. Chea Dara on His Appointment as a Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo in Charge of Rector of the National Defense University
(Phnom Penh): General Chea Dara, who was well-known to the general public and people all over the country, was known for his reputation while standing in the area of the Temple of Preah Vihear at a time when Cambodia was in a border dispute with Thailand.
During that time, General Chea Dara, who served as the Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in charge of the Preah Vihear Temple, used all kinds of strategies to lead the officers, deputies and soldiers to fight with the Thai side until they were successful on the battlefield. And on the international stage.
When the country is peaceful and there is no more war, on February 22, 2018, this General, who is good at theory and rhetoric, was entrusted by the Head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. New to be a personal advisor in charge of the Rector of the National Defense University.
For this new mandate, General Chea Dara has been trusted by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and has been appointed as a personal advisor in charge of the Rector of the National Defense University of the Ministry of National Defense, with the rank of Minister in addition to the current position. This is according to the Royal Decree of the Acting Head of State Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum dated September 18, 2018.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, continued to support the livelihood of veteran and well-known singer-songwriters in the mid-1990s while suffering from high blood pressure. Mr. Sous Sangvechar.
Mr. Sous Sangvachar, a well-known singer known to the Cambodian people as having a similar voice to Mr. Sin Sisamouth, is currently staying at a house in Prey Tea village, Choam Chao commune, Por Sen Chey district, Phnom Penh.
On the afternoon of September 18, 2018, Mr. Nop Channarin, Spokesman and Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of National Assembly Senate Relations and Inspection, handed over $ 1,000 as a gift from Mrs. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An to Mr. Sous Sang. It spies and families.
Mr. Nop Channarin stated that in the past as well as now, she has always taken care to help the family of Mr. Sous Sangveachar and other artists who are facing difficulties throughout the country.
Mr. Nop Channarin continued that Mr. Sous Sangvachar's health is now normal, only he is disabled and difficult to move from one place to another. However, he's tried to exercise regularly, never stopping, relying on crutches to accompany him.
Please note that Mr. Sous Sangvachar is now over 50 years old and has three children in his care. In the past, Mr. Sangvachar's children have received a 30% scholarship from Dr. Ly Chheng, Director General of BELTEI. But now he has a hard time supporting his children's education, he wants to ask for support from philanthropists so that their children can continue their education.
Chinese Defense Minister Congratulates Samdech Tea Banh on His Appointment as Cambodia's Minister of Defense
(Phnom Penh): General Wei Fenghe, Member of the Central Military Commission and Minister of National Defense of the People's Republic of China, sends a congratulatory message to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh on his appointment as Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense. Of Cambodia for this new mandate.
According to a letter from the Chinese Minister of Defense, received by Fresh News on the afternoon of September 19, 2018, "I have been informed that Samdech has been appointed Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Defense. Nation of the Kingdom of Cambodia again for this 6th legislature. On my own behalf and on behalf of the Ministry of Defense of the People's Republic of China, I would like to express my congratulations to Samdech. "
"I would like to join Samdech in continuing to work to make the relationship between the two countries closer, increase friendship, expand cooperation and maintain common security, and promote cooperation to the next level," he said.
