(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, who has always received the support of the people and workers, urged the owners or employers of factories, enterprises and work establishments that do not yet have a place to eat for workers in Its factories should prepare this necessary space appropriately to improve the working environment and contribute to reducing labor costs.
Such a call was made on the occasion of Samdech's meeting with a total of 27,444 workers from 24 factories in Kampong Speu province on September 19, 2018, which was held at Svay Teap village, Ang Por Peul commune, Kong Pisey district.
Seeing the urgent needs of workers at lunch, Samdech Techo Hun Sen immediately called on the factory owners to provide a suitable place for their workers to eat. At noon.
"Every factory needs to have a hospital, in addition to having a proper place to eat, I think in Phnom Penh there may be some difficulties in terms of location, but factories outside do not have to have difficulties in terms of location," he said. Eat the food of workers.
Samdech also said that in the past, more than 83% of factories have already set up a hospital for their workers, but for factories that do not have a hospital, please set up as soon as possible, especially the place to eat. Food is also a necessity for workers in Cambodia because this is part of the concern for the well-being of workers.
In addition to appealing to factory owners or employers, the head of the Royal Government also called on workers to increase their work capacity in each factory to increase productivity.
The call for such workers comes amid complaints from employers about productivity issues, as the minimum wage for workers continues to rise every year.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on the factory owners and workers to work together to maintain a better working environment in the factory to increase productivity, increase exports and for progress in the textile, garment and footwear sector. Both related sectors.
