Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of Meeting with Nearly 30,000 Workers in Kampong Speu Province
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Wednesday, September 19, 2018, continued to hold talks with a total of 27,444 workers. People from 24 factories in Kampong Speu province. The meeting took place in Svay Teap village, Ang Por Peul commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech was really pleased to meet the workers again in the new government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his failure in the past two weeks due to the busyness of forming a new government and completing missions in China and Vietnam.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for the first time, Samdech had to deliver two different speeches in two different meetings and in two different countries in just four hours during his mission in China. And Vietnam.
* Samdech Techo said that it was a fatigue for that mission, but Samdech was happy because he worked for the benefit of the nation and the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated that on September 27, he will attend the United Nations General Assembly in New York, USA. In this General Assembly, Samdech Techo will also deliver a speech.
* Samdech Techo stated that this year, Samdech did not attend the Pchum Ben festival because he was busy visiting abroad, namely attending the Japan-Mekong meeting and other meetings.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen warned some people that the election in Cambodia only has the Commune / Sangkat Council Election in 2022 and the National Assembly Election in 2023, there will be no re-election as mentioned and desired. That one.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that bringing Kem Sokha home was a court decision to ease some pressure. Samdech Techo said that the case of Mr. Kem Sokha has not been acquitted at all, just change the place of detention for humanitarian reasons.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that there may be considerations from the legal point of view of arranging the detention of people in the house.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked all the workers who went to the polls to support the democratic process. In particular, vote for the Cambodian People's Party to support the development process and maintain peace.
* The head of the Royal Government stated that roads and wells must be rehabilitated after floods and flash floods.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the promotion of national economic growth continues to pay attention and expects that by the end of the sixth term of the Royal Government, the income of the people will increase to more than 2,000 US dollars per year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this year has been 19 years that the Royal Government led by Samdech has set a policy to deploy factories to the provinces to provide employment opportunities for people.
* The Prime Minister continued that the effort to deploy factories to the provinces is a good policy and can also be said to be a success.
* Samdech Techo stated that the bombing killed only one group or one place, but if the economic bomb explodes again, it will kill the people of a country, which requires high attention on this economic issue.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated that during the Pchum Ben festival, 50,000 Riels will be donated to all types of civil servants and will be paid before Pchum Ben.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that it is very difficult to bring happiness like now, so no evil group can come and destroy this happiness.
In this morning's conversation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on the factory owners and workers to work together to maintain a better working environment in the factory.
* The Prime Minister also requested the factory owners to provide a suitable dining area for workers.
* Responding to the complaints of factory owners about the productivity of workers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on all workers to increase their capacity to increase productivity in production.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on factories, enterprises and establishments to register with the National Social Security Fund so that workers can benefit from the policies of the Royal Government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen appealed to workers not to block the road to protest for other issues, such as demanding compensation for the boss ran away. Samdech Techo confirmed that Samdech did not allow workers to lose money, and Samdech has already released $ 22 million to solve this issue.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that taking the road as a hostage to protest is not a good thing because it does not affect the factory owner, but it affects the passengers, especially it can affect those who have to go to the emergency services Urgent at the hospital as well.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during his upcoming meeting with the Secretary-General of the United Nations in New York, he would inform the Secretary-General of the United Nations that he was ready to expand to other countries in the mission. Keep the peace.
* Samdech Techo stated that before going to bed, almost every night, Samdech always listened to the advice of Ngoy and Achar Ou Chong.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that tomorrow, Samdech will allow German MPs to pay a courtesy call and discuss some work.
