Banteay Meanchey Provincial Authorities Call on Residents of Daun Moul and Prek Samrong Villages in Mongkul Borei District to Examine Their Land Plans Posted at Wat Rattanasampov Phal
(Banteay Meanchey): In the public posting ceremony of the systematic judgment on land registration on September 18, 2018, Mr. Suon Bavor, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, called on the people of Daun Moul and Prek villages. Samrong of Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district, please hurry to check the list of their plots, a total of 1,018 plots, which are posted at Wat Rattanasampov Phal (located in Daun Moul village).
Mr. Robora, Deputy Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Land Management, said that the public disclosure of the documents on the judgment of land registration was organized by the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Banteay Meanchey Province for verification. Data that the department's team has followed in the past.
Mr. Bora said that the public posting is for 15 days from September 18 in two villages, Daun Moul and Prek Samrong villages, Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district. Stakeholders verify their names, family status and plots, as well as protest in case of wrongdoing.
Regarding the fee for systematic land registration, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has agreed with the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, requiring only the landowner or land holder to pay for the systematic land registration service. "When I came to get the card."
He added that in the past, in Banteay Meanchey province, systematic land registration has been carried out and 121,595 real estate ownership certificates have been issued. Separately, for the plot data in the above two villages, there are 1,018 plots.
The Deputy Director of the Department requested the authorities at all levels, relevant institutions and the people who own the land in the above-mentioned jurisdiction to facilitate and cooperate well to implement the land registration successfully.
Mr. Suon Bavor said that in accordance with the Rectangular Strategic Policy of the Royal Government, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has paid close attention to land registration throughout the country to reduce land disputes and accelerate national economic development. .
The provincial governor also called on the people in the above village to hurry to check the list of plots in time, which is posted publicly in the area of Wat Rattanasampov Phal in Daun Moul village.
This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to meet with nearly 30,000 other workers in Kampong Speu province.
(Kampong Speu): Although after the formation of the new Royal Government, many jobs, both domestic and foreign, are besieging the Prime Minister of Cambodia, but meeting with workers from factories is still a task that Samdech Techo Hun Sen did not overlook that.
On Wednesday, September 19, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to meet with a total of 27,444 workers from 24 factories in the province. Kampong Speu. The meeting took place in Svay Teap village, Ang Por Peul commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province.
According to Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, the 24 factories that allow workers to meet with Samdech Techo Hun Sen are invested by 23 Chinese and one Korean investor. These factories include 8 garment factories, 10 shoe factories, 4 laundries, 1 toy factory and 1 Christmas tree.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng considered the presence of factories, enterprises and establishments in Kampong Speu province as a success of the policy of attracting investment, the national policy on employment and employment, the policy of industrial development in Cambodia, the policy on education, technical and vocational training and The National Social Protection Policy Framework of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
It should be noted that in order to promote the industrial sector to be stronger, Samdech Techo Hun Sen began to meet directly with workers since August 20, 2017. For more than a year now, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has met with workers, administration chiefs, division chiefs, team leaders a total of 56 times with a total of 793,783 participants. As for Kampong Speu province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has already met three times.
