Senior Minister Sun Chanthol attends the 2018 Global Infrastructure Cooperation Conference in Seoul, Korea
(Seoul, South Korea): On Tuesday, September 18, 2018, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport of Cambodia, participated in a conference on cooperation. Global Infrastructure 2018 in the Republic of Korea.
The conference is co-organized by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Korea and the International Association of Construction Contractors of Korea (ICAK).
On behalf of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, Deputy Minister Son Byeong Suk stressed the importance of infrastructure connectivity in job creation and resource development opportunities.
In addition, the use of advanced technology will help the country to build a "smart city". Understanding the importance of infrastructure connectivity, the Deputy Minister pointed out that the Republic of Korea now has more than 10,000 kilometers of highways as the country enters the fourth industrial revolution.
Korea has expressed its commitment to continue to contribute to the construction of overseas infrastructure that can benefit everyone in the region and the world.
In that conference, the delegation of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport of Cambodia actively participated in workshops on various projects, including: Workshop on: "Sewerage system in Cambodia".
The Global Infrastructure Cooperation Conference was established to improve ASEAN connectivity by supporting the development of infrastructure in all areas of the region, which has been held annually since 2013.
The conference aims to promote infrastructure cooperation between the government, major foreign clients, multilateral development banks, construction and engineering companies and many foreign companies.
