(Preah Vihear): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, on September 19, 2018, said that the old people are the ones who have great merits in the cause of helping to develop and build the country until today. He also considered the elders as the parents of the Preah Vihear provincial administration, which we all have to learn from.
He said this on the occasion that he, together with the Chairman of the Provincial Council, the Deputy Governor, the Director of Departments and Units, participated in the celebration of the 16th International Peace Day on September 21, 2018 and the Cambodian Day of the Elderly and the National Day of the Elderly and International Day of the Elderly, October 1, 2018 under the theme "Association of the Elderly Increases Unity to Develop the Community and Society".
Mr. Un Chanda said, "Why do we get together to celebrate this? What we are celebrating now is a tribute to the merits that our elders have left as a blessing, which is a great merit." It's important that as a leader, the successor of the next generation, it is imperative to learn from the heroic example of sacrifice of our elders in Preah Vihear province.
He continued, "Our elders who are sitting here are the ones who got their lives from the war. Many of our elders have given their lives in a war-torn country." We are meeting now on the occasion of a peaceful and prosperous country, a gathering of the great families of the Cambodian people under the shadow of peace under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, especially the government led by the Cambodian People's Party. .
In addition, all ministries, institutions, competent authorities, sub-national administrations and all organizations facilitate the Association of the Elderly, the Association of Former Civil Servants and the Cambodian Veterans Association and support the establishment of old associations in the community. Localize all communes to increase the spirit of solidarity to help each other among the elderly in Cambodia, especially the elderly, the disabled and the poor, the homeless.
In particular, the Cambodian Red Cross, development partners, philanthropists, national and international NGOs continue to increase their support activities in the form of humanitarian assistance in the form of food, materials, budget and technology to provide welfare services for the elderly who have been experiencing difficulties in both life and health. Physical and mental.
Professors, teachers in higher education institutions and general education schools continue to pay attention to provide education, morals, ethics, virtues and traditions, good traditions to all students and students to respect the elders and care. Old people, which is our good tradition.
In addition, every family in each community continues to strengthen the morals, ethics, virtues and good traditions of our Khmer, especially to educate children and the younger generation to respect the advice of parents, grandparents and respect the elders.
The message also emphasized that all compatriots should work together to nurture the elderly, the disabled, the poor and the homeless to have appropriate accommodation in each community by building old people's centers, especially in pagodas. And religious churches that can help provide shelter or food as practical as possible.
In addition, all public and private radio and television stations, as well as all news agencies, help spread the word about the achievements and achievements of the elderly for the younger generation, as well as society as a whole, and promote activities that highlight Caring for and promoting the well-being of the elderly in our Cambodian society.
At the same time, the Royal Government has paid close attention to the implementation of the policy on social security for the armed forces ready to retire through the provision of social land concessions and has been preparing a draft law on the social security system for the people of Cambodia.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has established the Cambodian National Committee for the Elderly, a mechanism for implementing policies for the elderly and supporting various programs and programs to help improve the well-being of the elderly throughout the country. The two Koreas have finally reached an agreement on the military, but the meaning has not been confirmed ...
