(Phnom Penh): US President Donald Trump has claimed that he is pleased to work with Cambodia to deepen US-Cambodian relations.
The statement of the President of the United States of America was made in front of the Cambodian Ambassador to the United States, Mr. Chum Suntory, during the presentation of his credentials on September 17, 2018.
According to a press release from the Cambodian Embassy in the United States, the President of the United States of America stressed the importance of Chum Suntory's mission in many ways, which means that the relationship is restored. More than 25 years after the Paris Agreement.
Donald Trump also expressed his admiration and amazement at the economic progress that Cambodia has achieved in the past as well as now.
"The economic development that your country has achieved so far is astonishing and the United States is proud to be a partner in this development," Donald Trump was quoted as saying.
"We know that Cambodia has the potential for greater development in the future, and we look forward to working together in the face of many challenges and opportunities," Tram said. "We anticipate progress in free and fair trade, regional security and responsible and democratic governance, and strive to expand cooperation in the field of general health."
The US President also reaffirmed his commitment to working better with the Cambodian Ambassador to deepen US-Cambodian relations. "I look forward to working with you to advance our common agenda and deepen relations between the two countries," he said.
During the presentation of the credentials, Mr. Chum Suntory also highlighted to the President of the United States some of the achievements that Cambodia has made in the socio-economic development of the past two decades after Cambodia achieved complete peace and stability in the past decade. 90.
The ambassador added that US bilateral trade and development assistance have made a significant contribution to Cambodia's growth.
