Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Asks South Korea to Accelerate Construction of Construction Technology Institute in Cambodia
(Seoul, South Korea): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, requested the South Korean Institute of Construction Technology (KICT) to expedite the construction of this construction technology training institute in Cambodia as soon as possible. Possible.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol made the request during a visit to the Korea Institute of Construction Technology in Seoul, South Korea on September 18, 2018.
The Senior Minister also informed about the current challenges related to the development of Cambodia's road infrastructure. The senior minister pointed out that the current traffic accidents caused by human factors and black spots kill about 5 people and injure 20 to 50 people a day.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol noted that Cambodia needs to improve the standard of road construction to reduce traffic accidents and maintain the quality of road infrastructure to be strong and durable.
The senior minister added that road repair technology is important because the southern parts of the country, such as Kampot, Kep, Sihanoukville and Koh Kong, receive heavy rains during the rainy season.
KICT has established a standard for modern Korean construction and signed a memorandum of understanding with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport of Cambodia on November 16, 2016.
