The Minister of Agriculture believes that the delegation of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship will be a success for the country after returning from the program "Southeast Asian Youth Ship and Japan"
This expression of hope and confidence was made on the occasion that Mr. Veng Sakhon allowed the youth delegation led by Mr. Srang Kimly, President of the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association to pay a courtesy call and ask for advice and wisdom before leaving. To attend the above program. This program lasts for 52 days from October 23 to December 12, 2018.
According to Mr. Sran Kimly, the Cambodian Southeast Asian Youth Ship Association was established by the General Assembly on November 7, 2004 with the aim of training young people with knowledge, experience, spirit and qualifications as youth representatives. Cambodia to participate in the SSEAYP program.
The SSEAYP program was organized by the Government of Japan with the active support and close cooperation of the 10 ASEAN member countries to strengthen and expand the friendship, solidarity and understanding between the youth of Japan and the youth of the 10 ASEAN countries.
At the same time, expand the knowledge and vision of young people about their world. Increase the spirit and clear skills of young people in international cooperation. Cultivate youth leadership in youth development and society. In fact, to date, the association has a total of 569 members who have participated in this beneficial SSEAYP program.
The Minister also gave some recommendations to the youth delegation, including:
1. Continue to make efforts to study, research and fill the gaps because the future is far away and especially while the country is completely peaceful and stable under the wise leadership of the head of the Royal Government.
2: Increase the spirit of responsibility and attention in capturing images as well as important development realities of other countries to study, understand and apply when returning home.
3. Gather good experiences and new technologies that are useful for strengthening and expanding capacity.
4: To know how to connect and learn about the development process of each country to help the Royal Government to transform the country into a high middle income country by 2030.
5: Continue to promote Khmer culture and traditions on the international stage, worthy of the Khmer people.
At the same time, the Minister hopes and believes that the youth delegation will be proud of the country's success, and the Minister also wished the 29 youth delegates a safe journey.
