Financial literacy is considered as a way to maintain a balance between the financial environment and financial stability. The National Bank of Cambodia initiates financial literacy programs in Cambodia and has always been active in promoting financial literacy to the general public.
Ms. Chea Serey, Assistant Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said, "Financial literacy is key to boosting the financial environment and protecting financial clients, which has contributed to a more equitable economic growth." "So gaining financial knowledge is no longer an option, but a necessity."
She added that the project is a new step towards promoting the rights of people as financial clients in a fast-growing economy. This project is possible thanks to the collaboration and support of VISA.
Ms. Chum Monica, Managing Director of VISA Cambodia, said, “VISA is proud to continue to work with the National Bank of Cambodia to improve financial literacy in Cambodia. "According to the Asian Development Bank, Cambodia's GDP growth of 7% in 2018-2019 indicates strong economic development."
"As people participate in the global economy, financial literacy is becoming more important in enabling people to benefit from these developments," she said.
