Singapore was without electricity for more than half an hour at midnight on Tuesday, causing a huge impact!
Electricity supplier SP Group has issued an apology with the promise to open an investigation into the power outage. The company added that electricity was restored at 1:56 a.m., 38 minutes after the power outage, but in some areas electricity was available at 3:30 a.m., while homes and shops or commercial buildings 146,797 houses were affected.
The power outage in Singapore is considered one of the most shocking on the island, as it is extremely rare in one of Southeast Asia's fastest-growing economies. But even though the country is modern and has invested billions of dollars in electricity infrastructure, it is still unavoidable. Importantly, so far, experts have not 100% concluded that the cause of the problem.
