(Phnom Penh): An elderly man left the district of Svay Rieng province with a package of vegetables, fish, meat to visit and send to his wife, who came to work as a factory worker in Phnom Penh, but unfortunately due to chronic tuberculosis, the man The father vomited blood and died suddenly in Toul Pong market.
The above incident happened on the afternoon of September 18, 2018 in Toul Pong Market, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh. The body of the victim, 52-year-old Kith Peat, was born in Romeas Hek district, Svay Rieng province.
According to the wife, before the incident, the victim, the husband, took a taxi from Svay Rieng province and packed fish, meat, vegetables to bring to Phnom Penh, the purpose was to visit his wife, who works in a factory in Toul Pong Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
