Government Spokesperson: Rong Chhun and his allies' threats to demonstrate to put pressure on the Royal Government is a violation of the law
(Phnom Penh): The spokesman of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Mr. Phay Siphan, said on the afternoon of September 18, 2018 that the threat of demonstrations to put pressure on the Royal Government of Cambodia by Mr. Rong Chhun, President of the Cambodian Trade Union Confederation and its allies. It is a violation of Cambodian law.
Mr. Phay Siphan wrote on his official Facebook page: "Defending sovereignty and independence, organizing demonstrations against the inauguration, forcing the Royal Government to follow foreign orders is a violation of Cambodian law."
Mr. Phay Siphan's remarks came after Mr. Rong Chhun warned to lead a demonstration after the Pchum Ben ceremony for the government to accept the EU's request to approve the decision on September 13, 2018 for the Royal Government of Cambodia to restore. Democracy and respect for human rights, as well as demanding that the Cambodian government release Kem Sokha to full freedom and pardon Sam Rainsy.
Mr. Phay Siphan continued that taking the excuses and content of the European Union, which has not yet issued any legal rules against non-cooperation with Cambodia, is an opportunity to create anarchy in Cambodian society and serve foreign politics. Only that is not really the Khmer interest.
Mr. Phay Siphan added that the Royal Government at all levels will take legal action to maintain sovereignty, independence and national unity without the cooperation of this person or this group network at any cost.
Mr. Phay Siphan stated: “I would like to reiterate to Mr. Rong Chhun and his party that the entire Cambodian people have already officially and publicly expressed their national unity through elections, Cambodia is a sovereign state. Exactly. The European Union is not a colony of Cambodia. ”
He added that Cambodia has had very good cooperation with each other for decades. In the case of bilateral and multilateral through ASEAN, Cambodia and the EU are the only dialogue, development and cooperation partners. In the statement of the European Parliament, that is his beliefs and political tendencies, but the congratulatory message and congratulations of the German Chancellor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen is already meaningful enough for Rong Chhun and his party.
He added that Cambodia and the European Union will remain partners forever, and in the near future political and economic forums can also confirm the strong intention for this cooperation. The Royal Government is continuing to discuss with the European Parliament all the challenges of mutual respect. Cambodian and Thai investors join hands to import fertilizers and pesticides to meet the needs of the Cambodian market.
