Preah Vihear CamControl officials warn all Thai traders to import quality goods to Cambodia, otherwise they will not be allowed to sell.
(Preah Vihear): In order to protect the safety, quality of food as well as the well-being of the people, Preah Vihear Provincial CamControl officials carefully inspected the goods imported from Thailand and put them up for sale at booths during the Thai trade fair in Preah Vihear Province. To ensure that these goods are of good quality and do not affect health, especially on food.
Mr. Duong Mony, President of CamControl Preah Vihear Branch, said that CamControl Preah Vihear Branch cooperated with the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities, including Preah Vihear Provincial Hall officials, to inspect the goods that were on display for sale. Usage dates imported from Thailand for sale at a one-week Thai trade fair in Preah Vihear city, Preah Vihear province.
Mr. Duong Mony added that the goods imported by Thai traders for sale at the trade fair in Preah Vihear province were inspected to see that none of the goods were defective or out of date. He also advised Thai traders to import quality goods, goods that have the correct packaging, have a clear production date, otherwise when officials check that the quality is not allowed to sell.
Mr. Duong Mony also appealed to all citizens and the public before buying anything, especially food that is packaged in cans, bottles or bags, to check the label or date that is posted or printed on Clear the cans or bottles to avoid spending money and buy items that are damaged or out of date to eat, which can affect health.
Cambodian Breeders Association reacts to Duke Duong Chhay urging people not to eat pork, the association says not to believe in this inspiration
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Breeders' Association reacted immediately to the posting of information and Duong Chhay's call not to allow Cambodians to eat pork and called on people not to believe this advertisement.
The reaction of the Cambodian Breeders Association came after Duke Duong Chhay on September 16, 2018 posted a picture of a dead pig claiming to be a dead pig in Vietnam and even called on the people Do not eat more pork either.
Through its official Facebook page, the Cambodian Breeders' Association on September 18, 2018 confirmed that the association closely monitors this information daily on pig raising, disease status and pig market situation, both domestically and abroad. Well.
Dissemination of vague information has angered Cambodian pig farmers because it could hurt the pork market in Cambodia. After a series of reactions from the association as well as the pig farmers, Duke Duong Chhay also came out to apologize for the mistakes in his advertisement.
However, Duke Duong Chhay also called on people to check carefully before buying meat to eat.
Ministry of Information bans the broadcast of the song "Only sincere" left by Khmer Living Production because it seriously affects the value of domestic workers
