(Phnom Penh): In connection with the third tripartite discussion on raising the minimum wage of workers in the textile, garment and footwear sector for 2019, employers have increased the wage figure from $ 175 to $ 176 The union side also reduced its demand from $ 192 to $ 189.
This was confirmed by Mr. Heng Sour, Deputy Chairman of the Secretariat of the Labor Advisory Committee after the tripartite technical working group meeting held on the morning of September 18, 2018 at the Ministry of Labor.
Mr. Heng Sour said, "Today, our tripartite technical working group met again and reached a new and more positive result, in which the employers increased the figure from $ 175 to "$ 176 for the new year minimum wage, and the union side has adjusted its demands from $ 192 to $ 189."
According to Mr. Heng Sour, the next meeting of the tripartite technical working group will be held on October 4, 2018, which is the last meeting. According to the schedule, on the afternoon of October 5, 2018, it is time for the Labor Advisory Committee to meet for the second time to review the proposal made by the tripartite technical working group on October 4.
In the opinion of the employer's representative, Mr. Kan Monica stated that although the minimum wage of workers in Cambodia is lower than in Vietnam, which is a competitor of Cambodia, but it is still higher than other competitors such as Myanmar, Bangladesh. Twice, so it makes the possibility of competition very difficult for Cambodia.
Mr. Kan Monica said that the wage setting must be done with the utmost caution because the impact is not only on the textile, garment and footwear sectors, but also on other sectors. At this point, he noted that employers in some sectors also want to add labor, but they seem to be hesitant because of the recent increase in wages for workers.
The representative of the employer side continued to call on the Royal Government to help reduce the price of electricity and reduce the fees from Camcontrol, Mr. Kan Monica claimed that if the Royal Government facilitates this issue for employers to invest in the textile sector. Garment and footwear in Cambodia will continue to move forward. A group of Chinese people arrested a Chinese man for pouring hot water, causing serious injuries, was arrested by the police
