(Kratie): Residents have requested the Kratie City Authority to take action against a giant sand truck transporting sand through Kratie City every day that is overloaded, which can cause damage to bridges and traffic jams.
Residents said that sand trucks passing through Kratie City every day could cause damage such as bridges, roads and traffic jams, and that the trucks were known to be carrying sand from a sand dredging site in Russey Char village. Thmor Kre, Chit Borey district, Kratie province, and another sand dredging site in Krakor village, Krakor commune, Kratie city.
Residents said that from the sand dredging site from Russey Char village to Kratie city, they had to cross two dilapidated bridges, Krakor Bridge and Andeng Daun Bridge. Passing more than 10 tons, but the sand trucks continue to transport without fear.
They also asked the Kratie municipal authorities to take action against the vehicles, saying that if they were allowed to continue, the bridge would collapse one day and there would be a traffic accident for the passengers.
