(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chheang Vun, Chairman of the Fifth Committee of the National Assembly, said that a liberal, multi-party democracy is not on the seats in the National Assembly, but on the will of the people who came out to vote without coercion. Forced.
Mr. Chheang Vun said this on September 17, 2018, after concluding the first meeting of the National Assembly Standing Committee in the new mandate of the National Assembly, which was chaired by Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
The reason for his statement was that some people suggested that Cambodia formed a one-party government that was inconsistent with the liberal, multi-party democracy enshrined in the Constitution. The chairman of the National Assembly's Fifth Committee stated, "In fact, a liberal, multi-party democracy is not based on the seats of the people in the National Assembly, but on the will of the people to vote. He has the right to vote for any party. Also.
He continued, "If there are candidates from many parties, it is multi-party and more than two parties to multi-party. And if I am not mistaken, in the past, the election in Cambodia was up to 20 parties. "So your people came out to vote democratically, according to the will of his choice."
Mr. Chheang Vun added that the people elected the 125 CPP and also elected other parties, but the insufficient number of votes could form a parliamentary seat. He considered that those who said that the Royal Government of Cambodia was not in line with democracy were the language of feudal lords.
According to the Chairman of the Fifth Commission, the Cambodian people who voted for the CPP are their rights. Mr. Chheang Vun asked the question, if the people are not allowed to follow their will, will they only follow foreign servants?
"Please confirm that someone with a bad tongue, he always gives this reason, that reason," he said. He did not think that 83% of the people went to the polls without coercion and voted for the CPP, which is the right of the people. Why want to force people to choose something else to satisfy those outside? Foreign? Foreign servants? Impossible. This is the will of the people. "The people are in charge of choosing their leaders."
