Immigration police continue to detain 9 Vietnamese nationals who came to stay and work illegally in Tuol Kork district
(Phnom Penh): The Joint Operations Team of the Investigation and Enforcement Department of the General Department of Immigration on September 17, 2018, continued to detain nine Vietnamese nationals who came to stay and work illegally.
Lt. Gen. Ouk Haysila, Director of the Investigation and Enforcement Department, said that the operation was coordinated by Mr. Seang Sok, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to inspect the shop. Coffee is located along Street 336, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Kor, Khan Toul Kork.
According to the director general of the department, after the operation, the specialized force found nine Vietnamese nationals who were staying illegally without passports and using incorrect documents.
After the operation, the nine Vietnamese nationals were taken to the General Department of Immigration for document inspection and further questioning.
(China): China's National Health Commission will allow online prescribing services for the purchase of certain common chronic diseases as part of efforts to promote better information sharing between health institutions. . This is according to a statement issued by the commission.
Doctors can now prescribe the right medication for patients online after reviewing the patient's medical history file stored electronically. Prescribers will also be allowed to dispense the medication after reviewing the prescription.
In the message, health institutions are asked to use medical history documents, which are electronic documents for the provision of consulting services, prescriptions, care and medical examinations, so that hospitals can share more information about their medical history.
Health care centers across China have also been asked to share information on diagnoses and treatments by 2020.
Health facilities are encouraged to provide convenient services to facilitate appointments, payment for treatment and reduce patient waiting times.
In addition, the proclamation also introduces the use of artificial intelligence (AI) technology for the detection and imaging of diseases and therapies through medicine to help increase work efficiency.
(China): Chinese companies that make advanced drones are looking to partner with Russian companies that make the same drones as the two countries want to deepen cooperation in technology.
China continues to deepen cooperation with Russia, not only in the general industry, but also in new industries such as drone manufacturing. China commends Russia for having top experts and scientists working in areas such as renewable energy, virtual intelligence and automation.
Many Chinese companies are pioneering the drone cooperation between China and Russia. Ehang, a drone manufacturer in southern China's Guangdong Province, is among the top Chinese drone makers that have partnered with Russian drone makers.
"Our cooperation will focus on the use of drones for industrial applications, such as sewer inspection, gas inspection, laser statistics and modeling," said Zhang Hunter, vice president of E-Hang. Russia has a very high level of technological knowledge on this work. But the fact that we incorporate that technology into drones is a whole different story. "This is what we are talking about with our Russian partner."
The partnership between the two companies took place at last year's China-Russia Expo in the northeastern Chinese city of Harbin. Many customers in Russia are very interested in e-shop drone technology.
Later, there was a coordination from an organization in Guangzhou, an organization that promotes scientific and technological cooperation between China and Russia, with Russia as a member.
Over the past 10 years, the organization has promoted thousands of Russian projects, bringing more than 500 Russian experts to China to assist Chinese companies in scientific work, such as new materials work. Save energy and big data.
"We have long-standing partnerships with 23 research institutes in Russia, such as the Russian Academy of Sciences," said Liang Zhengfa, deputy secretary-general of the Guangdong CIS International Coalition for Scientific and Technological Cooperation. Our offices at those institutions provide the latest information on Russia's technological achievements. "And we recommend suitable projects to Chinese companies that need them."
In addition to the general industry, China and Russia are also collaborating on new areas that are expected to boost economic growth for the two countries, including digital technology, automation and AI.
Liang says that when people think of Russia's industry, they often think of armaments, oil and gas. And very few people know that Russia is the originator of many new technologies and cultivates a lot of human resources in various fields.
What Russia does not have is a market as large as China's to enable these new technologies to be quickly deployed in industrial plants.
China's one-way belt media community focuses on promoting cultural cooperation between countries participating in the one-way belt initiative and disseminating the influence of Chinese culture on International stage since its inception three years ago.
Launched in 2016 by China International Television Corporation, along with other international media outlets, the One Belt One Road media community aims to promote cooperation and communication between TV stations in countries with the goal of helping development. Of the One Belt One Road Initiative.
Five new members joined the community during this year's summit in Xi'an, including the Arab Media Federation. To date, the community has mobilized 103 media outlets from 51 countries around the world.
At the summit, dozens of achievements were announced from the collaboration between China International Television Corporation and other countries, covering a wide range of topics, from stories about people's lives to China's efforts on reform work
"As all forms of media are growing rapidly in the future, our community will expand cooperation in the field of digital media and other channels of digital media," said Xin Jianing, deputy director of China International Television Corporation. . "Through digital media, we are able to increase our co-production volume and better content and quickly spread it around the world."
