The case of 5 disabled soldiers suing the inspector of Thpong district, Kampong Speu province for embezzling money of MP Hun Many has been resolved
(Kampong Speu): The case of five disabled soldiers in Thpong district, Kampong Speu province, who accused the district police inspector Hun Sokhorn of embezzling money from MP Hun Many, was resolved this weekend in the presence of the district governor. There will be the participation of the inspector as well as the five disabled soldiers.
As a result of the interrogation in the search for a solution, in fact, the five disabled people did not complain to the district inspector to the three institutions, including: the National Assembly, the Minister of Interior and the Anti-Corruption Unit, this is the case. Started by a deputy inspector, a police chief and two other police officers at the provincial police commission, they arranged and tricked the five disabled people to put their thumbprints on the complaint form.
The five disabled soldiers claimed with the district authorities that they had not complained to Hun Sok Hon to the Ministry of Interior, the National Assembly and the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU). Long Saroeun, deputy chief of the district criminal division, and Chea Ton, deputy district police chief, called them while they were transplanting rice in the fields to get a thumbs up for 50,000 riel.
They also said that on April 27, 2018, 46-year-old Long Saroeun alias Tum gave them a thumbs-up for not receiving 50,000 riel from Mr. Hun Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu constituency. Came to greet the disabled soldiers and distributed 50,000 Riels per family.
They said that on September 11, 2018, they saw Long Saroeun and Chea Ton and two other provincial police officers calling them while they were transplanting in the field to get their thumbs up again. He said that the four police officers did not read the contents of the paper to them, as they were not interested in suing anyone.
Later, many media outlets reported that the five of them had filed a complaint against Inspector Hun Sok Hon to the Ministry of Interior, the National Assembly and the ACU, alleging that he had committed corruption and embezzled 50,000 riel from each of them. . When they heard this, they expressed their anger at the four officials and falsified their medals. They went to complain to the district inspector, but they refused.
At the same time, they also requested and rejected the letter complaining to Inspector Hun Sok Hon to the Ministry of Interior, the National Assembly and the ACU because the complaint to the district inspector to the three higher units was organized by Long Saroeun. Deputy Criminal Division and Mr. Chea Ton, Deputy Police Inspector of Thpong District and two other provincial police officers to abuse Inspector Hun Sok Hon only.
Thpong district police chief Hun Sokhon also said he had not acted as charged. He said that this story was completely slandered by two people: Ton, the position of Deputy Inspector of Criminal Affairs, and Long Saroeun, the Deputy Chief of Criminal Division of Thpong District, because they had bad intentions, wanted to hurt him, wanted to tarnish his reputation. Wanting to be the district inspector only.
He said that Mr. Chea Ton was transferred from Mr. Sam Samuon, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Speu from Deputy Inspector General of Criminal Affairs to Deputy Inspector General of Immigration in early 2018 and was angry with him. Mr. Athikar said that when he was the Deputy Inspector General of Criminal Investigation, Chea Ton took the position to demand money for a cockfighting place and then arrested him, accusing him of being the perpetrator and many other things.
Mr. Lon Chenda, Acting District Governor, said that after the broadcast, he invited the five families to come and interrogate each other at Thpong District Hall to confirm the truth so that there would be no confusion. They did not give a thumbs up to sue Hun Sok Hon. Around this case, he will send a report to the provincial level to open a search for criminals who cheat people's fingerprints.
