(Sydney) - A potential and symbolic crop for Australia is now suffering after reports from distributors and consumers across the country that they have found needles embedded in the fruit. This type is fresh. This is according to the release by Xinhua on Monday morning, September 17, 2018.
Australian Minister of Health Greg Hunt has ordered authorities to investigate the cause of the sewing needles and needles in the strawberry. Nationwide, there are now six well-known strawberry distributors.
Police are now investigating and initially concluded that some employees who were unhappy with their work or had mental health problems were more likely to be behind harming consumers. Above this. In addition, the Food Safety Authority of Australia-New Zealand (FSANZ) has been asked to come forward with the Australian authorities to find out the exact cause.
