The Vietnamese man, Phuong Minh Kok, was arrested on November 29, 2016 at the Cambodia-Vietnam border checkpoint while signing for three containers of goods from Ecuador with a total of 24 tons of seafood. There were also more than 1,100 kilograms of cocaine hidden inside the sea fish.
