After the Cambodian crisis ended through the Paris Peace Accords of October 23, 1991, Dr. Beat Richner returned to Cambodia at the request of King Norodom Sihanouk to reorganize Kantha Bopha Hospital.
In 1992, he established the Kantha Bopha Foundation and reopened Kantha Bopha Hospital. Since the re-establishment of Kantha Bopha Hospital, Dr. Richner has worked hard to ensure the hospital's operation is based on three principles: free, quality and non-corrupt care.
After sacrificing for the cause of children and mothers in Cambodia for about 25 years, the doctor reluctantly left Cambodia in March 2017. Although he worked hard to raise hundreds of millions of dollars to treat Cambodian children, leaving Cambodia did not bring anything with him, only a black bag that he brought with him when he traveled to Cambodia in 1991. .
