(Phnom Penh): After Beat Richner, the founder of Kantha Bopha Hospital, passed away on September 9, 2018 in his home country of Switzerland, Kantha Bopha Hospital in Cambodia also held a memorial service for him at the hospital. On September 14th, coinciding with the 7-day and 100-day anniversary, Kantha Bopha Hospital held a ceremony to pay homage to Preah Ratanak Trai, Samathan Sil and Nimand Prosong Chamroeun Preah Borod and Preah Tesna.
On the morning of September 15, 2018, tomorrow, Kantha Bopha Hospital will invite 72 monks to count the feet of the monks to give birth and give food to the monks and then pass the ceremony to dedicate the merit to Dr. Beat Richner to calm down. Sok. This was confirmed by the Deputy Director of Kantha Bopha Hospital, Mr. Heng Sothy.
He added that seeing that many of our people continued to pay their respects to the late Dr. Beat Richner, Minister of Health, as well as the Kantha Bopha Hospital Funeral and Fund Committee decided to postpone his funeral at the hospital. Kantha Bopha for up to 100 days, facilitating our people who want to come and share their condolences, burn incense and pay their last respects to the deceased.
