Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Vows to Protect Kbal Chhay Forest at No Cost
(Preah Sihanouk): The Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Mr. Yun Min, is determined to protect the forest in Kbal Chhay area well, no matter what the cost, because the forest in Kbal Chhay area is the most important source of fresh water. Indispensable.
This statement was made on September 14, 2018, on the occasion of the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration re-planting seedlings in the area of Kbal Chhay, O'Arev point in Village 2, Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville. Some crooks have been clearing land to illegally occupy land.
Speaking at the reforestation ceremony, Mr. Yon Min once again warned that anyone involved in deforestation in Kbal Chhay would be prosecuted without any understanding, no matter what, the forest must be protected. This is absolutely to keep fresh water sources for use throughout Sihanoukville.
He added that the location in the restricted area in accordance with the spirit of Sub-Decree No. 116 of the Royal Government, which was looted by some crooks, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration will rehabilitate in collaboration with agricultural experts. All re-seedlings.
According to Mr. Nen Chamroeun, Director of the Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Agriculture, 5,500 saplings have been planted so far, including Korkir and Kranhong seedlings. According to the plan of the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, many more places are planned to be planted in Kbal Chhay area.
It should be noted that this Kbal Chhay area has been designated by the Royal Government as Sub-Decree No. 116 as a multi-use area and requires the protection of this forest to maintain fresh water sources for use in the whole of Sihanoukville.
Meanwhile, during the mandate of Mr. Yun Min, the provincial governor, seeing the real hardships of the people living in Kbal Chhay area, the government also decided to cut a small part of the land so that the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration could distribute it to the people as part of the policy of 5 meters. Multiply by 20 meters. However, it is observed that there are still some individuals who continue to steal, clear the forest and take over the land by dragging some brokers.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara orders Capital-Provincial Departments to protect social land concessions if they are violated, do not register
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, has ordered the Capital-Provincial Land Departments to protect social land concessions. He added that if there are violators, they must not be registered.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara issued such an order on the afternoon of September 14, 2018, when he closed the training course on measuring techniques with modern equipment at the Ministry.
The Deputy Prime Minister stated that "the goal of providing affordable housing is the main goal of our ministry, the capital and provincial departments. "Our province has social land concessions ... Please manage the land that is the target for this social work so that there will be no encroachment, and if it is encroached upon and occupied, do not register it."
According to the Deputy Prime Minister for the qualified land that has already taken control of the first step, he would like to request a review and can discuss with the provincial level. He said that if the place can build a house, please start immediately.
Mr. Pa Socheatvong Calls on Local CPP Members to Strengthen Work Activities to Help People Strong
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pa Socheatvong, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Party Committee and Chairman of the Meanchey District Assistance Team, called on local CPP members to strengthen their work to help the people more than the previous mandate.
At the same time, Mr. Pa Socheatvong also called on all CPP members in Meanchey district to continue to pay attention to the well-being of local people to be warmer than the previous mandate so that people have more confidence in Cambodian People's Party for this new mandate.
Mr. Pa Socheatvong made the remarks while attending a ceremony to summarize the results of the 2018 6th National Assembly Election and a solidarity dinner to celebrate the victory of the Cambodian People's Party at Modern 2 Entertainment Center along National Road No. 2 Sangkat Chak Angre Krom on September 14, 2018.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Pich Keo Mony, Chairman of Stung Meanchey II Sangkat Assistance Team, Mrs. Teav Thida, First Deputy Chairman of Stung Meanchey II Sangkat Assistance Team and about 500 members of Meanchey District Strengthening Team. .
At the same time, Mr. Pa Socheatvong called on all people to take care of the achievements that Cambodia has achieved now, especially to maintain peace for the whole society so that the Royal Government has more opportunities to develop the country. The people can afford to improve their lives and live happily.
(Siem Reap): What the public seems to be skeptical about the story of a young woman who hanged herself in Sangkat Sala Kamroeuk, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province, and it is claimed that she died because of a small exam, on September 14, 2018, the mother of The victim confirmed the fact that her daughter hanged herself due to a family crisis, not a failed exam.
The victim's mother confirmed that her daughter had been wearing a scarf in the room on July 4, 2018, more than three months ago, and not just died after the results of the bankruptcy exam were announced. Journalists and Facebook users do not continue to share this false information, which leads to the soul of his child is confused.
At the same time, the victim's sister also confirmed, "I urge all those who publish the news to stop because my sister died a long time ago. "It has nothing to do with the bankruptcy exam, and I ask the journalists to stop going down. May his soul rest in peace, and do not bring this up again."
The victim's family added that posting the picture and posting it with false content would seriously damage his family's reputation. The victim also stopped studying and got married in April 2018.
In connection with this case, the Siem Reap Provincial Police, through Fresh News, has completely denied the allegations and published baseless allegations. The Siem Reap Provincial Police confirmed that this case was caused by the victim being upset and having a family crisis, not because of a failed exam.
According to the general, when the victim's brother came to call the victim to come out to eat, but the victim did not answer with suspicion, the brother pushed the door and saw his sister. He committed suicide and the victim's younger brother ran to call his mother to come and see. When he arrived, the victim's mother also saw that her daughter was dead.
The General Commissioner emphasized that the re-presentation of the story was due to the recent posting of photos of the young woman's body, linking the story with the failed exam and technical errors of Ministry of Education only to avoid misunderstandings. Ministry of Foreign Affairs reveals the results of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Hanoi, Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, led a two-day delegation from September 12-13, 2018 in Hanoi, Vietnam at the invitation of Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung. Fox Park.
During his two-day visit to Hanoi, Samdech Techo Hun Sen attended the 27th World Economic Forum, delivering keynote speeches and answering questions from the World Economic Forum on the vision of developing countries in the Mekong region. In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also held bilateral and tripartite meetings with leaders from various countries as well as leaders of the World Economic Forum.
The following is the result of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Hanoi, Vietnam, released by the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs on September 14, 2018: China will fully control the taxi service due to security concerns. Video inside)
(China): Many Chinese regulators will launch a national security inspection campaign on taxi services, fearing that the Internet-based service could endanger consumers rather than make life easier. The concern comes after a recent case in which two female customers were raped and killed by a taxi driver.
China's Ministry of Transport and the Ministry of Public Security on Monday jointly announced a campaign aimed at cracking down on illegal activities involving taxi call services. The campaign will start immediately and will be valid until the end of this year.
Stakeholders will make more efforts to strengthen the work related to protecting the privacy of taxi drivers, take stricter measures against taxi drivers who have been sued and have to check cars and taxi drivers on the road. Not set.
As part of this campaign, local transport authorities and police must ensure that they respond in a timely manner when problems arise, as well as make further efforts to strengthen security, such as checking the history of Czech taxi drivers. See how responsible the driver is for his taxi business and also develop new mechanisms that are more effective in resolving complaints, alerts and responding quickly.
Taxi companies will be asked to use new technology to mitigate the risk. These new technologies include face recognition technology to check the identity of the driver and big data technology to detect some suspicious activity, such as driving in the wrong direction or parking for a long time. Normal.
The statement also urged authorities to respond quickly to crimes and request technical assistance from taxi service providers to help police better investigate crimes.
Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin have called on the two countries to forge closer ties through sub-national cooperation.
The Chinese president said that sub-national cooperation plays an important role in bilateral ties, and that cooperation between the two countries should be based on the resources available at the grassroots level, implemented at the grassroots level and benefit those areas.
Xi called for more people-to-people exchanges between cultures and cultures so that the general public of the two countries could get to know each other better and establish a foundation in a society that Will facilitate cooperation between the two countries. Xi also urged the two countries to promote institutional exchanges on cultural, tourism, education and media work at the sub-national level on a regular basis.
The Russian president also stressed that the Russian government welcomes Chinese businessmen to invest in Russia, and the Russian government is willing to continue to provide favorable business conditions for Chinese businessmen to strengthen sub-national cooperation between the two countries. Two.
The roundtable was also attended by Chinese sub-national leaders from nine regions and Russian sub-national leaders from 13 regions.
The Eastern Economic Forum was first held in 2015 on the initiative of Russian President Putin. And President Xi is the first Chinese president to attend the forum.
