Mr. Khuong Sreng urges the 12 district administrations to pay attention to strengthening garbage collection agencies at various locations to improve the environment
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, instructed the 12 Khan administrations to pay attention as well as strengthen the garbage collection agencies in the communes, which are contracted officials and the Phnom Penh administration has chosen to improve the environment and how. Strengthen existing mechanisms in line with Cintri as a collector and work together more effectively.
Mr. Khuong Sreng made this remark during a meeting on waste issues with the 12 district governors and relevant departments on the afternoon of September 14, 2018 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall. On that occasion, the Governor of Phnom Penh urged all district governors and officials of relevant departments to impose fines on individuals who throw garbage in public places in violation of the inter-ministerial law.
The Governor of Phnom Penh also said that if Phnom Penh wants to increase the number of tourists, it must have a better environment and security. So we all work together to make Phnom Penh a tourist destination that makes people want to come to our city.
