CamControl officers inspected fuel stations and depots in Russey Keo and Prek Pnov and found a depot that did not sell enough fuel
(Phnom Penh): On September 14, 2018, CamControl officers inspected a number of gas stations and depots in Russey Keo district and 6 fuel depots in Russey Keo and Prek Pnov districts. As a result, a depot was found not selling enough oil.
The operation was led by Mr. Nguon Somlyvong, Deputy Director of the Department, in collaboration with the Laboratory's professional officers and through a mobile fuel laboratory vehicle. The operation is aimed at protecting the economic interests of consumers, protecting the machinery of all types of vehicles and protecting the environment arising from improper fuel consumption, and in particular to prevent fraud.
As a result of quality control and quantity of fuel of 6 stations and depots in the above location, 5 stations and depots are in compliance with the quality and measurement, while 1 depot has a lack of fuel in accordance with the measurement standards.
After inspecting this, the inspection staff asked the station owner and depot to make a contract to adjust the vending machine according to the correct prediction through the competent authority.
