(Phnom Penh): Police in Po Sen Chey district have arrested five Chinese nationals for allegedly using violence and extorting $ 45,000 from employees of the Hang Sing loan company. On September 14, 2018, while the other two assailants were fleeing.
Por Sen Chey District Police Inspector Colonel Yim Saran told Fresh News that the incident caused by the Chinese violence occurred at 4:30 AM on September 12, 2018 at the loan site. Hang Sing, Prey Tea 1 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey.
On September 12, 2018, the victim and the driver drove a car from a handicraft shop in Daun Keo town, Takeo province to collect money from a Chinese road factory located in Po Sen Chey district. Saang district, Kandal province.
Upon arrival, the victim paid $ 25,000 from the Chinese road company. After receiving the payment, the victim was owed $ 45,000 by the fast loan company Hang Sing in front of the factory. The victim then agreed to pay $ 3,000 to the lender.
However, the loan company refused to bring the victim to the office in Prey Tea 1 village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, when the five suspects put the victim on the car and attacked the victim, causing swelling. Posterior neck. When he arrived at the Hangsing headquarters, he took the victim up to the second floor and asked the victim to hand over the money. When the victim refused, there was an argument and the victim ran away from the office.
Later, the victims went to file a complaint at the Saang District Police Inspectorate, Kandal Province, and then the Saang District Police Inspectorate contacted the Po Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate to open a search and arrest six suspects and interrogate them. Three were involved, while two others have not yet been arrested.
The suspect is currently being held in police custody at the Po Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate to build a case for further proceedings.
