Vice President of the Khmer Rouge Party requested the Ministry of Interior to summon Mr. Suong Sophorn for questioning, accusing him of falsifying the report
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pen Sap, Vice President of the Khmer Rouge Party, on September 14, 2018, wrote a letter to Samdech Horm Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, to summon Mr. Suong Sophorn for questioning, alleging that Suong Sophorn falsified reports that he had resigned.
Mr. Pen Sap's letter states: "I have never resigned from any position in the Khmer Rouge party formed and led by Suon Serey Ratha. "Because participating in politics is my will to help the country and the Cambodian people as Cambodian children."
He considered that the writing of Mr. Suong Sophorn's report to the Ministry of Interior about the Congress and the resignation of the Vice President of the Party is a lie of the Ministry of Interior, falsifying documents and using fake documents to become party president and form internal separatists. The party is different from the original statute of the ruling Khmer Rouge party.
