(China): In the future, the buying and selling of Chinese yuan will be possible more widely as China has a strong position to promote financial transparency. This is according to the People's Bank of China on Friday.
The announcement was made in response to the growing demand for yuan-denominated goods and services, the growing use of the yuan in international markets, as well as China's efforts to strengthen overall financial transparency.
"The market needs to make the yuan trading increasingly convenient," the People's Bank of China said in a letter posted on its website.
According to the message, more yuan could be used to buy and sell goods, trade and services than in the past.
At the same time, the yuan can also be used in foreign-approved equity accounts, unlike in the past where the yuan could only be used for foreign direct investment. According to the People's Bank of China.
"In the future, as financial transparency becomes more transparent, the volume of approved cross-border investments will continue to increase and the volume of yuan trading will increase accordingly," the statement said. .
At present, overseas parties that buy and sell yuan are only companies and institutions, not individual investors. According to the People's Bank of China.
After raising investment quotas for the Shanghai-Hong Kong and Shenzhen-Hong Kong stock exchange programs this year, Chinese authorities are preparing to launch the Shanghai-London Stock Exchange program this year.
