Siem Reap Provincial Police Office confirms the case of a young woman who hanged herself due to a family crisis, not upset about the exam failure as posted on social media
(Siem Reap): In recent days, it has been observed that a photo of a young woman committing suicide has been linked to a failed exam and technical error by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. The case has been widely shared by Facebook users, claiming that the victim committed suicide due to failing the exam.
This incident happened at 12 noon on July 4, 2018 in Chunlong village, Sala Kamroeuk commune, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province.
To confirm this case, on September 13, 2018, the Siem Reap Provincial Police, through Fresh News, completely denied the allegations and published baseless allegations. The Siem Reap Provincial Police confirmed that this case was caused by the victim being upset and having a family crisis, not because of a failed exam.
The General Commissioner emphasized that the re-presentation of the story was due to the recent posting of photos of the young woman's body, linking the story with the failed exam and technical errors of Ministry of Education only to avoid misunderstanding.
Therefore, I would like to confirm that this case is not a suicide due to the failed exam results in 2018, it is a different story.
(Phnom Penh): In the discussion of the minimum wage for workers in the textile, garment and footwear sector (2nd time) for 2019, which was held on the morning of September 14, 2018, the union side put the figure of 192 dollars Employers have set a figure of $ 175 and the government has put $ 177, according to Heng Sour, deputy director of the Secretariat of the Labor Advisory Committee.
Mr. Heng Sour said that in the second tripartite technical working group meeting at the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training today, each party presented their respective official figures for the 2019 minimum wage as follows: To: union side $ 192, employer side $ 175 and government side $ 177.
Heng Sour said that the tripartite technical working group will continue to discuss to bring the figures closer together until a confluence point is found. He said that the Royal Government has provided a rate of more than 4% to be used as a basis for further discussions to bring the figures closer in setting the minimum wage in 2019.
He added that each party also raised various proposals related to the investment climate and the environment of the export of textiles, clothing and footwear, in which the workers also requested support for the well-being of workers. In addition, the provision of food and transportation costs in addition to the increase in wages in the near future.
Mr. Pasina, President of the Coalition of Workers' Movement Unions, said that the current problem of workers in Cambodia is not only the issue of wages, but also other issues such as the cost of rent, water, electricity, food, transportation services and so on. .
The union leader complained that the provision of health services was still a problem for workers, with the union noting that workers still did not trust health services at partner hospitals. Of the state or a partner of the Socialist Party, etc., because some doctors do not care about workers who go to receive health services for free.
Please be informed that the minimum wage of workers in the textile, garment and footwear sector in Cambodia is increasing every year, and in 2018, the minimum wage of workers in this sector increased to 170 US dollars per month.
