Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: This year, the Cambodian economy will continue to grow at a strong rate of 7.2%, senior ADB officials congratulate Cambodia on its great success in boosting economic growth
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Cambodian Governor of the Asian Development Bank (ADB), spoke about the economic situation in Cambodia, which is achieving strong macroeconomic stability. Over the last two decades.
"Cambodia has achieved macroeconomic stability and a high average economic growth rate of 7.7% per year, and the Cambodian economy is expected to continue to grow strongly at around 7.2% per year," he said. This year 2018.
The hearing was attended by the Chief of Staff and Mr. Mabob Amed in order to discuss the work with the Royal Government of Cambodia and other relevant institutions, as well as to monitor the progress and achievements of the implementation of projects under the ADB financing framework. .
According to the doctor, the strong growth of the Cambodian economy has increased the gross domestic product per capita more than seven times from more than 200 US dollars in 1992 to nearly 1,500 US dollars in 2018. The poverty rate dropped from about 50% in 1992 to around 13.5% in 2014, despite some external challenges and risks.
He added that the Cambodian economy achieved high growth based on a number of important factors, such as:
1. Ensuring peace, political stability and the creation of a conducive environment for development. Public. 3: Sustainable development that focuses on human resource development and social protection. 4. Economic diversification through the strengthening of physical infrastructure in both urban and rural areas.
In addition, Mr. Mabob Ahmed highly appreciated the efforts of the Royal Government and congratulated Cambodia on its great success in maintaining and promoting sustainable economic growth, maintaining better social equity and reducing poverty. The Cambodian government has a clear policy to develop the nation. New Results of the 2018 Baccalaureate Exam in Science for Preah Vihear Province
