Environment Minister: Cambodia is committed to joining the international community in eliminating the use of ozone depleting substances
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, said that Cambodia is committed to joining the international community in eliminating the use of ozone depleting substances. This is according to the Minister's congratulatory letter on World Ozone Day, September 16, 2018, on September 14, 2018.
Mr. Say Sam Al said that on behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, I would like to congratulate the government and people of the world on celebrating World Ozone Day under the theme: "Keep the planet cool and Continue to protect our ozone layer and our atmosphere on World Ozone Day "to inspire people from all walks of life to continue to contribute to keeping the planet cool.
He also praised the success of the Montreal Protocol on the protection of the ozone layer by contributing to the prevention of global warming and the almost complete elimination of ozone-depleting substances that have the potential to cause global warming.
Mankind's efforts to curb ozone depletion have actively contributed to reducing global warming of 135 billion tons of carbon dioxide between 1990 and 2010.
