Cambodian MPs ask the President of the International Socialist Organization to urge the S&D party to withdraw the proposal that opposes democracy, peace and development in Cambodia
The agreement was reached during a bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Lao Prime Minister Thongloun Sisoulith after the World Economic Forum on ASEAN in Hanoi, Vietnam on the afternoon of September 13, 2018.
The three points agreed upon by both sides are: First, there should be no more troops of the two countries in the confrontation area, second, there should be no people in that area, and third, there must be joint patrols that can be done. On foot and through Tron hosting under joint supervision.
Ahead of the talks between the two prime ministers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that he had ordered all Cambodian troops to withdraw from the border in the conflict zone, and that the withdrawal would end at 5:00 pm tomorrow.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "What is new in our relationship is to build trust through the establishment of joint patrols. In the past, the Lao army followed the Lao army, the Cambodian army followed the Cambodian army. Now, if we want to go, we go together. "The remaining issue to be resolved is that both sides must submit technical procedures to the French side, and the French side has already agreed to the request of the two prime ministers."
The Prime Minister of Laos, Thongloun Sisoulith, supported the statement made by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. He said the area was an unresolved area. He said that the agreement of the two Prime Ministers is an important agreement, the content of which builds mutual trust, which makes our two people happier.
Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit also met on September 1, 2017 at the Peace Palace. During the meeting, the Prime Ministers of the two countries discussed a lot on the border issue between the two countries and also agreed to write a letter to the French government asking for experts to help change the scale of the two countries' maps from 1: 100,000 to 1 50,000.
Please be reminded that both the meeting of the Prime Minister as well as the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia-Laos took place after Laos deployed troops on Cambodian territory in Otangao and O'Alay areas, Siem Pang district, Stung Treng province, and was asked by Cambodia to withdraw. All back on August 11, 2017, at the request of the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
