Many defective goods were confiscated by CamControl officers and burned after finding them for sale at Svay Pat Market, Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): Food safety is a special case that every citizen should be aware and must know how to check carefully before buying to eat at home or to eat on a trip or other gatherings ⁇. But for a while, it was observed that some goods that were damaged or out of date were used by company agents or buyers to resell in the markets in remote rural areas.
In order to prevent and prevent the defective goods from being sold in the rural market, the CamControl branch in Preah Vihear province cooperated with the provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities to inspect the goods in the markets in Preah Vihear province and confiscated Many expired goods are also burned.
In fact, on September 13, 2018, CamControl officials in Preah Vihear province, in cooperation with the provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities, inspected goods in Svay Pat market in Svay Pat commune, Rodos commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province. As a result, damaged goods were found and confiscated: 21.94 liters of orange juice, 4.5 liters of syrup, 7.2 kg of fruit juice, 3.78 liters of canned coffee, 2.4 kg of Mama and The cake weighs 0.77 grams as well.
Mr. Duong Mony, President of CamControl Preah Vihear Branch, said that expired and damaged goods were also collected and burned.
At the same time, Mr. Camcontrol also advised traders to inspect all goods purchased and resold, to check the date of production, check clearly to avoid selling to harm the health of people. The NEC decided to delete the names of 50 MPs who hold positions in the Royal Government and recognize 38 new MPs
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) today decided to delete the names of 50 CPP lawmakers who took office in the Royal Government after they resigned. Parliament.
According to the press release, on September 10, 2018, the NEC received a letter of request from the Cambodian People's Party on the declaration of recognition of candidates elected to the National Assembly for the sixth term.
The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) announced that "recently, some party deputies and candidates in some provincial capitals have resigned."
On September 12, 2018, the NEC agreed to delete the names and recognize the candidates for the 6th legislature in accordance with Article 139 of the Law on the National Assembly Election.
According to the press release, this article states that "Members of the National Assembly must lose their membership in many cases, for example, the applicant resigns in writing from the member of the National Assembly." The party may nominate a new member to be selected from among the candidates listed in the order in which the constituency list of their constituency is elected without having to re-vote.
