(China): Three rehabilitation projects opened on Sunday, highlighting China-Nepal ties in Tibet. The three projects include the Restoration of the Nepal Consulate General in Lhasa and the restoration of two border bridges damaged by a 8.1-magnitude earthquake in April. 2015 ago.
The Consulate General will be rebuilt on the old site on an area of about 8,500 square meters. The consulate will be used both as a place of work, as a reception area and as a place for diplomatic activities. The construction will be completed next year. Nepal's parliamentary spokesman Krishna Bahadur Mahara said the reconstruction projects would boost bilateral ties between China and Nepal.
This is according to the e-commerce development report of the BRICS Plus 2018 group released by the China E-Commerce Association. E-commerce has become a new driving force behind the growth of the BRICS countries, including Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa, the report said.
In 2017, the BRICS group sold 1.5 percent more cross-border online goods than in 2016, generating nearly $ 130 billion in total sales, according to the report.
"The booming e-commerce has made the flow of trade between the five countries smoother and easier," said Xiao Lihua, vice president of Alibaba and assistant chief executive.
"There are still many opportunities for this cooperation to expand and expand as we still have a lot of work to do," said Xiao Lihua, vice president of Alibaba. This task is not just to eliminate systemic barriers and create a new system.
"We still need to deal with a lot of issues related to mobile payments, shipping and tax returns," he said. Of course, we have experienced these problems many times before. "But now the flow of trade is easier."
According to the report, e-commerce not only facilitates trade but also promotes industry development and job creation, and enables small and medium-sized enterprises to participate. More in the global production cost chain, or so-called cost-cutting action system globally.
Sophie Zhang is the Vice President of an e-commerce company in Russia called Umka China. E-commerce has enabled many small Chinese companies to expand their business overseas, she said.
