Ministry of Commerce and Administration of Pailin Province Holds Training Course on Cassava and Red Corn Market Search to Improve Agricultural Market
(Pailin): On September 13, 2018, Pailin Provincial Department of Commerce, in collaboration with the Trade Training and Research Institute and the Export-Import Department of the Ministry of Commerce, opened a training course on market exploration of cassava and corn. Presided over by Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, as well as the participation of silo owners, traders, entrepreneurs, small and medium business owners.
Mr. Suon Vichea, President of the Trade Training and Research Institute of the Ministry of Commerce, said: “Currently, the cassava and red corn market has great potential for Cambodia, especially in the Northwest Zone in Pailin, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces. Therefore, the agricultural sector is a leading sector for the people of Cambodia and has increased profits to support the livelihood of local farmers.
Mr. Phan Chanthul commended the Ministry of Commerce and the Pailin Provincial Department of Commerce for organizing this training to make it easier to understand and share experiences with each other, especially for silo owners, traders, enterprise owners. Small and medium enterprises around the province are developing agriculture to be more prosperous.
He added that finding a market for cassava and corn is an indispensable demand and potential because the agricultural market for cassava and corn is leading and growing demand for overseas markets, and it is also a dominant agricultural sector. Of Pailin province as well.
The provincial governor said that on behalf of the provincial authorities, they want to make the market for agricultural products of farmers better and the market price higher, and all relevant officials need to pay more attention to find the market for agricultural products. Investment partners in agriculture, as well as promote a more diversified agricultural market, which is an opportunity that can help farmers to easily trade with a stable and clear market prices.
Mr. Sok Sathim, Director of the Provincial Department of Commerce, said that in Pailin Province, cassava and red corn are sold to three main markets: Thailand, Vietnam and China and supplied to CP Pailin Branch for Feed production in 2017 was 84,600 tons of red corn and 30,339 tons of dried cassava. Battambang Provincial Governor Distributes Cambodian Red Cross Donation to 200 Families in Battambang City
(Battambang): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province and Honorary President of the Provincial Red Cross Branch, on the afternoon of September 13, 2018, visited and brought mosquito nets as a gift of the Red Cross to distribute to 200 families from 4 communes. In Battambang city, in the area of Toul Ta Ek pagoda, located in Toul Ta Ek village, Sangkat Toul Ta Ek and Ochar village in Sangkat Ochar in Battambang city, Battambang province.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. But Kim Sean, Deputy Governor of Battambang and Chairman of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as members of the Provincial Council, Battambang City Council, members of the Provincial Red Cross and other relevant local authorities.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Nguon Rattanak said that in order to prevent epidemics and protect the well-being of the people, the provincial branch of the Cambodian Red Cross brought the donations of the Chinese Red Cross through the Cambodian Red Cross to distribute, including: The family receives 1 mosquito net, 1 T-shirt, 1 liter and a half of VK pure water, 1 portable bag and 10,000 Riels.
Mr. But Kim Sean also brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always thinks about the well-being of the people who are suffering, poor and vulnerable. Victims of various disasters, regardless of caste, race, color or political affiliation.
He continued that all citizens should take care to take good care of their health, clean the environment around the house, be clean in living, drink boiled water, adhere to clean food, drink clean and live clean and strive to cultivate. Combined cropping to support family livelihoods. In addition, the President had a conversation with the people to drink clean water, boiled water as well.
Mr. But Kim Sean also confirmed on that occasion that the Battambang Red Cross branch will continue to serve the people everywhere in a timely manner for all our people.
