Minister of Agriculture sets out 7 principles for ministry leaders to implement agricultural development policies successfully
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on September 13, 2018, chaired a standing meeting to announce the composition of the leadership and assign roles and responsibilities to the leadership of the Ministry. The Ministry.
On that occasion, the Minister instructed and instructed the Ministry's leadership to pay more attention and take responsibility for the implementation of the agricultural development policy (2019-2023) to achieve the 7 points of the Royal Government's will. Key features include:
First, continue to support the promotion and promotion of agricultural development to ensure food security and nutrition to reduce poverty and promote productivity, diversification and commercialization of agriculture in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase IV.
Second, promote stable and resilient climate change agriculture practices. Promote good agricultural practices in both animal production and animal health and fisheries to ensure change and improve the management of natural risks and climate change at all levels.
Third, all measures must be taken to reduce the deterioration of soil quality, unsustainable land use and declining ecosystems. The specialized unit must continue to work hard to determine the appropriate planting area according to the type of crop and the long-term use direction.
Fourth, to encourage and encourage the private sector to participate in the dissemination of new technologies such as the use of agricultural machinery and agricultural equipment, new seed production, processing, packaging, gaining support for the domestic market and exports.
Fifth, increase multilateral cooperation in the implementation of contract production to increase the warmth and confidence of farmers and traders.
Sixth, all subordinate units must continue to promote the effective implementation of existing laws and regulations and continue to prepare and compile legal documents in accordance with national development trends.
Seventh, promote diversified agriculture, including animal husbandry, crop production, fish farming in community forests and fishing communities to reduce the district's dependence on natural resources leading to poverty reduction.
