Expert doctor: Diabetes will increase to more than 550 million by 2030
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Trung Thilev, a diabetes specialist from Choray Ho Chi Minh Hospital, confirmed that the number of people with diabetes worldwide is currently found by experts. There are 442 million cases, and experts estimate that there will be 552 million cases by 2030.
This morning, September 13, 2018, in the program of free screening and treatment for people with type 2 diabetes and nutrition at 50 people at Cho Ray Hospital, Phnom Penh, in collaboration with With DHG Pharma.
"In terms of the number of people with diabetes worldwide, the number of people diagnosed with diabetes in 2014 was 442 million now, for the year 2030," said Dr. Trung Thilev. It is estimated that there are up to 552 million people.
Diabetes mellitus occurs regardless of age or gender, but is caused by a lack of proper blood sugar control, which can lead to an increase in blood sugar levels, he said. Blood sugar is the cause of this deadly disease.
After the previous free monthly screening and treatment program for this course, Choray Phnom Penh Hospital in collaboration with DHG Pharma organized a screening and treatment program for type II diabetes and free nutrition for the first 50 new patients. One day by a highly experienced Vietnamese specialist from Cho Ray Hospital, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam.
This free screening and treatment program for people with type 2 diabetes is a meaningful humanitarian program of Choray Hospital Phnom Penh and DHG Pharma to contribute to the well-being of Cambodians. Opportunity to receive quality health care from highly experienced Vietnamese specialists along with modern medical equipment at Choray Hospital, Phnom Penh.
At the same time, the doctor added that the effects of diabetes are divided into two parts: first: research side effects are patients with hypoglycemia or hyperglycemia, swelling of the legs, pneumonia and second: long-term effects. Prolonged or chronic can affect blood vessels, block blood vessels in the brain, large nerves, eyes, kidneys, nerves.
(Phnom Penh): Following the strict recommendation of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, General Dr. Sok Phal, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, urged all relevant police forces to crack down on illegal Chinese. There are no exceptions.
According to General Sok Phal, the police must crack down on those who commit illegal acts, and those who act in accordance with Cambodian law must be protected, while the number of Chinese in Cambodia has now risen to more than 210,000. There is an increase compared to 2017.
General Sok Phal said that in 2017, there were only more than 100,000 Chinese in Cambodia, not including diplomats, tourists and civil society organizations, but by the end of the second half, More than 210,000, according to Chinese statistics, came to extend visas.
Please be informed that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, on September 12, 2018, issued an order to four main units of the Ministry of Interior to establish an operation team to visit Sihanoukville immediately. Investigate and help crack down on crime after the emergence of some irregular activities.
The four units include: the General Department of Administration, the General Commission of the National Police, the General Department of Immigration, and the legal team of the Ministry of Interior.
However, a series of crimes, especially those involving Chinese nationals, have also been cracked down on by the police and the relevant authorities, and many perpetrators have been arrested. The Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Vietnam agreed to maintain peace, political stability and development in the border areas.
(Hanoi, Vietnam): In a bilateral meeting between Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his Vietnamese counterpart Nguyen Suon Phuc, the two sides discussed a trade agreement to be signed in the near future.
The meeting between Cambodian and Vietnamese leaders took place on the morning of September 13, 2018, on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen attending the 27th World Economic Forum on ASEAN in Hanoi, Vietnam.
The leaders of the two countries also explored all means to boost trade growth to achieve the goals that both leaders want. At the same time, the Cambodian and Vietnamese leaders also discussed bilateral, multilateral, regional and international issues of common concern. Samdech Techo also congratulated Vietnam on September 2 Victory Day.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam informed Samdech Techo PM about the upcoming visit of the King of Cambodia and Samdech Mey to pay a state visit to Vietnam in 2019. Samdech Techo accepted an invitation to visit Vietnam in the near future to sign the Cambodia-Vietnam Trade Agreement.
At the same time, Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc considered that the presence of Samdech Techo was very important in the World Economic Forum, especially his speech at the opening ceremony of the World Economic Forum and the intervention in the Plenary Summit on the new vision for the region. The Mekong is very meaningful and very meaningful, especially for ASEAN and the countries in the Mekong region.
He said he was happy to continue working with all ASEAN leaders to continue their mission to build a stronger and more prosperous ASEAN community.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Sri Lanka agree to promote bilateral, multilateral, regional and international relations with common concern
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that he had visited Sri Lanka in 1979 as the Minister of Foreign Affairs, and at that time the situation of the two countries was the same, that is, we could not cooperate with each other. Yes.
Through this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the Sri Lankan side through the Foreign Ministries of the two countries to work together to promote relations in tourism and other areas with the same potential.
Samdech also responded to the invitation of the Prime Minister of Sri Lanka to visit Sri Lanka in the near future. During the meeting, the two leaders also exchanged views on promoting bilateral, multilateral, regional and international relations of common concern.
On the same day, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen also met with His Excellency Professor Claus Swab, Founder and Executive Director of the World Economic Forum.
During the meeting, he welcomed the Prime Minister to attend the World Economic Forum in Hanoi, Vietnam.
The Prime Minister expressed his pleasure to be invited to participate in the Economic Forum in Vietnam again, which has exchanged fruitful views. At the same time, Samdech asked the director to distribute this important document on the topic for the whole world.
He hopes to invite Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, in relation to the agricultural sector, which Cambodia has potential for dialogue. The Prime Minister also mentioned the context of the Fourth Industrial Revolution, which Cambodia as well as other countries in the region are equally interested in.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Announces the Change of Police Inspector of O'Yadao District, Ratanakkiri Province, but Has Not Been Officially Announced
(Ratanakkiri): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on January 11, 2018, announced the transfer of a new police inspector of O'Yadao district, Ratanakkiri province, with Mr. Soy Samnang appointed as the new inspector to replace Mr. Mao San. Who was promoted to deputy police commissioner in charge of security planning.
But until now, the above leadership has not yet officially announced the change, without knowing the reason yet.
However, as of now, it has been almost a year and the transfer of duties and appointments of the above police officers has not been officially made yet, for some reason.
Regarding the transfer of duties and appointments, Lieutenant Colonel Soy Samnang told Fresh News this morning, September 13, 2018, that he was ready and waiting for orders from higher authorities. Meanwhile, Major General Nguon Koeun, Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Commissioner, could not be reached for comment this morning. Ministry of Interior holds a meeting to review and summarize the work results of provinces bordering Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior this morning, September 13, 2018, held a meeting to review and summarize the past work of the provinces bordering Vietnam to report to Prince Sar Kheng. Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, Director General of the General Department of Administration, Ministry of Interior, with the participation of the Provincial Governor of Cambodia, which borders Vietnam, and other stakeholders.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Prak Sam Oeun emphasized that the meeting was held to understand the current situation and developments along the border of Cambodia, which borders Vietnam and easy to report to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister. Interior and ask for further guidance on the issues that have arisen and what may happen.
According to the Director General of Administration, so far Cambodia-Vietnam has erected 84% of the border posts, with the remaining 14% to be implemented. However, the demarcation of the border is still a complex geographical issue. Preah Vihear Governor: Peaceful country, we can develop anywhere
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, said that when the country is peaceful, we can develop anywhere. The provincial governor said this on the morning of September 13, 2018, on the occasion that he, along with the chairman of the provincial council, and many government officials attended the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of Wat Kork Beng temple in Kampong commune. Pranak, Preah Vihear city, Preah Vihear province.
Mr. Un Chanda said that because the country is so peaceful, we have been able to get together for festivals and other gatherings, but if the country is not peaceful, we will not get together like now. Yes.
At the same time, he thanked the people, grandparents, who went to vote for the Cambodian People's Party until it was a great success, making Samdech Techo Hun Sen the Prime Minister in the sixth mandate to Samdech led the Cambodian ship towards peace and further development.
Mr. Un Chanda said that the policy in the government of the sixth mandate has been set out, with four priority areas: 1: Human resources, 2: Roads, 3: Irrigation 4: The electricity sector, which these four sectors are all important for the development and alleviation of people's lives to improve.
At the same time, Mr. Un Chanda also thanked the Venerable Mey Kun Province for initiating the construction of this huge church, which can be said that a church that no province can do that, and he also said Thanks to the Buddhists near and far who have donated money to build this temple to be deposited in Buddhism, the state religion.
On that occasion, Mr. Un Chandak also participated in the construction of 5 million Riels, Major General Chan Sopheaktra, Commander of Preah Vihear Military Operation Area, also contributed 1,200,000 Riels.
Cambodia, Indonesia agree to further strengthen bilateral cooperation in trade, culture, investment and tourism
The two sides also acknowledged the potential for more investment and trade in the two countries, which will further strengthen cooperation by promoting closer cooperation between the two governments and peoples.
Mr. Sudirman Haseng, together with Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, agreed to continue to strengthen Cambodia-Indonesia bilateral cooperation in areas such as trade, culture, investment, tourism, especially economic and financial cooperation. Develop economic and people-to-people relations between the two countries through the establishment of joint mechanisms to strengthen partnerships in related fields.
In fact, in order to promote closer and deeper cooperation between the two countries, the two sides plan to hold the 60th anniversary of Cambodia-Indonesia diplomatic relations in 2019 through the organization of trade fairs, seminars. School and bilateral meetings, as well as study the possibility of arranging direct flights.
