For more details, please read the announcement of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia below: The body of a man was found dumped near the administrative post, Sangkat Chrakmtes, Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): The body of an unidentified man was found by residents and dumped near the Chrakmtes Sangkat Administration Post along National Road 1 near the Chrakmtes Sangkat Administrative Police Station, 50 meters away. Surprise to road users and authorities all morning.
The body was found dumped at 6:00 AM on September 13, 2018 in Sala Tean Village, Sangkat Chrakmtes, Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province.
According to the authorities, according to the first step, the body of the victim was kind, wearing a black shirt and shorts, and the body was killed by the perpetrators elsewhere and the body was packed in a black plastic bag and transported by car. From the east, drop it on the sidewalk of National Road No. 1 near the administrative checkpoint in Sangkat Chrakmtes, 50 meters away.
According to residents near the scene, at around 4 a.m., a car was seen coming from the east, and stopped for a while. Turn the car back to the east, but did not notice anything until 6:00 in the morning, the baker found the body and complained to the authorities.
After the forensic examination, the police did not know the identity and concluded that it was a murder case with the condition of the body with a cracked mouth and a scar on the back of the head, and the police confirmed that it was indeed a murder case.
Currently, the body was taken to the pagoda near the scene and the authorities are searching for the detainee to be punished according to law. UNFPA vows to assist the health sector in training and educating Cambodian midwives to help reduce maternal and infant mortality rates in Cambodia
